independent_pp\": 11.4,\n36\t      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_object_sr_pct\": 99.2,\n37\t      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_goal_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n38\t      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial_sr_pct\": 88.8,\n39\t      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_long_sr_pct\": 90.2,\n40\t      \"e5_xvla_attn_mean_k05_long_sr_pct\": 94.0\n41\t    },\n42\t    \"tables\": [\n43\t      {\n44\t        \"title\": \"Table A: Cross-Suite Δ(Random-L2norm) at k=0.5 — CV Scaling Law Breakdown\",\n45\t        \"columns\": [\n46\t          \"Model\",\n47\t          \"CV\",\n48\t          \"Object Δ(pp)\",\n49\t          \"Spatial Δ(pp)\",\n50\t          \"Goal Δ(pp)\",\n51\t          \"Long Δ(pp)\",\n52\t          \"Range(pp)\"\n53\t        ],\n54\t        \"rows\": [\n55\t          [\n56\t            \"π0.5\",\n57\t            \"0.055\",\n58\t            \"+36.0\",\n59\t            \"+16.0\",\n60\t            \"+13.8\",\n61\t            \"-4.6\",\n62\t            \"40.6\"\n63\t          ],\n64\t          [\n65\t            \"X-VLA\",\n66\t            \"0.151\",\n67\t            \"+28.0\",\n68\t            \"+12.6\",\n69\t            \"+8.5\",\n70\t            \"+17.0\",\n71\t            \"19.5\"\n72\t          ],\n73\t          [\n74\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n75\t            \"0.215\",\n76\t            \"-1.8\",\n77\t            \"~+5\",\n78\t            \"+8.8\",\n79\t            \"~+3\",\n80\t            \"~10.6\"\n81\t          ]\n82\t        ],\n83\t        \"notes\": \"Object suite 上 monotonic（ρ=-1.0），Long suite 上 π0.5 reversal 破坏 monotonicity。Cross-suite mean |ρ|≈0.45。\"\n84\t      },\n85\t      {\n86\t        \"title\": \"Table B: π0.5 Random k=0.9 Cross-Suite — Token-Independent ≠ Task-Independent\",\n87\t        \"columns\": [\n88\t          \"Suite\",\n89\t          \"Baseline(%)\",\n90\t          \"Random k=0.9(%)\",\n91\t          \"Δ from baseline(pp)\",\n92\t          \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\",\n93\t          \"Method gap(pp)\"\n94\t        ],\n95\t        \"rows\": [\n96\t          [\n97\t            \"Object\",\n98\t            \"98.2\",\n99\t            \"9.3\",\n100\t            \"-88.9\",\n101\t            \"98.2\",\n102\t            \"-88.9\"\n103\t          ],\n104\t          [\n105\t            \"Spatial\",\n106\t            \"97.2\",\n107\t            \"54.0\",\n108\t            \"-43.2\",\n109\t            \"95.3\",\n110\t            \"-41.3\"\n111\t          ],\n112\t          [\n113\t            \"Goal\",\n114\t            \"96.4\",\n115\t            \"62.2\",\n116\t            \"-34.2\",\n117\t            \"89.6\",\n118\t            \"-27.4\"\n119\t          ],\n120\t          [\n121\t            \"Long\",\n122\t            \"92.8\",\n123\t            \"31.4\",\n124\t            \"-61.4\",\n125\t            \"80.0\",\n126\t            \"-12.8\"\n127\t          ]\n128\t        ],\n129\t        \"notes\": \"Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm。Task sensitivity 是 method-specific，非 architecture-level property。\"\n130\t      },\n131\t      {\n132\t        \"title\": \"Table C: E5 Attention Pruning Demolishes Entanglement Narrative (X-VLA k=0.5)\",\n133\t        \"columns\": [\n134\t          \"Suite\",\n135\t          \"L2norm(%)\",\n136\t          \"Random(%)\",\n137\t          \"Attn-Last(%)\",\n138\t          \"Attn-Mean(%)\",\n139\t          \"Best Attn vs L2norm(pp)\"\n140\t        ],\n141\t        \"rows\": [\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"Object\",\n144\t            \"42.6\",\n145\t            \"70.6\",\n146\t            \"99.2\",\n147\t            \"98.4\",\n148\t            \"+56.6\"\n149\t          ],\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"Spatial\",\n152\t            \"58.8\",\n153\t            \"71.4\",\n154\t            \"88.8\",\n155\t            \"91.6\",\n156\t            \"+32.8\"\n157\t          ],\n158\t          [\n159\t            \"Goal\",\n160\t            \"59.0\",\n161\t            \"67.2\",\n162\t            \"98.2\",\n163\t            \"97.4\",\n164\t            \"+38.4\"\n165\t          ],\n166\t          [\n167\t            \"Long\",\n168\t            \"44.6\",\n169\t            \"61.6\",\n170\t            \"90.2\",\n171\t            \"94.0\",\n172\t            \"+49.4\"\n173\t          ]\n174\t        ],\n175\t        \"notes\": \"Attention pruning 在所有 4 suites 上实现 88-99% SR at k=0.5。问题不在 connector entanglement，在 importance metric。\"\n176\t      }\n177\t    ],\n178\t    \"figures\": [],\n179\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-suite 数据系统性地破坏 2-axis framework 的两个核心预测： (1) Axis-1 独立性：token-independent connectors should be immune to task complexity → π0.5 random k=0.9 Object=9% vs Goal=62% 证伪（53pp gap）。 (2) CV universal predictor：CV 应在所有 suite 上预测 method preference → Long-horizon 上 π0.5 出现 reversal（L2norm > random），OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也 reversal。 E5 attention pruning 数据进一步瓦解 Axis-1 定义：X-VLA（\\\"entangling\\\"）在 attention pruning 下表现如同 \\\"independent\\\" connector。Axis-1 的区分不在 \\\"token coupling\\\" 而在 \\\"susceptibility to norm-based importance bias\\\"。 Reframe：论文不能声称发现了 governing principle，而应定位为 \\\"comprehensive empirical study revealing that importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture\\\"。\\n\\n\\nπ0.5 random k=0.9 在 Object 上出现 catastrophic cliff（9.3%），但在 Goal 上仅下降至 62.2%——同一 linear projection connector、同一 random method、同一 k，仅 task distribution 不同就产生 53pp 差异。这直接破坏 \\\"token-independent connector 不受 task complexity 影响\\\" 的核心假设。 机制：Object suite 需要 precise object identity discrimination（visually similar condiments），random 在 cliff zone 摧毁 concentrated discriminative features；Goal suite 的 task 由 language instruction 区分，vision tokens 冗余度更高，random 破坏的影响小。 L2norm 在相同 k=0.9 的 cross-suite range 仅 18.2pp（vs random 53pp），证明 cross-suite sensitivity 是 METHOD-dependent 而非 connector-dependent。 E5 attention pruning 数据更具破坏性：X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2%（Object）、98.2%（Goal），vs L2norm=42.6%/59%。这意味着 X-VLA 的 \\\"entanglement\\\" 问题完全可以通过更换 importance metric 解决，BART encoder 产生的不是 \\\"irreversible entanglement\\\" 而是 \\\"norm-unfriendly importance distribution\\\"。 CV scaling law 在 Object 内仍然成立（Spearman -1.0），但 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm > random，Δ=-4.6pp），导致 cross-suite 平均 |ρ|≈0.45，远低于 paper 声称的 \\\"universal predictor\\\" 所需的 >0.8。 OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也出现 method preference reversal（random > L2norm +8.8pp），而 Object 上 L2norm > random（+1.8pp）。同一 CV=0.215 的 model，跨 suite 后 method preference 反转。 Framework 在 20 个 model×suite 预测中仅正确约 12 个（62%），达不到 \\\"principled framework\\\" 标准。\\n\"\n180\t  },\n181\t  {\n182\t    \"name\": \"π0.5 Token-Independent Confirmation (4B, Linear Proj)\",\n183\t    \"description\": \"π0.5 作为 2nd token-independent data point，验证 CV=0.055 的 linear projection 在所有 suite 上的 pruning 行为。 worst 档：π0.5 数据揭示 \\\"immune class\\\" 不存在——random pruning 在 cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) 产生 catastrophic collapse，且行为极度 task-dependent。\\n\",\n184\t    \"results\": {\n185\t      \"pi05_cv\": 0.055,\n186\t      \"pi05_baseline_object_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n187\t      \"pi05_baseline_spatial_sr_pct\": 97.2,\n188\t      \"pi05_baseline_goal_sr_pct\": 96.4,\n189\t      \"pi05_baseline_long_sr_pct\": 92.8,\n190\t      \"pi05_random_k095_object_sr_pct\": 71.1,\n191\t      \"pi05_random_k0925_object_sr_pct\": 27.6,\n192\t      \"pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct\": 10.8,\n193\t      \"pi05_random_k085_object_sr_pct\": 5.0,\n194\t      \"pi05_random_k07_object_sr_pct\": 75.5,\n195\t      \"pi05_random_k05_object_sr_pct\": 69.4,\n196\t      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n197\t      \"pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr_pct\": 98.0,\n198\t      \"pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr_pct\": 33.4,\n199\t      \"pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr_pct\": 51.0,\n200\t      \"pi05_random_cliff_depth_pp\": 66.1,\n201\t      \"pi05_l2norm_v_shape_depth_pp\": 17.6,\n202\t      \"pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_cross_suite_avg_pp\": 15.3,\n203\t      \"pi05_attention_k07_object_sr_pct\": 0.6,\n204\t      \"pi05_attention_k05_object_sr_pct\": 37.8,\n205\t      \"pi05_attention_k095_object_sr_pct\": 98.4\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"tables\": [\n208\t      {\n209\t        \"title\": \"Table D: π0.5 Random Cliff Zone (Object Suite)\",\n210\t        \"columns\": [\n211\t          \"k\",\n212\t          \"Tokens kept\",\n213\t          \"Random SR(%)\",\n214\t          \"L2norm SR(%)\",\n215\t          \"Δ(L2-R)(pp)\"\n216\t        ],\n217\t        \"rows\": [\n218\t          [\n219\t            \"0.95\",\n220\t            \"730\",\n221\t            \"71.1\",\n222\t            \"98.2\",\n223\t            \"+27.1\"\n224\t          ],\n225\t          [\n226\t            \"0.925\",\n227\t            \"710\",\n228\t            \"27.6\",\n229\t            \"99.2\",\n230\t            \"+71.6\"\n231\t          ],\n232\t          [\n233\t            \"0.90\",\n234\t            \"691\",\n235\t            \"10.8\",\n236\t            \"98.2\",\n237\t            \"+87.4\"\n238\t          ],\n239\t          [\n240\t            \"0.85\",\n241\t            \"653\",\n242\t            \"5.0\",\n243\t            \"98.0\",\n244\t            \"+93.0\"\n245\t          ],\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"0.70\",\n248\t            \"538\",\n249\t            \"75.5\",\n250\t            \"55.0\",\n251\t            \"-20.5\"\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"0.50\",\n255\t            \"384\",\n256\t            \"69.4\",\n257\t            \"33.4\",\n258\t            \"-36.0\"\n259\t          ],\n260\t          [\n261\t            \"0.30\",\n262\t            \"230\",\n263\t            \"36.4\",\n264\t            \"51.0\",\n265\t            \"+14.6\"\n266\t          ]\n267\t        ],\n268\t        \"notes\": \"方法偏好在 k=0.7 附近反转。Cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) L2norm 完胜；aggressive zone (k=0.5-0.7) random 完胜。\"\n269\t      },\n270\t      {\n271\t        \"title\": \"Table E: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random k=0.9 — 'Immune' Class Falsified\",\n272\t        \"columns\": [\n273\t          \"Suite\",\n274\t          \"Baseline(%)\",\n275\t          \"Random k=0.9(%)\",\n276\t          \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\",\n277\t          \"Δ from baseline (random, pp)\"\n278\t        ],\n279\t        \"rows\": [\n280\t          [\n281\t            \"Object\",\n282\t            \"98.2\",\n283\t            \"9.3\",\n284\t            \"98.2\",\n285\t            \"-88.9\"\n286\t          ],\n287\t          [\n288\t            \"Spatial\",\n289\t            \"97.2\",\n290\t            \"54.0\",\n291\t            \"95.3\",\n292\t            \"-43.2\"\n293\t          ],\n294\t          [\n295\t            \"Goal\",\n296\t            \"96.4\",\n297\t            \"62.2\",\n298\t            \"89.6\",\n299\t            \"-34.2\"\n300\t          ],\n301\t          [\n302\t            \"Long\",\n303\t            \"92.8\",\n304\t            \"31.4\",\n305\t            \"80.0\",\n306\t            \"-61.4\"\n307\t          ]\n308\t        ],\n309\t        \"notes\": \"同一 model/method/k，cross-suite range=53pp。Framework 预测 token-independent 应 <5pp variation。\"\n310\t      }\n311\t    ],\n312\t    \"figures\": [],\n313\t    \"analysis\": \"π0.5 数据是 worst 档的 smoking gun：CV=0.055 的 pure linear projection 不 \\\"immune\\\"，只是 L2norm 恰好在 cliff zone 有效。 换用 random pruning，即出现 catastrophic cliff。换 suite（Goal/Long），random 的 cliff 消失但 L2norm 的 advantage 也缩小。 这意味着 \\\"compressibility\\\" 不是 connector 的 intrinsic property，而是 (connector, method, k, task) 四元组的 emergent property。 2-axis framework 的简化——将其压缩为 (connector, task) 二维——在 worst 档数据下失效。 Paper 需要 reframe：不是 \\\"connector determines compressibility\\\"，而是 \\\"we provide the first comprehensive map of the 4D pruning landscape across VLA architectures\\\"。\\n\\n\\nπ0.5（CV=0.055）本应是 \\\"immune\\\" class 的完美验证，但数据揭示了截然不同的图景： (1) Random-specific cliff：k=0.95→71.1% → k=0.925→27.6% → k=0.9→10.8% → k=0.85→5.0%，在 10% keep ratio 变化范围内产生 66pp collapse。这个 cliff 是 random-specific 的——L2norm 在同区间保持 98.0-99.2% 的 plateau。 (2) Fixed-mask experiment 排除了 temporal inconsistency（T0=12% = per-call 12%），证明 cliff 是 spatial coverage 的 structural failure。 (3) V-shape non-monotonicity：L2norm 在 k=0.5 出现 valley（33.4%），k=0.7=55.0% 和 k=0.3=51.0% 都更高。Token position visualization 确认 k=0.5 恰好是 spatial clustering 最严重的点（1 cluster, 78% coverage）。 (4) Cross-suite 数据摧毁 \\\"immune\\\" 标签：random k=0.9 在 Object=9% 但 Goal=62.2%（+53pp），Spatial=54%，Long=31.4%。Object 的 concentrated critical features（visually similar condiments）在 cliff zone 极度脆弱，而 Goal 的 language-disambiguated tasks 对 random token loss 更 robust。 (5) Attention pruning 不解决问题：k=0.7 attn=0.6%（比 random 的 75.5% 差 75pp），k=0.5 attn=37.8%（与 L2norm 33.4% 持平）。π0.5 的 attention map 不提供有效 importance signal。 In worst tier, π0.5 从 \\\"immune class exemplar\\\" 降级为 \\\"case study demonstrating that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of method × k × task, not a simple connector property\\\"。Cross-suite average Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5 = (+36+16+13.8-4.6)/4 = 15.3pp，远低于 Object-only 的 36pp。\\n\"\n314\t  },\n315\t  {\n316\t    \"name\": \"VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (SmolVLA M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\",\n317\t    \"description\": \"SmolVLA VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long suites 上的压缩性能验证。 worst 档：VTR cross-suite recovery 衰减，且 VTR 训练在非 Object suite 上有不稳定性。\\n\",\n318\t    \"results\": {\n319\t      \"vtr_m32_object_sr_pct\": 60.1,\n320\t      \"vtr_m32_spatial_sr_pct\": 53.2,\n321\t      \"vtr_m32_goal_sr_pct\": 56.4,\n322\t      \"vtr_m32_long_sr_pct_predicted\": 48.0,\n323\t      \"smolvla_baseline_object_sr_pct\": 59.2,\n324\t      \"smolvla_baseline_spatial_sr_pct\": 44.6,\n325\t      \"smolvla_baseline_goal_sr_pct\": 60.8,\n326\t      \"smolvla_baseline_long_sr_pct\": 36.6,\n327\t      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_object\": 1.015,\n328\t      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial\": 1.193,\n329\t      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_goal\": 0.928,\n330\t      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_long_predicted\": 0.874,\n331\t      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_mean\": 0.95,\n332\t      \"vtr_m96_dip_p_value\": 0.034,\n333\t      \"vtr_m96_dip_confirmed\": true,\n334\t      \"hard_pruning_k05_all_suites_sr_pct\": 0.0\n335\t    },\n336\t    \"tables\": [\n337\t      {\n338\t        \"title\": \"Table F: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery (SmolVLA)\",\n339\t        \"columns\": [\n340\t          \"Suite\",\n341\t          \"Hard Prune k=0.5(%)\",\n342\t          \"VTR M=32(%)\",\n343\t          \"Baseline(%)\",\n344\t          \"Recovery Ratio\"\n345\t        ],\n346\t        \"rows\": [\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"Object\",\n349\t            \"0.0\",\n350\t            \"60.1\",\n351\t            \"59.2\",\n352\t            \"1.015\"\n353\t          ],\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"Spatial\",\n356\t            \"0.6\",\n357\t            \"53.2\",\n358\t            \"44.6\",\n359\t            \"1.193\"\n360\t          ],\n361\t          [\n362\t            \"Goal\",\n363\t            \"0.0\",\n364\t            \"56.4\",\n365\t            \"60.8\",\n366\t            \"0.928\"\n367\t          ],\n368\t          [\n369\t            \"Long (pred)\",\n370\t            \"0.0\",\n371\t            \"~48\",\n372\t            \"36.6\",\n373\t            \"~0.87\"\n374\t          ]\n375\t        ],\n376\t        \"notes\": \"Recovery ratio 从 Object(1.0) 下降到 Long(0.87)。VTR 在 complex tasks 上 recovery 衰减 ~13%。\"\n377\t      }\n378\t    ],\n379\t    \"figures\": [],\n380\t    \"analysis\": \"VTR 从 \\\"universal compression method\\\" 降级为 \\\"effective recovery tool for pixel-shuffle connectors, with decreasing efficacy on complex tasks\\\"。 M=96 dip 的 statistical significance (p=0.034) 不足以证明 systematic failure（n=3 power ~0.2），但足以引起 reviewer 对 training stability 的质疑。 Cross-suite recovery 衰减是合理的：VTR 在 Object suite 上训练，cross-suite 是 zero-shot transfer。Long-horizon tasks 的 action sequence 依赖 precise temporal-spatial correspondence，VTR 的 cross-attention bottleneck 可能丢失这些 long-range dependencies。 Paper 策略：VTR 作为 §4.7 的 case study 保留，但移除 \\\"universal compression\\\" 措辞，改为 \\\"recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge to near-baseline on trained distribution, with ~13% degradation on out-of-distribution complex tasks\\\"。\\n\\n\\nVTR M=32 在 Object 上实现 near-lossless compression（60.1% vs baseline 59.2%），Spatial 上甚至超过 baseline（53.2% vs 44.6%，可能因为 VTR 训练 regularization 效应）。 但 Goal suite recovery ratio = 56.4/60.8 = 0.928，低于 Object。预测 Long-horizon（未测）recovery ratio 进一步下降至 ~0.87：Long tasks 需要 multi-step reasoning，VTR 的 cross-attention 可能无法完全保留 temporal action sequence 所需的 spatial information chain。 M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）在 worst 档被确认为 training instability（非 statistical fluke），因为 M=96 的 3-seed std=3.2pp 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 VTR 的 flat M-curve 可能是 M=16-64 的幸运区间，M=96 暴露了 cross-attention query 数量与 pixel-shuffle token structure 之间的 resonance 问题。 VTR 仍然是 valid contribution（从 0% hard pruning 恢复到 ~baseline），但 worst 档将其定位为 \\\"SmolVLA-specific case study\\\" 而非 \\\"general method\\\"，因为： (1) cross-suite recovery 有衰减（Goal 0.93, Long predicted 0.87）， (2) M=96 dip 暗示 training sensitivity， (3) OpenVLA VTR 完全失败（下条）。\\n\"\n381\t  },\n382\t  {\n383\t    \"name\": \"VTR Universality Test: OpenVLA MLP Projector (M=128/32/64)\",\n384\t    \"description\": \"VTR 在 OpenVLA（MLP projector）上的泛化性测试。M=128 full VTR 已失败（0% SR），VTC-only M=32/M=64 作为 fallback。\\n\",\n385\t    \"results\": {\n386\t      \"openvla_vtr_m128_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n387\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_pct_predicted\": 3.0,\n388\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_pct_predicted\": 5.0,\n389\t      \"openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_pct_predicted\": 2.0,\n390\t      \"openvla_baseline_sr_pct\": 74.0,\n391\t      \"overfitting_confirmed\": true,\n392\t      \"failure_mode\": \"model outputs identical action every timestep\"\n393\t    },\n394\t    \"tables\": [\n395\t      {\n396\t        \"title\": \"Table G: VTR on OpenVLA — Universal Failure\",\n397\t        \"columns\": [\n398\t          \"Config\",\n399\t          \"M\",\n400\t          \"Params(M)\",\n401\t          \"Steps\",\n402\t          \"Train Loss\",\n403\t          \"SR(%)\"\n404\t        ],\n405\t        \"rows\": [\n406\t          [\n407\t            \"Full VTR\",\n408\t            \"128\",\n409\t            \"22.2\",\n410\t            \"20K\",\n411\t            \"converged\",\n412\t            \"0.0\"\n413\t          ],\n414\t          [\n415\t            \"VTC-only\",\n416\t            \"32\",\n417\t            \"22.2\",\n418\t            \"100K\",\n419\t            \"converged\",\n420\t            \"~3\"\n421\t          ],\n422\t          [\n423\t            \"VTC-only\",\n424\t            \"64\",\n425\t            \"22.2\",\n426\t            \"100K\",\n427\t            \"converged\",\n428\t            \"~5\"\n429\t          ],\n430\t          [\n431\t            \"VTC-only\",\n432\t            \"96\",\n433\t            \"22.2\",\n434\t            \"100K\",\n435\t            \"converged\",\n436\t            \"~2\"\n437\t          ],\n438\t          [\n439\t            \"LoRA baseline\",\n440\t            \"—\",\n441\t            \"883\",\n442\t            \"100K\",\n443\t            \"0.065\",\n444\t            \"0.0\"\n445\t          ]\n446\t        ],\n447\t        \"notes\": \"所有 VTR configs 失败。Train loss 收敛但 SR ≈0。Failure mode: identical action output。\"\n448\t      }\n449\t    ],\n450\t    \"figures\": [],\n451\t    \"analysis\": \"VTR universality 完全失败。这不是 hyperparameter tuning 问题——M=128/96/64/32 全部 <5% SR，且 LoRA fine-tuning 也产生 0% SR（libero_lora_baseline），说明 OpenVLA 的 fine-tuning 本身就 fragile。 Reviewer 会问：\\\"如果 VTR 只在 SmolVLA 上 work，它是在修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement 还是只是在 SmolVLA 的特定 action space 上 overfit？\\\" Response 策略：M=128 passthrough control（58.0% ≈ baseline 59.2%）证明 VTR 确实在学 re-encoding 而非 action space memorization。但这个 argument 仅对 SmolVLA 成立。\\n\\n\\nM=128 VTR 在 20K steps 后 0% SR（model 对所有 observation 输出相同 action）确认 severe overfitting。 VTC-only M=32/M=64 预测同样失败（<5% SR），因为根本原因不在 VTR architecture 而在 MLP projector tokens 的特性： (1) MLP projector tokens 已经是 individually meaningful 的（CV=0.215, 有 gradient differentiation），VTR 的 cross-attention 无法提供额外信息，反而引入 information bottleneck。 (2) OpenVLA 的 256 tokens × 7B parameters 的 scale 与 SmolVLA 的 128 tokens × 450M parameters 完全不同——VTR 的 ~22M params 对 7B model 来说是 rounding error，无法学到有意义的 re-encoding。 (3) M=96/M=64/M=32 的 training loss 持续下降但 eval SR 不恢复，典型的 action space overfitting pattern。 在 worst 档，这确认 VTR 是 pixel-shuffle-specific method。Paper 中 VTR 需要 reframe：不是 \\\"universal compression tool\\\" 而是 \\\"architecture-specific recovery mechanism that works because pixel-shuffle tokens need re-entangling, while MLP tokens are already independent and don't benefit from cross-attention re-encoding\\\"。\\n\"\n452\t  },\n453\t  {\n454\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96)\",\n455\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA 上的 VTC cross-attention compressor M-sweep。所有 M 值预期失败。\\n\",\n456\t    \"results\": {\n457\t      \"openvla_vtc_m32_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n458\t      \"openvla_vtc_m64_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n459\t      \"openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss\": 2.45,\n460\t      \"openvla_vtc_m96_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n461\t      \"all_m_values_fail\": true\n462\t    },\n463\t    \"tables\": [],\n464\t    \"figures\": [],\n465\t    \"analysis\": \"确认 VTR/VTC 在 MLP projector + discrete action space 的组合下无效。 Paper 中作为 negative result 报告：VTR effectiveness = f(connector_type)，strengthens architecture-dependency narrative。\\n\\n\\nM=96 已训完（final train loss 2.45, eval loss 2.66），远高于 SmolVLA VTR 的 ~0.05 train loss。这不是欠拟合——100K steps with OpenVLA 的 tokenized action space 天然产生高 cross-entropy loss。 M=32/M=64 的 v3/v4/v5 版本反复失败（disk full, GPU crash, training instability），即使成功训完也预期 0% SR。 根本原因：OpenVLA 使用 discrete tokenized actions（不是 continuous actions），VTC 的 cross-attention 将 256 个 vision tokens 压缩到 M 个 queries，但 OpenVLA 的 LLM decoder 期望完整的 256-token vision context 来做 autoregressive action token generation。压缩后的 M queries 无法提供 decoder 所需的 token-level spatial precision。\\n\"\n466\t  },\n467\t  {\n468\t    \"name\": \"X-VLA Cliff Threshold Localization (k=0.80/0.85, 3-seed)\",\n469\t    \"description\": \"X-VLA 在 k=0.80 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位 cliff。Non-monotonic pattern 已确认。 worst 档：cliff 是真实的，但 E5 attention pruning 证明它是 L2norm-specific artifact。\\n\",\n470\t    \"results\": {\n471\t      \"xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_mean\": 89.0,\n472\t      \"xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_std\": 0.72,\n473\t      \"xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_mean\": 67.9,\n474\t      \"xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_std\": 0.31,\n475\t      \"xvla_l2norm_nonmonotonic_gap_pp\": 21.1,\n476\t      \"xvla_random_k085_sr_mean\": 63.6,\n477\t      \"xvla_random_k080_sr_mean\": 89.4,\n478\t      \"xvla_e5_attn_k05_sr_mean\": 98.4,\n479\t      \"cliff_is_l2norm_specific\": true,\n480\t      \"cliff_is_method_independent\": false\n481\t    },\n482\t    \"tables\": [\n483\t      {\n484\t        \"title\": \"Table H: X-VLA Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic\",\n485\t        \"columns\": [\n486\t          \"k\",\n487\t          \"L2norm SR(%)\",\n488\t          \"L2norm SD(pp)\",\n489\t          \"Random SR(%)\",\n490\t          \"Attn-Last SR(%)\"\n491\t        ],\n492\t        \"rows\": [\n493\t          [\n494\t            \"0.90\",\n495\t            \"97.6\",\n496\t            \"—\",\n497\t            \"97.8\",\n498\t            \"~99\"\n499\t          ],\n500\t          [\n501\t            \"0.85\",\n502\t            \"67.9\",\n503\t            \"0.31\",\n504\t            \"63.6\",\n505\t            \"~97\"\n506\t          ],\n507\t          [\n508\t            \"0.80\",\n509\t            \"89.0\",\n510\t            \"0.72\",\n511\t            \"89.4\",\n512\t            \"~99\"\n513\t          ],\n514\t          [\n515\t            \"0.70\",\n516\t            \"56.2\",\n517\t            \"—\",\n518\t            \"65.2\",\n519\t            \"99.2\"\n520\t          ],\n521\t          [\n522\t            \"0.50\",\n523\t            \"42.6\",\n524\t            \"—\",\n525\t            \"70.6\",\n526\t            \"99.2\"\n527\t          ]\n528\t        ],\n529\t        \"notes\": \"Attention pruning 完全消除 cliff 和 degradation。问题在 metric 不在 architecture。\"\n530\t      }\n531\t    ],\n532\t    \"figures\": [],\n533\t    \"analysis\": \"Cliff localization 数据本身是 solid experimental result。但在 worst 档，E5 data 完全改变其解读： cliff 不是 connector architecture 的 intrinsic property，而是 L2norm importance metric 在 low-CV distribution 上的 pathological behavior。 Attention pruning（zero additional training）消除所有 degradation，这意味着 BART encoder 并没有 \\\"entangle\\\" tokens in a way that prevents pruning，它只是让 tokens 的 L2-norm 不再是 good importance proxy。 Paper 需要重新定义 Axis-1：从 \\\"token coupling\\\" 改为 \\\"importance metric suitability\\\"，或者承认 2-axis framework 是 L2norm-specific observation 而非 architecture-level insight。\\n\\n\\nX-VLA k=0.85 L2norm = 67.9%±0.31pp（3-seed，SD<1pp 确认完全 deterministic）。k=0.80 = 89.0%±0.72pp。 Non-monotonic gap = 21.1pp（k=0.85 < k=0.80），2-token 差异产生 21pp SR change。Random pruning 在同区间也出现 cliff（63.6% vs 89.4%），但 per-task crash pattern 不同（T4, T6 both crash across methods → architectural bottleneck）。 在 worst 档，这个 cliff 的意义被 E5 attention pruning 完全重新诠释： - L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% → attn_last k=0.5 = 99.2%（+56.6pp） - 同样的 50 tokens，同样的 k=0.5（保留 25 tokens），attention 几乎完美而 L2norm catastrophic - 因此 cliff 不是 \\\"BART encoder entanglement creates irreversible token dependencies\\\"，而是 \\\"L2norm 在 BART encoder 的 near-uniform norm distribution 上退化为 spatially clustered selection\\\" - Reviewer argument：\\\"如果换 importance metric 就消除了 cliff，那 Axis-1 的 'token coupling' 定义有根本缺陷——关键不在 coupling 而在 importance metric。\\\"\\n\"\n534\t  },\n535\t  {\n536\t    \"name\": \"OFT CV Diagnostic (Token Importance Measurement)\",\n537\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA-OFT 的 token importance CV 测量。Expected CV≈0.219（≈Standard OpenVLA）。\\n\",\n538\t    \"results\": {\n539\t      \"oft_cv\": 0.219,\n540\t      \"oft_cv_std\": 0.012,\n541\t      \"oft_entropy\": 0.667,\n542\t      \"openvla_standard_cv\": 0.215,\n543\t      \"cv_delta_pp\": 0.4,\n544\t      \"sr_eval_blocked\": true,\n545\t      \"gpu_incompatibility\": \"Blackwell SDPA requires A100+torch2.2\"\n546\t    },\n547\t    \"tables\": [\n548\t      {\n549\t        \"title\": \"Table I: Diagnostic Metrics — 6-Model Spectrum\",\n550\t        \"columns\": [\n551\t          \"Model\",\n552\t          \"Connector\",\n553\t          \"CV\",\n554\t          \"Entropy\",\n555\t          \"Eval SR Available?\"\n556\t        ],\n557\t        \"rows\": [\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"π0\",\n560\t            \"Pure linear\",\n561\t            \"0.038\",\n562\t            \"0.959\",\n563\t            \"Offline only\"\n564\t          ],\n565\t          [\n566\t            \"π0.5\",\n567\t            \"Pure linear (×√d)\",\n568\t            \"0.055\",\n569\t            \"—\",\n570\t            \"Yes (4 suites)\"\n571\t          ],\n572\t          [\n573\t            \"X-VLA\",\n574\t            \"Linear + BART 12L\",\n575\t            \"0.151\",\n576\t            \"0.614\",\n577\t            \"Yes (4 suites)\"\n578\t          ],\n579\t          [\n580\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n581\t            \"3-layer MLP\",\n582\t            \"0.215\",\n583\t            \"0.661\",\n584\t            \"Yes (Object only)\"\n585\t          ],\n586\t          [\n587\t            \"OFT\",\n588\t            \"3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\",\n589\t            \"0.219\",\n590\t            \"0.667\",\n591\t            \"No (GPU blocked)\"\n592\t          ],\n593\t          [\n594\t            \"SmolVLA\",\n595\t            \"Pixel-shuffle\",\n596\t            \"0.314\",\n597\t            \"0.952\",\n598\t            \"Yes (4 suites)\"\n599\t          ]\n600\t        ],\n601\t        \"notes\": \"6 models 有 CV，但仅 3 models 有 full cross-suite SR。OFT 和 π0 只有 diagnostic metrics。\"\n602\t      }\n603\t    ],\n604\t    \"figures\": [],\n605\t    \"analysis\": \"OFT CV 完成了 6-model diagnostic table，但不改变任何结论。在 worst 档，这是 incrementally supportive 而非 decisive evidence。\\n\\n\\nOFT CV=0.219 ≈ Standard OpenVLA CV=0.215（Δ=0.004），确认 connector（3-layer MLP）而非 action head（OFT vs standard）决定 token importance distribution。 Entropy 也几乎相同（0.667 vs 0.661）。这是 framework 的 positive confirmation——same connector → same CV → same predicted pruning behavior。 但在 worst 档，这个 data point 的价值有限： (1) 无法在 LIBERO 上 eval SR（Blackwell GPU SDPA 不兼容），所以 CV 预测没有 ground truth 验证 (2) OFT 和 Standard OpenVLA 用相同 connector 产生相同 CV 是 trivially expected，不提供 additional discrimination power (3) Reviewer 会指出：\\\"你们有 6 个 model 的 CV，但只有 4 个能实际 eval SR。CV 作为 predictor 的 validation set 太小。\\\"\\n\"\n606\t  },\n607\t  {\n608\t    \"name\": \"OFT Full Graded-Class Evaluation (4 Suites)\",\n609\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA-OFT 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 上的 baseline + pruning evaluation。 worst 档：GPU 不兼容问题持续，无法完成 evaluation。\\n\",\n610\t    \"results\": {\n611\t      \"eval_blocked\": true,\n612\t      \"blocker\": \"Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility with OpenVLA-OFT\",\n613\t      \"workaround_attempted\": \"A100 rental, torch2.2 downgrade — both failed\",\n614\t      \"fallback_evidence\": \"CV=0.219≈OpenVLA, entropy=0.667≈0.661 — inferred graded behavior\",\n615\t      \"paper_impact\": \"Missing 2nd graded-class SR data point, relies on CV inference\",\n616\t      \"reviewer_risk\": \"Moderate — 2/3 connector classes have ≥2 SR-evaluated models, MLP class has only 1\"\n617\t    },\n618\t    \"tables\": [],\n619\t    \"figures\": [],\n620\t    \"analysis\": \"Missing OFT SR data 在 worst 档是 acknowledged limitation。Reviewer concern 等级 \\\"moderate\\\"——不会 reject paper，但会要求 camera-ready 补充或更 cautious language about MLP class generalization。\\n\\n\\nOFT evaluation 在 worst 档仍然被 GPU 不兼容阻塞。Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA implementation 与 OFT checkpoint 的 torch 版本不兼容，降级 torch 或租用 A100 都不可行（timeline 限制）。 Paper 只能用 CV/entropy comparison 间接 argue OFT follows OpenVLA pattern。Reviewer 会注意到 MLP projector class 只有 OpenVLA 1 个 model 有 SR data，不足以 generalize。 CogACT（literature baseline, MLP projector, 74.8%→74.2% under 78% pruning from EfficientVLA）可以作为 external evidence，但不是 our own evaluation。 In worst tier, this is a clear gap but not fatal — pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA, 1 model, universal 0%) and linear (π0/π0.5, 2 models, variable) are well-characterized. MLP class has 1 internal + 1 external data point.\\n\"\n621\t  },\n622\t  {\n623\t    \"name\": \"Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — 3rd Connector Family\",\n624\t    \"description\": \"RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) 在 LIBERO 上 fine-tune + pruning。 worst 档：fine-tuning 产生低 baseline，且 Perceiver 不清晰地落入 2-axis taxonomy。\\n\",\n625\t    \"results\": {\n626\t      \"fine_tuning_baseline_sr_pct_predicted\": 18.0,\n627\t      \"fine_tuning_difficulty\": \"high — requires custom training pipeline adaptation\",\n628\t      \"perceiver_cv_predicted\": 0.28,\n629\t      \"perceiver_pruning_k09_predicted_sr_pct\": 4.0,\n630\t      \"perceiver_pruning_k05_predicted_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n631\t      \"taxonomy_fit\": \"ambiguous — cross-attention creates partial entanglement different from both pixel-shuffle and BART\",\n632\t      \"paper_inclusion\": \"dropped — insufficient time and unclear taxonomy value\"\n633\t    },\n634\t    \"tables\": [],\n635\t    \"figures\": [],\n636\t    \"analysis\": \"Dropping RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档是 rational choice：paper 已经有足够的 models（5 models × 4 suites）作为 empirical contribution，加入一个 low-baseline 的新 connector 只会模糊 narrative。 但这意味着 paper 的 connector 覆盖限于 linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle 三类，reviewer 可能指出 \\\"what about attention-based connectors (Perceiver, Q-Former)?\\\" 作为 limitation。\\n\\n\\nRoboFlamingo 在 worst 档面临多重困难： (1) Fine-tuning infrastructure：RoboFlamingo 使用 Flamingo-style cross-attention perceiver resampler，将 variable-length vision tokens 压缩到 fixed 64 queries。这需要 custom training pipeline，previous attempts (train_c5_roboflamingo_v2) 被 killed。 (2) Low baseline：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 在 LIBERO manipulation tasks 上可能不如 direct projection（SmolVLA 59.2%, OpenVLA 74%），因为 LIBERO 需要 precise spatial information 而 perceiver 天然是 lossy compression。预测 baseline ~18% SR。 (3) Taxonomy ambiguity：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 与 BART encoder 的 self-attention 和 pixel-shuffle 的 spatial folding 都不同。它是 \\\"learned entanglement\\\" 而非 \\\"structural entanglement\\\"。CV 可能在 0.2-0.3 range，不清晰地落入现有 taxonomy。 (4) Timeline：距 abstract deadline 1 天，paper deadline 4 天，没有时间 debug fine-tuning pipeline + run full evaluation。 In worst tier, RoboFlamingo 被 dropped from paper。这减少了 paper 的 connector family 覆盖（3→2 confirmed families），但避免了 messy data 进一步复杂化已经 fragile 的 framework。\\n\"\n637\t  },\n638\t  {\n639\t    \"name\": \"VTR M-Sweep Completion (SmolVLA 3-seed × 5 M-values)\",\n640\t    \"description\": \"SmolVLA VTR M-sweep 的 3-seed 完成和 MLP adapter control。 worst 档：数据 solid 但 M=96 dip 和 high variance 引起质疑。\\n\",\n641\t    \"results\": {\n642\t      \"m16_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 56.9,\n643\t      \"m16_3seed_std_pp\": 1.3,\n644\t      \"m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 60.1,\n645\t      \"m32_3seed_std_pp\": 1.3,\n646\t      \"m64_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 62.0,\n647\t      \"m64_3seed_std_pp\": 2.3,\n648\t      \"m96_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 54.5,\n649\t      \"m96_3seed_std_pp\": 3.2,\n650\t      \"m128_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 58.0,\n651\t      \"m128_3seed_std_pp\": 3.5,\n652\t      \"mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 63.4,\n653\t      \"mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std_pp\": 2.6,\n654\t      \"vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue\": 0.15,\n655\t      \"m64_vs_m96_pvalue\": 0.034,\n656\t      \"baseline_sr_pct\": 59.2,\n657\t      \"m_curve_flat_within_3pp\": true,\n658\t      \"m96_dip_significant\": true\n659\t    },\n660\t    \"tables\": [\n661\t      {\n662\t        \"title\": \"Table J: VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Results\",\n663\t        \"columns\": [\n664\t          \"M\",\n665\t          \"Compression(%)\",\n666\t          \"Mean SR(%)\",\n667\t          \"Std(pp)\",\n668\t          \"Individual Seeds\",\n669\t          \"vs Baseline\"\n670\t        ],\n671\t        \"rows\": [\n672\t          [\n673\t            \"16\",\n674\t            \"87.5\",\n675\t            \"56.9\",\n676\t            \"1.3\",\n677\t            \"55.8/58.4/56.5\",\n678\t            \"-2.3pp\"\n679\t          ],\n680\t          [\n681\t            \"32\",\n682\t            \"75.0\",\n683\t            \"60.1\",\n684\t            \"1.3\",\n685\t            \"61.6/59.2/59.6\",\n686\t            \"+0.9pp\"\n687\t          ],\n688\t          [\n689\t            \"64\",\n690\t            \"50.0\",\n691\t            \"62.0\",\n692\t            \"2.3\",\n693\t            \"61.6/60.0/64.4\",\n694\t            \"+2.8pp\"\n695\t          ],\n696\t          [\n697\t            \"96\",\n698\t            \"25.0\",\n699\t            \"54.5\",\n700\t            \"3.2\",\n701\t            \"52.6/58.2/52.8\",\n702\t            \"-4.7pp\"\n703\t          ],\n704\t          [\n705\t            \"128\",\n706\t            \"0.0\",\n707\t            \"58.0\",\n708\t            \"3.5\",\n709\t            \"59.8/54.0/60.2\",\n710\t            \"-1.2pp\"\n711\t          ],\n712\t          [\n713\t            \"MLP-32\",\n714\t            \"75.0\",\n715\t            \"63.4\",\n716\t            \"2.6\",\n717\t            \"65.2/64.6/60.4\",\n718\t            \"+4.2pp\"\n719\t          ]\n720\t        ],\n721\t        \"notes\": \"M=96 dip p=0.034。M=128 seed43=54.0 outlier。Flat M-curve 成立但 variance 在高 M 处增大。\"\n722\t      }\n723\t    ],\n724\t    \"figures\": [],\n725\t    \"analysis\": \"VTR 在 worst 档仍是 paper 的 positive contribution：hard pruning 0% → VTR ~59% ≈ baseline 是 dramatic recovery。 但 M=96 dip 和 high-M variance 需要 honest reporting。建议 paper 用 M=32 或 M=64 作为 recommended setting（stable seeds, good compression ratio），将 M=96 dip 作为 \\\"open question: why does M=96 underperform?\\\" 放入 discussion。 Reviewer concern level: low-moderate. VTR 的 core claim（recovery from 0% to baseline）is robust. M=96 是 interesting anomaly 但不 undermine main contribution。\\n\\n\\nVTR M-sweep 数据 intrinsically solid：M=16(56.9%) 到 M=128(58.0%) 都在 baseline 59.2% 的 ±5pp 内，证明 near-lossless compression at any ratio。MLP adapter control（63.4%）与 VTC（60.1%）无显著差异（p=0.15），确认 architecture independence。 但 worst 档关注两个 weakness： (1) M=96 dip（54.5%, p=0.034 vs M=64=62.0%）虽然在 Bonferroni correction 后 marginally significant，但 3.2pp std 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 training instability——某些 seed/M 组合在 training dynamics 中进入 suboptimal basin。 (2) M=128 passthrough 的 3.5pp std 也高，且 seed43=54.0% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 59.8/60.2%）。如果 passthrough control 本身有 6pp variance，\\\"near-lossless\\\" 的声称需要 caveat。 In worst tier, VTR 仍然是 valid method（0%→~59% recovery），但 training stability concern 使其从 \\\"recommended practice\\\" 降级为 \\\"promising but needs further investigation\\\"。\\n\"\n726\t  },\n727\t  {\n728\t    \"name\": \"Consolidated Cross-Suite Framework Accuracy Assessment\",\n729\t    \"description\": \"综合所有 cross-suite 数据的 framework 准确率评估。 worst 档：framework accuracy ~62%，不足以支撑 \\\"principled framework\\\" 定位。\\n\",\n730\t    \"results\": {\n731\t      \"framework_predictions_total\": 20,\n732\t      \"framework_predictions_correct\": 12,\n733\t      \"framework_accuracy_pct\": 62,\n734\t      \"claims_surviving_review\": 2.5,\n735\t      \"surviving_claims\": \"C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement), C4 (VTR case study), partial C3b (MLP graded)\",\n736\t      \"failed_claims\": \"C1 (2-axis framework as principled theory), C5 (CV universal predictor)\",\n737\t      \"reframed_claims\": \"C1→empirical observation catalog, C5→within-suite heuristic\",\n738\t      \"paper_contribution_type\": \"empirical study with surprising findings\",\n739\t      \"corl_submission_viable\": true,\n740\t      \"corl_acceptance_probability_pct\": 45\n741\t    },\n742\t    \"tables\": [\n743\t      {\n744\t        \"title\": \"Table K: Framework Prediction Accuracy by Model\",\n745\t        \"columns\": [\n746\t          \"Model\",\n747\t          \"Connector Class\",\n748\t          \"Framework Prediction\",\n749\t          \"Object\",\n750\t          \"Spatial\",\n751\t          \"Goal\",\n752\t          \"Long\",\n753\t          \"Accuracy\"\n754\t        ],\n755\t        \"rows\": [\n756\t          [\n757\t            \"SmolVLA\",\n758\t            \"Pixel-shuffle\",\n759\t            \"Catastrophic all suites\",\n760\t            \"✓\",\n761\t            \"✓\",\n762\t            \"✓\",\n763\t            \"✓\",\n764\t            \"4/4\"\n765\t          ],\n766\t          [\n767\t            \"X-VLA\",\n768\t            \"BART encoder\",\n769\t            \"Task-dependent collapse\",\n770\t            \"✗(no collapse)\",\n771\t            \"✓\",\n772\t            \"✓\",\n773\t            \"✓\",\n774\t            \"3/4\"\n775\t          ],\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"π0.5\",\n778\t            \"Linear proj\",\n779\t            \"Immune to task complexity\",\n780\t            \"✗(random cliff)\",\n781\t            \"✗\",\n782\t            \"✗\",\n783\t            \"✗\",\n784\t            \"1/4\"\n785\t          ],\n786\t          [\n787\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n788\t            \"MLP\",\n789\t            \"Graded, L2norm preferred\",\n790\t            \"✓\",\n791\t            \"~\",\n792\t            \"✗(random preferred)\",\n793\t            \"~\",\n794\t            \"2/4\"\n795\t          ],\n796\t          [\n797\t            \"π0\",\n798\t            \"Linear proj\",\n799\t            \"Immune\",\n800\t            \"✓(offline)\",\n801\t            \"—\",\n802\t            \"—\",\n803\t            \"—\",\n804\t            \"1/1\"\n805\t          ]\n806\t        ],\n807\t        \"notes\": \"Total 11/17 ≈ 65%。π0.5 是 framework 最大 failure point。\"\n808\t      },\n809\t      {\n810\t        \"title\": \"Table L: Claim Survival Assessment\",\n811\t        \"columns\": [\n812\t          \"Claim\",\n813\t          \"Original Status\",\n814\t          \"Worst-Tier Status\",\n815\t          \"Surviving Evidence\"\n816\t        ],\n817\t        \"rows\": [\n818\t          [\n819\t            \"C1: 2-Axis Framework\",\n820\t            \"Primary contribution\",\n821\t            \"Fails as theory\",\n822\t            \"Descriptive taxonomy for L2norm-Object only\"\n823\t          ],\n824\t          [\n825\t            \"C2: Pixel-Shuffle Entanglement\",\n826\t            \"Strong\",\n827\t            \"Survives\",\n828\t            \"Universal 0% across 4 suites × 2 methods\"\n829\t          ],\n830\t          [\n831\t            \"C3: Connector-Specific Patterns\",\n832\t            \"Strong\",\n833\t            \"Partial survival\",\n834\t            \"MLP graded confirmed; linear 'immune' falsified\"\n835\t          ],\n836\t          [\n837\t            \"C4: VTR Recovery\",\n838\t            \"Strong\",\n839\t            \"Survives as case study\",\n840\t            \"0%→59% on SmolVLA; fails on OpenVLA\"\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"C5: CV Scaling Law\",\n844\t            \"Novel contribution\",\n845\t            \"Fails as universal\",\n846\t            \"Within-Object heuristic only; cross-suite |ρ|≈0.45\"\n847\t          ]\n848\t        ],\n849\t        \"notes\": \"2-3 claims survive review intact. Paper viable as empirical study, not as theory paper.\"\n850\t      }\n851\t    ],\n852\t    \"figures\": [],\n853\t    \"analysis\": \"在 worst 档，paper 的 identity 发生根本转变： FROM: \\\"We discover a principled 2-axis framework governing VLA token compressibility\\\" TO: \\\"We provide the first systematic study of token pruning across VLA architectures, revealing that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of (connector, method, k, task), not reducible to simple architectural rules\\\"\\nKey novel findings that survive independently of the framework: (1) Pixel-shuffle entanglement is real and irreversible — this is a genuine architectural insight (2) Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — supported by E5 attention data + π0.5 method divergence (3) L2norm is actively harmful on low-CV models — 36pp gap on π0.5, 28pp on X-VLA at k=0.5 Object (4) VTR achieves near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle — 0%→59% at any M ratio\\nThese 4 findings are individually publishable observations that together constitute a substantial empirical contribution for CoRL, even without a unified theory. Title: \\\"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures.\\\"\\n\\nFramework accuracy 计算方法： - SmolVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"catastrophic at k=0.95\\\" → 实际 all suites ≤0.1% → 4/4 correct - X-VLA × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"entangling, task-dependent collapse\\\" → Object OK (97.6%), Goal 70.2% (partial collapse), Spatial 78.8% (moderate), Long 27.5% (collapse) → 3/4 correct（Object 不 collapse，与预测不符） - π0.5 × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"independent, immune to task complexity\\\" → Object random k=0.9=9%（NOT immune!），但 L2norm=98.2% → method-dependent → 1/4 correct（框架不区分 method） - OpenVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"graded, L2norm preferred\\\" → Object L2norm>random (+1.8pp ✓), Goal random>L2norm (+8.8pp ✗) → 2/4 correct - π0 × offline: 预测 \\\"immune\\\" → k=0.1 improves → 1/1 correct Total: 4+3+1+2+1 = 11/17 = 65%（≈62% with margin of error）\\nClaims survival analysis: - C1 (2-axis framework): FAILS as theory → survives as \\\"descriptive taxonomy for L2norm pruning on Object suite\\\" - C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement): SURVIVES — universal 0% across all suites/methods/k is unambiguous - C3a (linear proj depends on pipeline): Partially survives — π0 immune, π0.5 method-dependent, X-VLA cliff - C3b (MLP graded): Survives on Object — graded curve confirmed - C4 (VTR): Survives as SmolVLA case study — 0%→59% recovery - C5 (CV predicts strategy): FAILS as universal law → survives as \\\"within-Object-suite heuristic\\\"\\n2.5 claims survive: C2, C4, half of C3b.\\nCoRL viability: paper 作为 \\\"comprehensive empirical study\\\" 仍然 viable（5 models × 4 suites × 3 methods 是任何 VLA pruning 工作中最大规模的 comparison）。Acceptance probability ~45%——足够好的 empirical contribution 但缺少 unified theory 会让某些 reviewers 觉得 \\\"incremental\\\"。\\n\"\n854\t  }\n855\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66dfde6d-dd0a-44a8-9964-18ea8fcd5ba7","uuid":"d9b27d81-355e-4825-bcbb-d910594ee45c","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:52:50.881Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T050917/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Suite Expansion: π0.5 + X-VLA + OpenVLA + SmolVLA × 4 Suites\",\n    \"description\": \"将所有 5 models 的 pruning 实验从 Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。 核心目的：验证 2-axis framework 的 cross-suite 一致性。 实际结果：framework 在 Object suite 上准确，但 cross-suite 后出现系统性偏差。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct\": 9.3,\n      \"pi05_random_k09_goal_sr_pct\": 62.2,\n      \"pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr_pct\": 54.0,\n      \"pi05_random_k09_long_sr_pct\": 31.4,\n      \"pi05_random_k09_cross_suite_range_pp\": 52.9,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct\": 89.6,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct\": 95.3,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct\": 80.0,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_cross_suite_range_pp\": 18.2,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct\": 97.6,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k09_goal_sr_pct\": 70.2,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr_pct\": 78.8,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k09_long_sr_pct\": 27.5,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k095_long_sr_pct\": 47.0,\n      \"smolvla_k095_all_suites_sr_pct\": \"<0.1 (all 4 suites)\",\n      \"cv_strategy_spearman_object\": -1.0,\n      \"cv_strategy_spearman_goal\": -0.5,\n      \"cv_strategy_spearman_long\": 0.5,\n      \"cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean\": 0.45,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_object_pp\": 36.0,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_goal_pp\": 13.8,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_pi05_long_pp\": -4.6,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_object_pp\": 28.0,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_goal_pp\": 8.5,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_xvla_long_pp\": 17.0,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_object_pp\": -1.8,\n      \"delta_R_L2_k05_openvla_goal_pp\": 8.8,\n      \"framework_accuracy_pct\": 62,\n      \"axis2_amplification_entangling_minus_independent_pp\": 11.4,\n      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_object_sr_pct\": 99.2,\n      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_goal_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial_sr_pct\": 88.8,\n      \"e5_xvla_attn_last_k05_long_sr_pct\": 90.2,\n      \"e5_xvla_attn_mean_k05_long_sr_pct\": 94.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table A: Cross-Suite Δ(Random-L2norm) at k=0.5 — CV Scaling Law Breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"CV\",\n          \"Object Δ(pp)\",\n          \"Spatial Δ(pp)\",\n          \"Goal Δ(pp)\",\n          \"Long Δ(pp)\",\n          \"Range(pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"π0.5\",\n            \"0.055\",\n            \"+36.0\",\n            \"+16.0\",\n            \"+13.8\",\n            \"-4.6\",\n            \"40.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"X-VLA\",\n            \"0.151\",\n            \"+28.0\",\n            \"+12.6\",\n            \"+8.5\",\n            \"+17.0\",\n            \"19.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"0.215\",\n            \"-1.8\",\n            \"~+5\",\n            \"+8.8\",\n            \"~+3\",\n            \"~10.6\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Object suite 上 monotonic（ρ=-1.0），Long suite 上 π0.5 reversal 破坏 monotonicity。Cross-suite mean |ρ|≈0.45。\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table B: π0.5 Random k=0.9 Cross-Suite — Token-Independent ≠ Task-Independent\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Suite\",\n          \"Baseline(%)\",\n          \"Random k=0.9(%)\",\n          \"Δ from baseline(pp)\",\n          \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\",\n          \"Method gap(pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Object\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"9.3\",\n            \"-88.9\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"-88.9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"97.2\",\n            \"54.0\",\n            \"-43.2\",\n            \"95.3\",\n            \"-41.3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"96.4\",\n            \"62.2\",\n            \"-34.2\",\n            \"89.6\",\n            \"-27.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Long\",\n            \"92.8\",\n            \"31.4\",\n            \"-61.4\",\n            \"80.0\",\n            \"-12.8\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Cross-suite range 53pp for random vs 18pp for L2norm。Task sensitivity 是 method-specific，非 architecture-level property。\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table C: E5 Attention Pruning Demolishes Entanglement Narrative (X-VLA k=0.5)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Suite\",\n          \"L2norm(%)\",\n          \"Random(%)\",\n          \"Attn-Last(%)\",\n          \"Attn-Mean(%)\",\n          \"Best Attn vs L2norm(pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Object\",\n            \"42.6\",\n            \"70.6\",\n            \"99.2\",\n            \"98.4\",\n            \"+56.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"58.8\",\n            \"71.4\",\n            \"88.8\",\n            \"91.6\",\n            \"+32.8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"59.0\",\n            \"67.2\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"97.4\",\n            \"+38.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Long\",\n            \"44.6\",\n            \"61.6\",\n            \"90.2\",\n            \"94.0\",\n            \"+49.4\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Attention pruning 在所有 4 suites 上实现 88-99% SR at k=0.5。问题不在 connector entanglement，在 importance metric。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-suite 数据系统性地破坏 2-axis framework 的两个核心预测： (1) Axis-1 独立性：token-independent connectors should be immune to task complexity → π0.5 random k=0.9 Object=9% vs Goal=62% 证伪（53pp gap）。 (2) CV universal predictor：CV 应在所有 suite 上预测 method preference → Long-horizon 上 π0.5 出现 reversal（L2norm > random），OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也 reversal。 E5 attention pruning 数据进一步瓦解 Axis-1 定义：X-VLA（\\\"entangling\\\"）在 attention pruning 下表现如同 \\\"independent\\\" connector。Axis-1 的区分不在 \\\"token coupling\\\" 而在 \\\"susceptibility to norm-based importance bias\\\"。 Reframe：论文不能声称发现了 governing principle，而应定位为 \\\"comprehensive empirical study revealing that importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture\\\"。\\n\\n\\nπ0.5 random k=0.9 在 Object 上出现 catastrophic cliff（9.3%），但在 Goal 上仅下降至 62.2%——同一 linear projection connector、同一 random method、同一 k，仅 task distribution 不同就产生 53pp 差异。这直接破坏 \\\"token-independent connector 不受 task complexity 影响\\\" 的核心假设。 机制：Object suite 需要 precise object identity discrimination（visually similar condiments），random 在 cliff zone 摧毁 concentrated discriminative features；Goal suite 的 task 由 language instruction 区分，vision tokens 冗余度更高，random 破坏的影响小。 L2norm 在相同 k=0.9 的 cross-suite range 仅 18.2pp（vs random 53pp），证明 cross-suite sensitivity 是 METHOD-dependent 而非 connector-dependent。 E5 attention pruning 数据更具破坏性：X-VLA k=0.5 attn_last=99.2%（Object）、98.2%（Goal），vs L2norm=42.6%/59%。这意味着 X-VLA 的 \\\"entanglement\\\" 问题完全可以通过更换 importance metric 解决，BART encoder 产生的不是 \\\"irreversible entanglement\\\" 而是 \\\"norm-unfriendly importance distribution\\\"。 CV scaling law 在 Object 内仍然成立（Spearman -1.0），但 Long-horizon 出现反转（π0.5 L2norm > random，Δ=-4.6pp），导致 cross-suite 平均 |ρ|≈0.45，远低于 paper 声称的 \\\"universal predictor\\\" 所需的 >0.8。 OpenVLA 在 Goal 上也出现 method preference reversal（random > L2norm +8.8pp），而 Object 上 L2norm > random（+1.8pp）。同一 CV=0.215 的 model，跨 suite 后 method preference 反转。 Framework 在 20 个 model×suite 预测中仅正确约 12 个（62%），达不到 \\\"principled framework\\\" 标准。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"π0.5 Token-Independent Confirmation (4B, Linear Proj)\",\n    \"description\": \"π0.5 作为 2nd token-independent data point，验证 CV=0.055 的 linear projection 在所有 suite 上的 pruning 行为。 worst 档：π0.5 数据揭示 \\\"immune class\\\" 不存在——random pruning 在 cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) 产生 catastrophic collapse，且行为极度 task-dependent。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pi05_cv\": 0.055,\n      \"pi05_baseline_object_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n      \"pi05_baseline_spatial_sr_pct\": 97.2,\n      \"pi05_baseline_goal_sr_pct\": 96.4,\n      \"pi05_baseline_long_sr_pct\": 92.8,\n      \"pi05_random_k095_object_sr_pct\": 71.1,\n      \"pi05_random_k0925_object_sr_pct\": 27.6,\n      \"pi05_random_k09_object_sr_pct\": 10.8,\n      \"pi05_random_k085_object_sr_pct\": 5.0,\n      \"pi05_random_k07_object_sr_pct\": 75.5,\n      \"pi05_random_k05_object_sr_pct\": 69.4,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr_pct\": 98.2,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr_pct\": 98.0,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr_pct\": 33.4,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr_pct\": 51.0,\n      \"pi05_random_cliff_depth_pp\": 66.1,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_v_shape_depth_pp\": 17.6,\n      \"pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_cross_suite_avg_pp\": 15.3,\n      \"pi05_attention_k07_object_sr_pct\": 0.6,\n      \"pi05_attention_k05_object_sr_pct\": 37.8,\n      \"pi05_attention_k095_object_sr_pct\": 98.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table D: π0.5 Random Cliff Zone (Object Suite)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"k\",\n          \"Tokens kept\",\n          \"Random SR(%)\",\n          \"L2norm SR(%)\",\n          \"Δ(L2-R)(pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.95\",\n            \"730\",\n            \"71.1\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"+27.1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.925\",\n            \"710\",\n            \"27.6\",\n            \"99.2\",\n            \"+71.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            \"691\",\n            \"10.8\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"+87.4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.85\",\n            \"653\",\n            \"5.0\",\n            \"98.0\",\n            \"+93.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.70\",\n            \"538\",\n            \"75.5\",\n            \"55.0\",\n            \"-20.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"384\",\n            \"69.4\",\n            \"33.4\",\n            \"-36.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.30\",\n            \"230\",\n            \"36.4\",\n            \"51.0\",\n            \"+14.6\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"方法偏好在 k=0.7 附近反转。Cliff zone (k=0.85-0.925) L2norm 完胜；aggressive zone (k=0.5-0.7) random 完胜。\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table E: π0.5 Cross-Suite Random k=0.9 — 'Immune' Class Falsified\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Suite\",\n          \"Baseline(%)\",\n          \"Random k=0.9(%)\",\n          \"L2norm k=0.9(%)\",\n          \"Δ from baseline (random, pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Object\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"9.3\",\n            \"98.2\",\n            \"-88.9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"97.2\",\n            \"54.0\",\n            \"95.3\",\n            \"-43.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"96.4\",\n            \"62.2\",\n            \"89.6\",\n            \"-34.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Long\",\n            \"92.8\",\n            \"31.4\",\n            \"80.0\",\n            \"-61.4\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"同一 model/method/k，cross-suite range=53pp。Framework 预测 token-independent 应 <5pp variation。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"π0.5 数据是 worst 档的 smoking gun：CV=0.055 的 pure linear projection 不 \\\"immune\\\"，只是 L2norm 恰好在 cliff zone 有效。 换用 random pruning，即出现 catastrophic cliff。换 suite（Goal/Long），random 的 cliff 消失但 L2norm 的 advantage 也缩小。 这意味着 \\\"compressibility\\\" 不是 connector 的 intrinsic property，而是 (connector, method, k, task) 四元组的 emergent property。 2-axis framework 的简化——将其压缩为 (connector, task) 二维——在 worst 档数据下失效。 Paper 需要 reframe：不是 \\\"connector determines compressibility\\\"，而是 \\\"we provide the first comprehensive map of the 4D pruning landscape across VLA architectures\\\"。\\n\\n\\nπ0.5（CV=0.055）本应是 \\\"immune\\\" class 的完美验证，但数据揭示了截然不同的图景： (1) Random-specific cliff：k=0.95→71.1% → k=0.925→27.6% → k=0.9→10.8% → k=0.85→5.0%，在 10% keep ratio 变化范围内产生 66pp collapse。这个 cliff 是 random-specific 的——L2norm 在同区间保持 98.0-99.2% 的 plateau。 (2) Fixed-mask experiment 排除了 temporal inconsistency（T0=12% = per-call 12%），证明 cliff 是 spatial coverage 的 structural failure。 (3) V-shape non-monotonicity：L2norm 在 k=0.5 出现 valley（33.4%），k=0.7=55.0% 和 k=0.3=51.0% 都更高。Token position visualization 确认 k=0.5 恰好是 spatial clustering 最严重的点（1 cluster, 78% coverage）。 (4) Cross-suite 数据摧毁 \\\"immune\\\" 标签：random k=0.9 在 Object=9% 但 Goal=62.2%（+53pp），Spatial=54%，Long=31.4%。Object 的 concentrated critical features（visually similar condiments）在 cliff zone 极度脆弱，而 Goal 的 language-disambiguated tasks 对 random token loss 更 robust。 (5) Attention pruning 不解决问题：k=0.7 attn=0.6%（比 random 的 75.5% 差 75pp），k=0.5 attn=37.8%（与 L2norm 33.4% 持平）。π0.5 的 attention map 不提供有效 importance signal。 In worst tier, π0.5 从 \\\"immune class exemplar\\\" 降级为 \\\"case study demonstrating that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of method × k × task, not a simple connector property\\\"。Cross-suite average Δ(R-L2) at k=0.5 = (+36+16+13.8-4.6)/4 = 15.3pp，远低于 Object-only 的 36pp。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (SmolVLA M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\",\n    \"description\": \"SmolVLA VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long suites 上的压缩性能验证。 worst 档：VTR cross-suite recovery 衰减，且 VTR 训练在非 Object suite 上有不稳定性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"vtr_m32_object_sr_pct\": 60.1,\n      \"vtr_m32_spatial_sr_pct\": 53.2,\n      \"vtr_m32_goal_sr_pct\": 56.4,\n      \"vtr_m32_long_sr_pct_predicted\": 48.0,\n      \"smolvla_baseline_object_sr_pct\": 59.2,\n      \"smolvla_baseline_spatial_sr_pct\": 44.6,\n      \"smolvla_baseline_goal_sr_pct\": 60.8,\n      \"smolvla_baseline_long_sr_pct\": 36.6,\n      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_object\": 1.015,\n      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial\": 1.193,\n      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_goal\": 0.928,\n      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_long_predicted\": 0.874,\n      \"vtr_recovery_ratio_mean\": 0.95,\n      \"vtr_m96_dip_p_value\": 0.034,\n      \"vtr_m96_dip_confirmed\": true,\n      \"hard_pruning_k05_all_suites_sr_pct\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table F: VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery (SmolVLA)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Suite\",\n          \"Hard Prune k=0.5(%)\",\n          \"VTR M=32(%)\",\n          \"Baseline(%)\",\n          \"Recovery Ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Object\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"60.1\",\n            \"59.2\",\n            \"1.015\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"0.6\",\n            \"53.2\",\n            \"44.6\",\n            \"1.193\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"56.4\",\n            \"60.8\",\n            \"0.928\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Long (pred)\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"~48\",\n            \"36.6\",\n            \"~0.87\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Recovery ratio 从 Object(1.0) 下降到 Long(0.87)。VTR 在 complex tasks 上 recovery 衰减 ~13%。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"VTR 从 \\\"universal compression method\\\" 降级为 \\\"effective recovery tool for pixel-shuffle connectors, with decreasing efficacy on complex tasks\\\"。 M=96 dip 的 statistical significance (p=0.034) 不足以证明 systematic failure（n=3 power ~0.2），但足以引起 reviewer 对 training stability 的质疑。 Cross-suite recovery 衰减是合理的：VTR 在 Object suite 上训练，cross-suite 是 zero-shot transfer。Long-horizon tasks 的 action sequence 依赖 precise temporal-spatial correspondence，VTR 的 cross-attention bottleneck 可能丢失这些 long-range dependencies。 Paper 策略：VTR 作为 §4.7 的 case study 保留，但移除 \\\"universal compression\\\" 措辞，改为 \\\"recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge to near-baseline on trained distribution, with ~13% degradation on out-of-distribution complex tasks\\\"。\\n\\n\\nVTR M=32 在 Object 上实现 near-lossless compression（60.1% vs baseline 59.2%），Spatial 上甚至超过 baseline（53.2% vs 44.6%，可能因为 VTR 训练 regularization 效应）。 但 Goal suite recovery ratio = 56.4/60.8 = 0.928，低于 Object。预测 Long-horizon（未测）recovery ratio 进一步下降至 ~0.87：Long tasks 需要 multi-step reasoning，VTR 的 cross-attention 可能无法完全保留 temporal action sequence 所需的 spatial information chain。 M=96 dip（p=0.034 vs M=64）在 worst 档被确认为 training instability（非 statistical fluke），因为 M=96 的 3-seed std=3.2pp 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 VTR 的 flat M-curve 可能是 M=16-64 的幸运区间，M=96 暴露了 cross-attention query 数量与 pixel-shuffle token structure 之间的 resonance 问题。 VTR 仍然是 valid contribution（从 0% hard pruning 恢复到 ~baseline），但 worst 档将其定位为 \\\"SmolVLA-specific case study\\\" 而非 \\\"general method\\\"，因为： (1) cross-suite recovery 有衰减（Goal 0.93, Long predicted 0.87）， (2) M=96 dip 暗示 training sensitivity， (3) OpenVLA VTR 完全失败（下条）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"VTR Universality Test: OpenVLA MLP Projector (M=128/32/64)\",\n    \"description\": \"VTR 在 OpenVLA（MLP projector）上的泛化性测试。M=128 full VTR 已失败（0% SR），VTC-only M=32/M=64 作为 fallback。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_vtr_m128_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m32_sr_pct_predicted\": 3.0,\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m64_sr_pct_predicted\": 5.0,\n      \"openvla_vtconly_m96_sr_pct_predicted\": 2.0,\n      \"openvla_baseline_sr_pct\": 74.0,\n      \"overfitting_confirmed\": true,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"model outputs identical action every timestep\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table G: VTR on OpenVLA — Universal Failure\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"M\",\n          \"Params(M)\",\n          \"Steps\",\n          \"Train Loss\",\n          \"SR(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Full VTR\",\n            \"128\",\n            \"22.2\",\n            \"20K\",\n            \"converged\",\n            \"0.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VTC-only\",\n            \"32\",\n            \"22.2\",\n            \"100K\",\n            \"converged\",\n            \"~3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VTC-only\",\n            \"64\",\n            \"22.2\",\n            \"100K\",\n            \"converged\",\n            \"~5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VTC-only\",\n            \"96\",\n            \"22.2\",\n            \"100K\",\n            \"converged\",\n            \"~2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LoRA baseline\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"883\",\n            \"100K\",\n            \"0.065\",\n            \"0.0\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"所有 VTR configs 失败。Train loss 收敛但 SR ≈0。Failure mode: identical action output。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"VTR universality 完全失败。这不是 hyperparameter tuning 问题——M=128/96/64/32 全部 <5% SR，且 LoRA fine-tuning 也产生 0% SR（libero_lora_baseline），说明 OpenVLA 的 fine-tuning 本身就 fragile。 Reviewer 会问：\\\"如果 VTR 只在 SmolVLA 上 work，它是在修复 pixel-shuffle entanglement 还是只是在 SmolVLA 的特定 action space 上 overfit？\\\" Response 策略：M=128 passthrough control（58.0% ≈ baseline 59.2%）证明 VTR 确实在学 re-encoding 而非 action space memorization。但这个 argument 仅对 SmolVLA 成立。\\n\\n\\nM=128 VTR 在 20K steps 后 0% SR（model 对所有 observation 输出相同 action）确认 severe overfitting。 VTC-only M=32/M=64 预测同样失败（<5% SR），因为根本原因不在 VTR architecture 而在 MLP projector tokens 的特性： (1) MLP projector tokens 已经是 individually meaningful 的（CV=0.215, 有 gradient differentiation），VTR 的 cross-attention 无法提供额外信息，反而引入 information bottleneck。 (2) OpenVLA 的 256 tokens × 7B parameters 的 scale 与 SmolVLA 的 128 tokens × 450M parameters 完全不同——VTR 的 ~22M params 对 7B model 来说是 rounding error，无法学到有意义的 re-encoding。 (3) M=96/M=64/M=32 的 training loss 持续下降但 eval SR 不恢复，典型的 action space overfitting pattern。 在 worst 档，这确认 VTR 是 pixel-shuffle-specific method。Paper 中 VTR 需要 reframe：不是 \\\"universal compression tool\\\" 而是 \\\"architecture-specific recovery mechanism that works because pixel-shuffle tokens need re-entangling, while MLP tokens are already independent and don't benefit from cross-attention re-encoding\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA 上的 VTC cross-attention compressor M-sweep。所有 M 值预期失败。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_vtc_m32_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n      \"openvla_vtc_m64_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n      \"openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss\": 2.45,\n      \"openvla_vtc_m96_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n      \"all_m_values_fail\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"确认 VTR/VTC 在 MLP projector + discrete action space 的组合下无效。 Paper 中作为 negative result 报告：VTR effectiveness = f(connector_type)，strengthens architecture-dependency narrative。\\n\\n\\nM=96 已训完（final train loss 2.45, eval loss 2.66），远高于 SmolVLA VTR 的 ~0.05 train loss。这不是欠拟合——100K steps with OpenVLA 的 tokenized action space 天然产生高 cross-entropy loss。 M=32/M=64 的 v3/v4/v5 版本反复失败（disk full, GPU crash, training instability），即使成功训完也预期 0% SR。 根本原因：OpenVLA 使用 discrete tokenized actions（不是 continuous actions），VTC 的 cross-attention 将 256 个 vision tokens 压缩到 M 个 queries，但 OpenVLA 的 LLM decoder 期望完整的 256-token vision context 来做 autoregressive action token generation。压缩后的 M queries 无法提供 decoder 所需的 token-level spatial precision。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"X-VLA Cliff Threshold Localization (k=0.80/0.85, 3-seed)\",\n    \"description\": \"X-VLA 在 k=0.80 和 k=0.85 的 3-seed 精确定位 cliff。Non-monotonic pattern 已确认。 worst 档：cliff 是真实的，但 E5 attention pruning 证明它是 L2norm-specific artifact。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_mean\": 89.0,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k080_sr_3seed_std\": 0.72,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_mean\": 67.9,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_k085_sr_3seed_std\": 0.31,\n      \"xvla_l2norm_nonmonotonic_gap_pp\": 21.1,\n      \"xvla_random_k085_sr_mean\": 63.6,\n      \"xvla_random_k080_sr_mean\": 89.4,\n      \"xvla_e5_attn_k05_sr_mean\": 98.4,\n      \"cliff_is_l2norm_specific\": true,\n      \"cliff_is_method_independent\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table H: X-VLA Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"k\",\n          \"L2norm SR(%)\",\n          \"L2norm SD(pp)\",\n          \"Random SR(%)\",\n          \"Attn-Last SR(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            \"97.6\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"97.8\",\n            \"~99\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.85\",\n            \"67.9\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"63.6\",\n            \"~97\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            \"89.0\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"89.4\",\n            \"~99\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.70\",\n            \"56.2\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"65.2\",\n            \"99.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.50\",\n            \"42.6\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"70.6\",\n            \"99.2\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Attention pruning 完全消除 cliff 和 degradation。问题在 metric 不在 architecture。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cliff localization 数据本身是 solid experimental result。但在 worst 档，E5 data 完全改变其解读： cliff 不是 connector architecture 的 intrinsic property，而是 L2norm importance metric 在 low-CV distribution 上的 pathological behavior。 Attention pruning（zero additional training）消除所有 degradation，这意味着 BART encoder 并没有 \\\"entangle\\\" tokens in a way that prevents pruning，它只是让 tokens 的 L2-norm 不再是 good importance proxy。 Paper 需要重新定义 Axis-1：从 \\\"token coupling\\\" 改为 \\\"importance metric suitability\\\"，或者承认 2-axis framework 是 L2norm-specific observation 而非 architecture-level insight。\\n\\n\\nX-VLA k=0.85 L2norm = 67.9%±0.31pp（3-seed，SD<1pp 确认完全 deterministic）。k=0.80 = 89.0%±0.72pp。 Non-monotonic gap = 21.1pp（k=0.85 < k=0.80），2-token 差异产生 21pp SR change。Random pruning 在同区间也出现 cliff（63.6% vs 89.4%），但 per-task crash pattern 不同（T4, T6 both crash across methods → architectural bottleneck）。 在 worst 档，这个 cliff 的意义被 E5 attention pruning 完全重新诠释： - L2norm k=0.5 = 42.6% → attn_last k=0.5 = 99.2%（+56.6pp） - 同样的 50 tokens，同样的 k=0.5（保留 25 tokens），attention 几乎完美而 L2norm catastrophic - 因此 cliff 不是 \\\"BART encoder entanglement creates irreversible token dependencies\\\"，而是 \\\"L2norm 在 BART encoder 的 near-uniform norm distribution 上退化为 spatially clustered selection\\\" - Reviewer argument：\\\"如果换 importance metric 就消除了 cliff，那 Axis-1 的 'token coupling' 定义有根本缺陷——关键不在 coupling 而在 importance metric。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OFT CV Diagnostic (Token Importance Measurement)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA-OFT 的 token importance CV 测量。Expected CV≈0.219（≈Standard OpenVLA）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"oft_cv\": 0.219,\n      \"oft_cv_std\": 0.012,\n      \"oft_entropy\": 0.667,\n      \"openvla_standard_cv\": 0.215,\n      \"cv_delta_pp\": 0.4,\n      \"sr_eval_blocked\": true,\n      \"gpu_incompatibility\": \"Blackwell SDPA requires A100+torch2.2\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table I: Diagnostic Metrics — 6-Model Spectrum\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Connector\",\n          \"CV\",\n          \"Entropy\",\n          \"Eval SR Available?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"π0\",\n            \"Pure linear\",\n            \"0.038\",\n            \"0.959\",\n            \"Offline only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"π0.5\",\n            \"Pure linear (×√d)\",\n            \"0.055\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Yes (4 suites)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"X-VLA\",\n            \"Linear + BART 12L\",\n            \"0.151\",\n            \"0.614\",\n            \"Yes (4 suites)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"3-layer MLP\",\n            \"0.215\",\n            \"0.661\",\n            \"Yes (Object only)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OFT\",\n            \"3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP)\",\n            \"0.219\",\n            \"0.667\",\n            \"No (GPU blocked)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SmolVLA\",\n            \"Pixel-shuffle\",\n            \"0.314\",\n            \"0.952\",\n            \"Yes (4 suites)\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"6 models 有 CV，但仅 3 models 有 full cross-suite SR。OFT 和 π0 只有 diagnostic metrics。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OFT CV 完成了 6-model diagnostic table，但不改变任何结论。在 worst 档，这是 incrementally supportive 而非 decisive evidence。\\n\\n\\nOFT CV=0.219 ≈ Standard OpenVLA CV=0.215（Δ=0.004），确认 connector（3-layer MLP）而非 action head（OFT vs standard）决定 token importance distribution。 Entropy 也几乎相同（0.667 vs 0.661）。这是 framework 的 positive confirmation——same connector → same CV → same predicted pruning behavior。 但在 worst 档，这个 data point 的价值有限： (1) 无法在 LIBERO 上 eval SR（Blackwell GPU SDPA 不兼容），所以 CV 预测没有 ground truth 验证 (2) OFT 和 Standard OpenVLA 用相同 connector 产生相同 CV 是 trivially expected，不提供 additional discrimination power (3) Reviewer 会指出：\\\"你们有 6 个 model 的 CV，但只有 4 个能实际 eval SR。CV 作为 predictor 的 validation set 太小。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OFT Full Graded-Class Evaluation (4 Suites)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA-OFT 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 上的 baseline + pruning evaluation。 worst 档：GPU 不兼容问题持续，无法完成 evaluation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"eval_blocked\": true,\n      \"blocker\": \"Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility with OpenVLA-OFT\",\n      \"workaround_attempted\": \"A100 rental, torch2.2 downgrade — both failed\",\n      \"fallback_evidence\": \"CV=0.219≈OpenVLA, entropy=0.667≈0.661 — inferred graded behavior\",\n      \"paper_impact\": \"Missing 2nd graded-class SR data point, relies on CV inference\",\n      \"reviewer_risk\": \"Moderate — 2/3 connector classes have ≥2 SR-evaluated models, MLP class has only 1\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Missing OFT SR data 在 worst 档是 acknowledged limitation。Reviewer concern 等级 \\\"moderate\\\"——不会 reject paper，但会要求 camera-ready 补充或更 cautious language about MLP class generalization。\\n\\n\\nOFT evaluation 在 worst 档仍然被 GPU 不兼容阻塞。Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA implementation 与 OFT checkpoint 的 torch 版本不兼容，降级 torch 或租用 A100 都不可行（timeline 限制）。 Paper 只能用 CV/entropy comparison 间接 argue OFT follows OpenVLA pattern。Reviewer 会注意到 MLP projector class 只有 OpenVLA 1 个 model 有 SR data，不足以 generalize。 CogACT（literature baseline, MLP projector, 74.8%→74.2% under 78% pruning from EfficientVLA）可以作为 external evidence，但不是 our own evaluation。 In worst tier, this is a clear gap but not fatal — pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA, 1 model, universal 0%) and linear (π0/π0.5, 2 models, variable) are well-characterized. MLP class has 1 internal + 1 external data point.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Perceiver Resampler (RoboFlamingo) — 3rd Connector Family\",\n    \"description\": \"RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) 在 LIBERO 上 fine-tune + pruning。 worst 档：fine-tuning 产生低 baseline，且 Perceiver 不清晰地落入 2-axis taxonomy。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fine_tuning_baseline_sr_pct_predicted\": 18.0,\n      \"fine_tuning_difficulty\": \"high — requires custom training pipeline adaptation\",\n      \"perceiver_cv_predicted\": 0.28,\n      \"perceiver_pruning_k09_predicted_sr_pct\": 4.0,\n      \"perceiver_pruning_k05_predicted_sr_pct\": 0.0,\n      \"taxonomy_fit\": \"ambiguous — cross-attention creates partial entanglement different from both pixel-shuffle and BART\",\n      \"paper_inclusion\": \"dropped — insufficient time and unclear taxonomy value\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dropping RoboFlamingo 在 worst 档是 rational choice：paper 已经有足够的 models（5 models × 4 suites）作为 empirical contribution，加入一个 low-baseline 的新 connector 只会模糊 narrative。 但这意味着 paper 的 connector 覆盖限于 linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle 三类，reviewer 可能指出 \\\"what about attention-based connectors (Perceiver, Q-Former)?\\\" 作为 limitation。\\n\\n\\nRoboFlamingo 在 worst 档面临多重困难： (1) Fine-tuning infrastructure：RoboFlamingo 使用 Flamingo-style cross-attention perceiver resampler，将 variable-length vision tokens 压缩到 fixed 64 queries。这需要 custom training pipeline，previous attempts (train_c5_roboflamingo_v2) 被 killed。 (2) Low baseline：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 在 LIBERO manipulation tasks 上可能不如 direct projection（SmolVLA 59.2%, OpenVLA 74%），因为 LIBERO 需要 precise spatial information 而 perceiver 天然是 lossy compression。预测 baseline ~18% SR。 (3) Taxonomy ambiguity：Perceiver Resampler 的 cross-attention 与 BART encoder 的 self-attention 和 pixel-shuffle 的 spatial folding 都不同。它是 \\\"learned entanglement\\\" 而非 \\\"structural entanglement\\\"。CV 可能在 0.2-0.3 range，不清晰地落入现有 taxonomy。 (4) Timeline：距 abstract deadline 1 天，paper deadline 4 天，没有时间 debug fine-tuning pipeline + run full evaluation。 In worst tier, RoboFlamingo 被 dropped from paper。这减少了 paper 的 connector family 覆盖（3→2 confirmed families），但避免了 messy data 进一步复杂化已经 fragile 的 framework。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"VTR M-Sweep Completion (SmolVLA 3-seed × 5 M-values)\",\n    \"description\": \"SmolVLA VTR M-sweep 的 3-seed 完成和 MLP adapter control。 worst 档：数据 solid 但 M=96 dip 和 high variance 引起质疑。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"m16_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 56.9,\n      \"m16_3seed_std_pp\": 1.3,\n      \"m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 60.1,\n      \"m32_3seed_std_pp\": 1.3,\n      \"m64_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 62.0,\n      \"m64_3seed_std_pp\": 2.3,\n      \"m96_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 54.5,\n      \"m96_3seed_std_pp\": 3.2,\n      \"m128_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 58.0,\n      \"m128_3seed_std_pp\": 3.5,\n      \"mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean_sr_pct\": 63.4,\n      \"mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std_pp\": 2.6,\n      \"vtc_vs_mlp_pvalue\": 0.15,\n      \"m64_vs_m96_pvalue\": 0.034,\n      \"baseline_sr_pct\": 59.2,\n      \"m_curve_flat_within_3pp\": true,\n      \"m96_dip_significant\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table J: VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"M\",\n          \"Compression(%)\",\n          \"Mean SR(%)\",\n          \"Std(pp)\",\n          \"Individual Seeds\",\n          \"vs Baseline\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"16\",\n            \"87.5\",\n            \"56.9\",\n            \"1.3\",\n            \"55.8/58.4/56.5\",\n            \"-2.3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"32\",\n            \"75.0\",\n            \"60.1\",\n            \"1.3\",\n            \"61.6/59.2/59.6\",\n            \"+0.9pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"64\",\n            \"50.0\",\n            \"62.0\",\n            \"2.3\",\n            \"61.6/60.0/64.4\",\n            \"+2.8pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"96\",\n            \"25.0\",\n            \"54.5\",\n            \"3.2\",\n            \"52.6/58.2/52.8\",\n            \"-4.7pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"128\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"58.0\",\n            \"3.5\",\n            \"59.8/54.0/60.2\",\n            \"-1.2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MLP-32\",\n            \"75.0\",\n            \"63.4\",\n            \"2.6\",\n            \"65.2/64.6/60.4\",\n            \"+4.2pp\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"M=96 dip p=0.034。M=128 seed43=54.0 outlier。Flat M-curve 成立但 variance 在高 M 处增大。\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"VTR 在 worst 档仍是 paper 的 positive contribution：hard pruning 0% → VTR ~59% ≈ baseline 是 dramatic recovery。 但 M=96 dip 和 high-M variance 需要 honest reporting。建议 paper 用 M=32 或 M=64 作为 recommended setting（stable seeds, good compression ratio），将 M=96 dip 作为 \\\"open question: why does M=96 underperform?\\\" 放入 discussion。 Reviewer concern level: low-moderate. VTR 的 core claim（recovery from 0% to baseline）is robust. M=96 是 interesting anomaly 但不 undermine main contribution。\\n\\n\\nVTR M-sweep 数据 intrinsically solid：M=16(56.9%) 到 M=128(58.0%) 都在 baseline 59.2% 的 ±5pp 内，证明 near-lossless compression at any ratio。MLP adapter control（63.4%）与 VTC（60.1%）无显著差异（p=0.15），确认 architecture independence。 但 worst 档关注两个 weakness： (1) M=96 dip（54.5%, p=0.034 vs M=64=62.0%）虽然在 Bonferroni correction 后 marginally significant，但 3.2pp std 是所有 M 值中最高的。这暗示 training instability——某些 seed/M 组合在 training dynamics 中进入 suboptimal basin。 (2) M=128 passthrough 的 3.5pp std 也高，且 seed43=54.0% 是 outlier（其他两个 seed 59.8/60.2%）。如果 passthrough control 本身有 6pp variance，\\\"near-lossless\\\" 的声称需要 caveat。 In worst tier, VTR 仍然是 valid method（0%→~59% recovery），但 training stability concern 使其从 \\\"recommended practice\\\" 降级为 \\\"promising but needs further investigation\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Consolidated Cross-Suite Framework Accuracy Assessment\",\n    \"description\": \"综合所有 cross-suite 数据的 framework 准确率评估。 worst 档：framework accuracy ~62%，不足以支撑 \\\"principled framework\\\" 定位。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"framework_predictions_total\": 20,\n      \"framework_predictions_correct\": 12,\n      \"framework_accuracy_pct\": 62,\n      \"claims_surviving_review\": 2.5,\n      \"surviving_claims\": \"C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement), C4 (VTR case study), partial C3b (MLP graded)\",\n      \"failed_claims\": \"C1 (2-axis framework as principled theory), C5 (CV universal predictor)\",\n      \"reframed_claims\": \"C1→empirical observation catalog, C5→within-suite heuristic\",\n      \"paper_contribution_type\": \"empirical study with surprising findings\",\n      \"corl_submission_viable\": true,\n      \"corl_acceptance_probability_pct\": 45\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table K: Framework Prediction Accuracy by Model\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Connector Class\",\n          \"Framework Prediction\",\n          \"Object\",\n          \"Spatial\",\n          \"Goal\",\n          \"Long\",\n          \"Accuracy\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SmolVLA\",\n            \"Pixel-shuffle\",\n            \"Catastrophic all suites\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"4/4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"X-VLA\",\n            \"BART encoder\",\n            \"Task-dependent collapse\",\n            \"✗(no collapse)\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"3/4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"π0.5\",\n            \"Linear proj\",\n            \"Immune to task complexity\",\n            \"✗(random cliff)\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"✗\",\n            \"1/4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"MLP\",\n            \"Graded, L2norm preferred\",\n            \"✓\",\n            \"~\",\n            \"✗(random preferred)\",\n            \"~\",\n            \"2/4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"π0\",\n            \"Linear proj\",\n            \"Immune\",\n            \"✓(offline)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"1/1\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"Total 11/17 ≈ 65%。π0.5 是 framework 最大 failure point。\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table L: Claim Survival Assessment\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Claim\",\n          \"Original Status\",\n          \"Worst-Tier Status\",\n          \"Surviving Evidence\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"C1: 2-Axis Framework\",\n            \"Primary contribution\",\n            \"Fails as theory\",\n            \"Descriptive taxonomy for L2norm-Object only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C2: Pixel-Shuffle Entanglement\",\n            \"Strong\",\n            \"Survives\",\n            \"Universal 0% across 4 suites × 2 methods\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C3: Connector-Specific Patterns\",\n            \"Strong\",\n            \"Partial survival\",\n            \"MLP graded confirmed; linear 'immune' falsified\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C4: VTR Recovery\",\n            \"Strong\",\n            \"Survives as case study\",\n            \"0%→59% on SmolVLA; fails on OpenVLA\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C5: CV Scaling Law\",\n            \"Novel contribution\",\n            \"Fails as universal\",\n            \"Within-Object heuristic only; cross-suite |ρ|≈0.45\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"2-3 claims survive review intact. Paper viable as empirical study, not as theory paper.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在 worst 档，paper 的 identity 发生根本转变： FROM: \\\"We discover a principled 2-axis framework governing VLA token compressibility\\\" TO: \\\"We provide the first systematic study of token pruning across VLA architectures, revealing that pruning behavior is an irreducible function of (connector, method, k, task), not reducible to simple architectural rules\\\"\\nKey novel findings that survive independently of the framework: (1) Pixel-shuffle entanglement is real and irreversible — this is a genuine architectural insight (2) Importance metric selection matters more than connector architecture — supported by E5 attention data + π0.5 method divergence (3) L2norm is actively harmful on low-CV models — 36pp gap on π0.5, 28pp on X-VLA at k=0.5 Object (4) VTR achieves near-lossless compression for pixel-shuffle — 0%→59% at any M ratio\\nThese 4 findings are individually publishable observations that together constitute a substantial empirical contribution for CoRL, even without a unified theory. Title: \\\"A Systematic Study of Token Pruning Strategies Across VLA Architectures.\\\"\\n\\nFramework accuracy 计算方法： - SmolVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"catastrophic at k=0.95\\\" → 实际 all suites ≤0.1% → 4/4 correct - X-VLA × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"entangling, task-dependent collapse\\\" → Object OK (97.6%), Goal 70.2% (partial collapse), Spatial 78.8% (moderate), Long 27.5% (collapse) → 3/4 correct（Object 不 collapse，与预测不符） - π0.5 × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"independent, immune to task complexity\\\" → Object random k=0.9=9%（NOT immune!），但 L2norm=98.2% → method-dependent → 1/4 correct（框架不区分 method） - OpenVLA × 4 suites: 预测 \\\"graded, L2norm preferred\\\" → Object L2norm>random (+1.8pp ✓), Goal random>L2norm (+8.8pp ✗) → 2/4 correct - π0 × offline: 预测 \\\"immune\\\" → k=0.1 improves → 1/1 correct Total: 4+3+1+2+1 = 11/17 = 65%（≈62% with margin of error）\\nClaims survival analysis: - C1 (2-axis framework): FAILS as theory → survives as \\\"descriptive taxonomy for L2norm pruning on Object suite\\\" - C2 (pixel-shuffle entanglement): SURVIVES — universal 0% across all suites/methods/k is unambiguous - C3a (linear proj depends on pipeline): Partially survives — π0 immune, π0.5 method-dependent, X-VLA cliff - C3b (MLP graded): Survives on Object — graded curve confirmed - C4 (VTR): Survives as SmolVLA case study — 0%→59% recovery - C5 (CV predicts strategy): FAILS as universal law → survives as \\\"within-Object-suite heuristic\\\"\\n2.5 claims survive: C2, C4, half of C3b.\\nCoRL viability: paper 作为 \\\"comprehensive empirical study\\\" 仍然 viable（5 models × 4 suites × 3 methods 是任何 VLA pruning 工作中最大规模的 comparison）。Acceptance probability ~45%——足够好的 empirical contribution 但缺少 unified theory 会让某些 reviewers 觉得 \\\"incremental\\\"。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":855,"startLine":1,"totalLines":855}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L5jHh1xd5v4hyd93h3RCyj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — importance_margin_vla_compress\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: **CoRL 2026** (Austin, Nov 9-12; abstract May 26, paper May 29)\n5\t- Timeline: 4 days to abstract, 7 days to paper (as of 2026-05-22)\n6\t\n7\t## Title (working)\n8\t\"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\t\n12\t**⚠️ D171 (2026-05-22): Restructured from 4-class taxonomy to 2-axis framework.** Cross-suite data broke the original per-model classification — X-VLA \"threshold-graded\" on Object becomes catastrophic on Goal (-27.8pp at k=0.9) and Long (-45pp at k=0.95). The same connector produces drastically different pruning outcomes depending on task complexity. Pruning sensitivity is the product of two independent axes:\n13\t\n14\t**Axis 1 — Token Coupling (connector architecture):**\n15\t| Type | Connectors | CV Range | Mechanism |\n16\t|------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n17\t| **Token-independent** | Pure linear (π0, π0.5), MLP (OpenVLA, OFT) | 0.038–0.219 | Tokens retain individual spatial meaning; pruning damage is local |\n18\t| **Token-entangling** | BART post-proc (X-VLA), Pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA) | 0.151–0.314 | Cross-token dependencies; pruning damage cascades |\n19\t\n20\t**Axis 2 — Task Complexity:**\n21\t| Level | Suites | Characteristics |\n22\t|-------|--------|----------------|\n23\t| **Simple** | Object, Spatial | Single-step, pruning impact contained |\n24\t| **Complex** | Goal, Long | Multi-step reasoning, token loss cascades through action sequence |\n25\t\n26\t**Key interaction (D169):** Token-entangling connectors are dramatically more sensitive to task complexity:\n27\t- X-VLA Object k=0.9: 97.6% → X-VLA Goal k=0.9: 70.2% (-27.8pp, same model/method/k, only task differs)\n28\t- X-VLA Long k=0.95: ~53% (-45pp from baseline) — removing 3 of 50 tokens collapses performance\n29\t- SmolVLA: 0% on Object already → floor effect, task complexity cannot worsen\n30\t- Token-independent (π0.5 Goal/Long): data collecting, expected smaller amplification\n31\t\n32\t**CV remains the primary Axis-1 diagnostic** — predicts both pruning tolerance and optimal strategy (Claim 5). Task complexity (Axis 2) explains within-model variance across suites that the old taxonomy could not capture.\n33\t\n34\t_Original per-connector evidence (from Object-suite 4-class taxonomy) retained below; reinterpret through 2-axis lens:_\n35\t- **Linear projection** (π0 3.3B, π0.5 4B): **\"Uniformly Critical\" (D139)**. NOT immune. π0.5 baseline=98.2%, random k=0.5=**69.4%** (-28.8pp), L2norm k=0.5=**33.4%** (-64.8pp). Gap=+36.0pp, random wins 9/10 tasks. Low CV (0.038/0.055) = uniformly important tokens → L2norm's systematic bias selects spatially clustered tokens → catastrophic at k≤0.7. Random preserves spatial coverage → 2× better at k=0.5. **L2norm extended curve:** k=0.1=2.6% (collapse) → k=0.3=51.0% → k=0.5=33.4% (valley) → k=0.7=55.0% → k=0.9=98.2%. V-shape with collapse at extreme compression. CV=0.055 makes this the extreme case of the scaling law. **⚠️ MAJOR FINDING (2026-05-22, fully investigated):** π0.5 random pruning exhibits sharp cliff at k=0.85-0.925 with non-monotonic recovery:\n36\t  - k=0.95: 71.1% FINAL (seed42 500ep; seed43=72.8%) — already 27pp below baseline\n37\t  - k=0.925: **27.6%** FINAL (seed42) — cliff entry point, 43pp drop from k=0.95\n38\t  - k=0.9: 10.8%±1.2pp (dual seed: seed42=12.0%, seed43=9.6%) — **87.4pp gap vs L2norm k=0.9=98.2%**\n39\t  - k=0.85: **5.0%** FINAL (seed42 v2=4.4%) — cliff floor\n40\t  - k=0.7: 75.5% (mean), k=0.5: 68.9%, k=0.3: 36.4% — recovery zone\n41\t  - Cliff profile: 71.1%(k=0.95) → 27.6%(k=0.925) → 10.8%(k=0.9) → 5.0%(k=0.85) — 66pp collapse over 10% keep ratio change\n42\t  **D151 (2026-05-22): Cliff is RANDOM-SPECIFIC.** L2norm maintains 98.0-99.2% plateau across the entire cliff zone:\n43\t  - L2norm k=0.95=98.2%, k=0.925=99.2%, k=0.9=98.2%, k=0.85=98.0% — zero degradation\n44\t  - Random k=0.925: 27.6% vs L2norm=99.2% → **71.6pp gap** (maximum separation)\n45\t  - Random k=0.85: 5.0% vs L2norm=98.0% → **93.0pp gap**\n46\t  - L2norm succeeds because deterministic selection consistently retains the same token subset; random sampling creates variable damage\n47\t  **D152 (2026-05-22): Cliff is TASK-SPECIFIC.** Object tasks collapse catastrophically, Spatial tasks degrade but survive:\n48\t  - Random k=0.9: Object=10.8% vs Spatial=54.6% — Spatial retains 5× more SR\n49\t  - Random k=0.85: Object=5.0% vs Spatial=TBD (collecting)\n50\t  - Within Object suite: all 10 tasks collapse at k=0.9 (2-16%). Within Spatial suite: degradation but not catastrophic.\n51\t  - Mechanism: Object tasks require precise object identity discrimination (visually similar objects); Spatial tasks rely on spatial layout (more distributed visual information). Random token loss destroys fine-grained discriminative features needed for Object before destroying spatial layout features.\n52\t  **Fixed-mask experiment (D149) NEGATES temporal inconsistency hypothesis:** per-episode fixed mask T0=12% = per-call random T0=12%. Temporal mask variation is NOT the cause.\n53\t  **D153: Cross-suite LIBERO-Spatial — weaker non-monotonicity, no catastrophic dip (2026-05-22)**\n54\t  Baseline: 97.2%. Random pruning profile:\n55\t  | k | Object | Spatial | Δ | Pattern |\n56\t  |---|--------|---------|---|---------|\n57\t  | 0.95 | 71.1% | deploying | — | — |\n58\t  | 0.925 | 28.8% (2-seed) | — | — | — |\n59\t  | 0.9 | 10.8% | 54.6% | +43.8pp | Spatial 5× more robust |\n60\t  | 0.85 | 5.0% | **58.4%** | **+53pp** | Maximum divergence |\n61\t  | 0.7 | 75.5% | 74.4% | -1pp | Suite-independent |\n62\t  | 0.5 | 69.4% | 71.6% | +2pp | Suite-independent |\n63\t  | 0.3 | 36.4% | 49.6% | +13pp | Spatial more robust |\n64\t  L2norm Spatial: k=0.9=95.0%, k=0.7=67.0%, k=0.5=55.6%, k=0.3=57.2%. L2norm k=0.95/k=0.85 deploying.\n65\t  **Object has deep V-shape dip**: 5%(k=0.85) → 10.8%(k=0.9) → 75.5%(k=0.7), 70pp recovery from cliff floor. **Spatial has weaker non-monotonicity**: k=0.5(71.6%) > k=0.85(58.4%) > k=0.9(54.6%), but no catastrophic collapse — floor stays above 50% vs Object's 5% floor. The cliff zone gap (Object 5% vs Spatial 58%) reflects concentrated vs distributed critical token patterns.\n66\t  **Mechanism**: Object tasks have **concentrated** critical tokens (object identity discrimination — visually similar objects). Random removal at cliff zone destroys these concentrated patches → catastrophic. Spatial tasks have **distributed** critical information (layout patches spread across image). Random removal damages any random subset but never completely destroys spatial signal → graceful degradation.\n67\t  **Paper value**: Two distinct cliff behavior modes — **concentrated-critical (Object)** vs **distributed-critical (Spatial)** — as a function of task semantics. Pruning sensitivity = f(connector, method, k, task_semantics). Suite-independent at moderate k (0.5-0.7), suite-dependent at cliff zone (0.85-0.95).\n68\t  **Paper value:** strengthens \"uniformly critical\" class — even uniform importance distribution doesn't make pruning safe. Simple deletion fails; learned compression (VTR) needed.\n69\t- **Linear projection + deep post-processing** (X-VLA 880M, linear proj + 12-layer BART encoder): robust k≥0.9 (97.6% SR), **cliff at k=0.7 (56.2% SR, -43pp)**. BART encoder introduces non-linear mixing that creates partial token dependencies. CV=0.151. **D127: random pruning k=0.9=97.8% ≈ L2norm 97.6% — pruning method independence confirmed for low-CV connectors.**\n70\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA 7B, OpenVLA-OFT 7B): graded degradation. k=0.1 normalized loss = 1.608 (+61%). Non-linear mixing creates partial dependencies. OFT entropy (0.667) ≈ Standard (0.661), CV(OFT)=0.219 ≈ CV(OpenVLA)=0.215, confirming connector — not action head — determines attention structure. **D136: OFT LIBERO eval infeasible (Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility, requires A100+torch2.2). OFT included via CV/entropy analysis only; cite official baseline ~97% SR.** π0.5 baseline confirmed 98.2% (D135).\n71\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA 450M): catastrophic cliff-edge. k=0.95 (removing 5%) → 0% SR. Spatial folding creates irreversible entanglement. **D147: Official HF checkpoint (HuggingFaceVLA/smolvla_libero) confirms identical cliff — random k=0.95 = 0%, L2norm k=0.95 = 0%. Cliff is architectural, not training artifact. Resolves W-C2.** **Dual-seed confirmed (2026-05-22):** Baseline 59.4%±0.3pp (seed42=59.2%, seed43=59.6%), random k=0.95: 0.1% mean (0.0%/0.2%), random k=0.5: 0.0%, L2norm k=0.95: 0.2% mean (0.4%/0.0%). All pruning ≤0.2% across both seeds. cqa1 supplementary: L2norm k=0.7=0%, random k=0.9=0%.\n72\t\n73\tKey controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) — same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. k=0.1: π0 improves 2.4% vs OpenVLA degrades 61%. This isolates connector as the causal factor.\n74\t\n75\tLearned re-encoding (VTR) overcomes the cliff-edge: cross-attention 60.1±1.3% and MLP adapter 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (vs 0% hard pruning), with M=128 passthrough (58.0%±3.5, 3-seed) ≈ baseline 59.2% — VTR recovers to baseline rather than exceeding it. SmolVLA M-curve confirmed flat (D105): M=16 (56.9%±1.3) = M=128 (58.0%±3.5), all 5 M-values within ±3pp of baseline 59.2%. VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio (0-87.5%) for pixel-shuffle connectors.\n76\t\n77\t## Paper Identity (Round 5 Upgrade — D171 2-Axis, 2026-05-22)\n78\t**ANALYSIS + METHOD paper.** (D091 → D097 → D171: 5 models × 3 connector families × 4 LIBERO suites)\n79\t\n80\t**Analysis contribution (primary)**: First systematic study revealing that VLA token pruning robustness is determined by the interaction of two axes: (1) connector architecture (token-independent vs token-entangling, diagnosed by importance CV 0.038→0.314) and (2) task complexity (simple vs multi-step). Token-entangling connectors (BART encoder, pixel-shuffle) show dramatically amplified sensitivity under complex tasks — X-VLA drops 27.8pp on Goal vs 1.6pp on Object at the same keep ratio. 5 models × 4 suites × 4 model sizes (450M-7B) eliminate confounds. No competing work does cross-architecture, cross-task VLA token analysis.\n81\t\n82\t**Method contribution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework:\n83\t- Step 1: **Connector Compressibility Diagnostic** (D104: resolved)\n84\t  - **Primary metric: Importance CV** (token importance heterogeneity) — zero-cost, one forward pass\n85\t  - CV forms continuous spectrum predicting pruning tolerance: π0=0.038 < π0.5=0.055 < X-VLA=0.151 < OpenVLA=0.215 < OFT=0.219 < SmolVLA=0.314\n86\t  - ⚠️ D106+: X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate pruning behavior (k=0.7 ≈50% SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7). CV is a valid continuous predictor, NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n87\t  - **Key discovery**: X-VLA \"linear projection\" passes through BART encoder (12 transformer layers) before decoder → introduces non-linear mixing → explains CV=0.151 (much higher than π0=0.038 pure linear)\n88\t  - **Entropy as mechanistic supplement** (CV is primary; entropy is supplementary):\n89\t    - π0: entropy=0.959 (per-layer mean, range 0.931–0.983), CV=0.038 — uniform & independent → most tolerant\n90\t    - **π0.5: entropy=0.666, CV=0.055** — similar entropy to OpenVLA (0.661) but vastly different pruning behavior (CV correctly differentiates)\n91\t    - X-VLA: entropy=0.614, CV=0.151 — selective & BART-mixed → intermediate\n92\t    - OpenVLA: entropy=0.661, CV=0.215 — selective & MLP-mixed → graded\n93\t    - SmolVLA: entropy=0.952, CV=0.314 — near-uniform but spatially entangled → catastrophic\n94\t  - **KEY INSIGHT**: Entropy clusters π0.5/X-VLA/OpenVLA together (0.61-0.67) despite very different pruning behaviors. CV correctly separates them (0.055 vs 0.151 vs 0.215). Entropy fails as diagnostic because it doesn't capture token independence structure — only attention distribution shape.\n95\t  - ✅ Batch 2 complete: continuous CV spectrum confirmed (X-VLA full 8-point curve validates threshold-graded class)\n96\t  - Supplementary: lightweight pruning probe (remove 5%, one forward pass) as practitioner-friendly alternative\n97\t- Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) — lightweight cross-attention module (~22M params) for universal compression\n98\t- For entangled tokens (pixel-shuffle): recovers from 0% (hard pruning) to ~59% ≈ baseline, M-curve flat D105 (near-lossless compression at any ratio 0-87.5%)\n99\t- For independent tokens (MLP projector): **D109 C4-ext confirmed 0% SR** at 20K steps (M=128, severe overfitting — model outputs identical action every step). VTR on MLP projector does NOT improve SR; reframed as \"VTR ceiling depends on connector type\" finding. User directive: performance degradation acceptable if efficiency improves — VTR value is 75% KV-cache reduction + attention speedup. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress to test whether smaller M values fare better.\n100\t\n101\t**Differentiation from concurrent work**: 4 concurrent works (Compressor-VLA, SpecPrune-VLA, LightVLA ICRA'26, See What Matters ICML'26) all propose pruning on MLP-projector VLAs. We (1) explain why pruning fails on pixel-shuffle architectures, (2) identify why pruning succeeds on linear projection (tokens are truly independent), and (3) propose a re-encoding method motivated by the diagnostic analysis.\n102\t\n103\t**Model coverage**: 5 VLA models × 3 connector families × 4 LIBERO suites × 4 model sizes (450M-7B). RC1 (only 2 models), RC2 (size confound), and RC7 (only one suite) fully addressed.\n104\t\n105\t## Core Claims (5 claims, expanded from 4)\n106\t\n107\t### Claim 1: 2-Axis Compressibility Framework (D107 → D171 UPGRADED)\n108\tPruning sensitivity = f(connector_architecture, task_complexity). Two axes interact:\n109\t\n110\t**Axis 1 — Token Coupling (connector determines base sensitivity):**\n111\t- **Token-independent** connectors (pure linear π0/π0.5, MLP OpenVLA/OFT): tokens retain spatial meaning → pruning damage is local, graded degradation\n112\t- **Token-entangling** connectors (BART X-VLA, pixel-shuffle SmolVLA): cross-token dependencies → pruning damage cascades\n113\t\n114\t**Axis 2 — Task Complexity (task amplifies entangling-connector sensitivity):**\n115\t- Simple tasks (Object): even entangling connectors tolerate mild pruning (X-VLA k=0.9=97.6%)\n116\t- Complex tasks (Goal/Long): entangling connectors collapse (X-VLA Goal k=0.9=70.2%, Long k=0.95≈53%)\n117\t- Key: same connector, same k, same method — **only task differs** → 27.8pp drop (Object→Goal)\n118\t\n119\t**CV predicts Axis-1 position**: 0.038 (most independent) → 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.219 → 0.314 (most entangled)\n120\t\n121\t**Evidence**: 5 models, 3 connector families, 4 LIBERO suites, 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Key controlled comparisons:\n122\t1. π0 (256 tokens, linear) k=0.1 = 0.976 vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, MLP) k=0.1 = 1.608 → connector isolates base sensitivity\n123\t2. X-VLA Object k=0.9 = 97.6% vs X-VLA Goal k=0.9 = 70.2% → task complexity isolates amplification\n124\t3. SmolVLA Object = 0% at k=0.95 → extreme entanglement dominates even on simple tasks\n125\t\n126\t🔴 **D108→D127→D130→D132: Pruning method comparison — MAJOR REVERSAL at aggressive compression**\n127\t\n128\tBoth L2 norm and random pruning tested on X-VLA and OpenVLA. **CV predicts not just tolerance but optimal strategy**:\n129\t\n130\t- **OpenVLA (MLP, CV=0.215)**: L2 norm consistently ≥ random at all k values. High CV → meaningful importance differentiation → L2 norm selection effective.\n131\t  - k=0.95: L2norm=69.4% ≈ random=69.2% (+0.2pp)\n132\t  - k=0.7: L2norm=49.8%¹ > random=44.4% (+5.4pp). ¹seed43 only, seed42 running on westd-38929:2\n133\t  - k=0.5: L2norm=39.2% > random=35.8% (+3.4pp)\n134\t  - k=0.3: L2norm=25.0%, random=pending (re-running)\n135\t\n136\t- **X-VLA (BART, CV=0.151)**: 🔴 **REVERSAL** — L2 norm ≈ random at mild compression, but **random MASSIVELY outperforms L2 norm at aggressive compression**:\n137\t  - k=0.9: L2norm=97.6% ≈ random=97.8% (≈0pp)\n138\t  - k=0.85: L2norm=68.0% > random=63.6% (+4.4pp, cliff boundary)\n139\t  - k=0.8: L2norm=89.0% ≈ random=89.4% (≈0pp, non-monotonic recovery)\n140\t  - **k=0.5: L2norm=42.6% << random=70.6% (-28.0pp!)** — CI non-overlapping, statistically significant. Random wins 9/10 tasks; T4 ketchup: L2norm=42% vs random=100% (+58pp). Only T6 butter both crash at 2%.\n141\t  - k=0.7: L2norm=56.2% << random=65.2% (+9pp). Crossover confirmed at k≈0.8.\n142\t  - **k=0.3: L2norm=22.8% << random=62.8% (+40pp!)** — gap scales monotonically with compression.\n143\t  - **D137**: seed43 k=0.5=71.0% confirms seed42=70.6% (Δ=0.4pp). Gap reproducible.\n144\t\n145\t- **SmolVLA**: all methods = 0% at all k values → trivially method independent.\n146\t\n147\t**KEY INSIGHT (D132→D137)**: Importance-based pruning can be **actively harmful** on low-CV architectures under aggressive compression, and the harm SCALES: +9pp@k=0.7, +28pp@k=0.5, +40pp@k=0.3. Mechanism: X-VLA's linear projection + BART encoder produces relatively uniform token norms (CV=0.151). L2 norm selection on a near-uniform distribution degenerates into selecting spatially clustered tokens → loses diversity → catastrophic failure. Random pruning preserves spatial coverage → dramatically better. Multi-seed confirmed.\n148\t\n149\t**This strengthens the paper**: CV serves as a dual predictor — predicts both (1) pruning tolerance ceiling and (2) whether importance-based methods help or hurt. Connector architecture determines both via its effect on token importance distribution.\n150\t\n151\t**Paper narrative upgrade**: From \"connector determines compressibility\" to \"connector determines both compressibility AND optimal compression strategy.\" This is a significantly stronger and more novel contribution.\n152\t\n153\t**Pending data**: X-VLA random k=0.7 (crossover characterization), multi-seed k=0.5 random (robustness). OpenVLA L2norm k_ratio=null provenance issue needs fixing.\n154\t\n155\t### Claim 2: Pixel Shuffle Creates Irreversible Token Entanglement\n156\tSmolVLA's pixel_shuffle connector spatially folds 1024 SigLIP patches into 64 tokens per camera (16x compression). Each resulting token encodes a 32x32 pixel region via channel-to-spatial reorganization. This creates extreme cross-token spatial entanglement: removing any single token eliminates an entire spatial quadrant's information with no redundancy to compensate.\n157\t\n158\t**Evidence**:\n159\t- k=0.95 (remove only 7/128 tokens = 5.5%) = 0% SR — even minimal removal is catastrophic\n160\t- k=0.9 (remove 13/128 tokens) = 0% SR\n161\t- Geometric prior (Sobel edge) k=0.5/0.7/0.9 = all 0%\n162\t- Attention entropy ratio 0.952 (near-uniform, TV=0.05)\n163\t- Official checkpoint Object (59.2% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0%\n164\t- Official checkpoint Spatial (43.8% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%])\n165\t\n166\t### Claim 3a: Linear Projection → Depends on Effective Pipeline (D107: RESOLVED)\n167\tPure linear projection (π0): immune. Linear projection + deep post-processing (X-VLA, BART 12L): \"robust-then-cliff\" — immune at k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation. The BART encoder introduces non-linear cross-token mixing that explains intermediate CV=0.151 and the cliff pattern.\n168\t\n169\t**Evidence** (X-VLA LIBERO SR — Batch 1 + Batch 2 COMPLETE, full 8-point curve):\n170\t- k=1.0: **99.2%** (baseline, 496/500) — per-task: [98, 100, 98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n171\t- k=0.95: **99.0%** (-0.2pp) — per-task: [98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n172\t- k=0.9: **97.6%** (-1.6pp) — per-task: [96, 98, 100, 92, 100, 96, 100, 98, 96, 100]\n173\t- k=0.7: **56.2%** (-43pp, CLIFF — 281/500) — per-task: [94, 2, 100, 80, 28, 92, 12, 66, 0, 88]\n174\t- k=0.5: **42.6%** (-57pp) — Batch 2 confirmed (MSH fix applied)\n175\t- k=0.3: **23.0%** (-77pp) — graded degradation continues below cliff\n176\t- k=0.2: **~4.0%** (-96pp) — near-zero\n177\t- k=0.1: **~0.0%** (-100pp) — complete failure\n178\t✅ Full curve confirms threshold-graded pattern: immune k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%).\n179\t\n180\t**Cliff localization (D114, D117: 3-seed deterministic, L2norm)**:\n181\t- k=0.80: **89.0% ± 0.72pp** (seeds: 88.8/88.4/89.8)\n182\t- k=0.85: **67.9% ± 0.31pp** (seeds: 68.0/67.6/68.2 — T4=26%, T6=0% across ALL 3 seeds)\n183\t- Non-monotonic: k=0.85 < k=0.80 by **21.1pp**. BART encoder creates length-dependent interactions near critical token density. SD < 1pp confirms fully deterministic, not stochastic.\n184\t\n185\t**Random pruning comparison (D127-D130, D132 REVERSAL)**:\n186\t- k=0.9: random=97.8% ≈ L2norm=97.6% → method independent at mild compression\n187\t- k=0.85: random=63.6% vs L2norm=68.0% (+4.4pp for L2norm at cliff boundary). Both crash on same tasks (T1, T4, T6, T8) → cliff is architectural.\n188\t- k=0.8: random=89.4% ≈ L2norm=89.0% → method independent, non-monotonic recovery confirmed in both\n189\t- 🔴 **k=0.5: random=70.6% >> L2norm=42.6% (+28pp REVERSAL, CI non-overlapping)**. Per-task random: [96, 46, 100, 92, 100, 94, 2, 82, 42, 100]. Random wins 9/10 tasks; L2norm actively harmful. T4: random=100% vs L2norm=42% (+58pp).\n190\t- k=0.7: random=65.2% vs L2norm=56.2% (+9pp random). Crossover confirmed at k≈0.8.\n191\t- 🔴 **k=0.3: random=62.8% vs L2norm=22.8% (+40pp!)** — gap SCALES with compression: +9@k=0.7, +28@k=0.5, +40@k=0.3.\n192\t- **D137 multi-seed confirmed**: seed43 k=0.5=71.0% (seed42=70.6%, Δ=0.4pp). Gap is reproducible.\n193\t- **Random non-monotonicity confirmed**: k=0.5 (70.6%) > k=0.7 (65.2%) > k=0.3 (62.8%). seed43 reproduces (71.0%). L2norm monotonically decreasing (42.6% > 22.8%). Random's k=0.5 \"sweet spot\" may reflect optimal diversity-coverage tradeoff: enough tokens removed to break BART clustering, but enough retained for spatial coverage.\n194\t- k=0.85 per-task (random): [100, 10, 100, 94, 24, 92, 0, 94, 22, 100] = 63.6%.\n195\t- **Non-monotonicity confirmed in both methods**: k=0.85 (42 tokens) cliff vs k=0.8 (40 tokens) recovery. 2-token difference, 21-26pp gap.\n196\t- **D132 KEY INSIGHT**: At aggressive compression (k=0.5), L2 norm is catastrophically worse than random for X-VLA. Low CV=0.151 → near-uniform importance → L2 norm degenerates into spatially clustered selection → loses diversity. This is the opposite of OpenVLA (CV=0.215) where L2 norm helps. **CV predicts optimal pruning strategy, not just tolerance.**\n197\t\n198\t**Cross-suite generalization (D117, updated with full results)**:\n199\t- X-VLA Spatial baseline: **91.6%** [88.8%, 93.7%] (500 eps, T5=48% is hardest task)\n200\t- X-VLA Goal baseline: **98.0%** [96.4%, 98.9%] (500 eps, all tasks ≥92%)\n201\t- X-VLA-Libero checkpoint covers all 4 suites without suite-specific fine-tuning.\n202\t\n203\t**⚠️ Cross-suite pruning sensitivity (key finding — potential new contribution)**:\n204\t\n205\tX-VLA pruning curve comparison across suites:\n206\t\n207\t| Suite | k=1.0 | k=0.9 | k=0.85 (L2/Rand) | k=0.8 (L2/Rand) | k=0.7 (L2/Rand) | k=0.5 (L2/Rand) |\n208\t|-------|-------|-------|-----|-------|----------|----------|\n209\t| Object | 99.2% | 97.8% | 68.0/63.6% | 89.0/89.4% | 56.2/65.2% | 42.6/**70.6%** |\n210\t| Spatial | 91.6% | 79.0% | 66.6/67.6% | — | — | 58.8%/**71.4%** |\n211\t| Goal | 98.0% | 70.2% | — | — | — | 61.0%/— |\n212\t\n213\t**Goal suite FINAL results (10/10 tasks, D123: suite-level monotonic confirmed)**:\n214\t- k=0.9: **70.2%** (351/500) — much larger drop than Object (-1.4pp) despite similar baseline\n215\t- k=0.5: **61.0%** (305/500) — suite-level monotonic (k=0.9 > k=0.5), D123 retracted earlier partial-data non-monotonic claim\n216\t\n217\t**Per-task non-monotonic pruning remains valid (selected tasks)**:\n218\t\n219\t| Task | k=1.0 | k=0.9 | k=0.5 | Pattern |\n220\t|------|-------|-------|-------|---------|\n221\t| T0 open drawer | 100% | 100% | 82% | monotonic ↓ |\n222\t| T2 close drawer | 94% | 96% | **100%** | **pruning improves** |\n223\t| T3 open+put (multi-step) | 100% | **6%** | **40%** | catastrophic + non-monotonic (k=0.5 > k=0.9) |\n224\t| T8 | — | — | — | +46pp non-monotonic (k=0.5 > k=0.9) |\n225\t| T9 | 98% | — | ~0% | catastrophic collapse (-98pp) |\n226\t\n227\t- Suite-level: Goal k=0.5=61.0% > Spatial k=0.5=58.8% — Goal slightly more robust, but both moderate degradation\n228\t- Per-task: T3/T8 show non-monotonicity (k=0.5 > k=0.9), T9 catastrophic collapse. These are genuine misalignments between global L2-norm ranking and task-specific token utility.\n229\t- T2 pruning improvement: consistent with π0 finding — simple tasks benefit from token noise removal\n230\t\n231\t**Key cross-suite finding**: Goal k=0.9 drops **27.8pp** (vs Object -1.4pp). Same connector, same pruning method, different task distribution → **task complexity amplifies pruning sensitivity**. Goal tasks involve multi-step reasoning that depends heavily on precise spatial tokens.\n232\t\n233\t**Task-level analysis (Spatial, k=0.5 vs baseline)**:\n234\t- Robust (Δ≤10pp): T0 \"between plate and ramekin\" (-4pp), T4 \"in top drawer\" (-2pp) — global spatial / unambiguous target\n235\t- Moderate (Δ 10-30pp): T2(-10), T3(-24), T6(-22), T8(-18) — mild spatial precision needed\n236\t- Catastrophic (Δ>40pp): T5 \"on ramekin\" (-48pp, 0%), T9 \"on cabinet\" (-58pp), T7 \"on stove\" (-64pp), T1 \"next to ramekin\" (-78pp)\n237\t- **T1 has 100% baseline but 22% at k=0.5** — high baseline ≠ pruning robustness\n238\t\n239\t**Mechanism**: Goal tasks are semantically diverse (different verbs/objects) → language instruction alone disambiguates → vision tokens are redundant for task selection. Spatial tasks are semantically near-identical (all \"pick bowl...\") → disambiguation relies entirely on spatial vision tokens → pruning destroys the only discriminative signal.\n240\t\n241\t**Paper framing upgrade (Reviewer suggestion, agreed)**:\n242\t- From \"connector determines pruning tolerance\" → \"pruning sensitivity = f(connector_type, task_semantics)\"\n243\t- Connector CV predicts degradation *class* (immune/threshold/graded/catastrophic)\n244\t- Task semantic structure determines degradation *severity* within that class\n245\t- When language disambiguates: aggressive pruning is safe (Goal k=0.5 ≈ baseline)\n246\t- When spatial vision disambiguates: even conservative pruning degrades (Spatial k=0.9 -12.6pp)\n247\t- **Potential new contribution**: first task-level pruning sensitivity analysis in VLAs. §4.6 should include per-task heatmap + the language-vs-spatial disambiguation framework.\n248\t\n249\tπ0 evidence:\n250\t- π0 (3.3B, 256 tokens, pure linear proj): k=0.1 normalized_L1 = 0.976 (-2.4% = improvement), k=0.5 = 0.983\n251\t- Attention entropy: π0 suffix-to-vision mean 0.959 (near-uniform across 18 layers, range [0.931, 0.983])\n252\t- Importance CV: π0 = 0.038 (lowest in spectrum)\n253\t\n254\t**Key insight**: \"Linear projection\" is NOT sufficient for immunity. The effective pipeline matters. X-VLA's BART encoder (12 transformer layers after linear proj) introduces partial dependencies → CV=0.151 → cliff at k=0.7. π0's pure linear proj → CV=0.038 → immune even at k=0.1.\n255\t\n256\t### Claim 3b: MLP Projector → Graded Degradation\n257\tMulti-layer MLP connectors create partial token dependencies through non-linear mixing, enabling graceful but real degradation.\n258\t\n259\t**Evidence** (OpenVLA 6-point degradation curve):\n260\t- k=1.0: 74.0% (baseline)\n261\t- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n262\t- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n263\t- k=0.7: 49.0% (-34% relative)\n264\t- k=0.5: 37.4% (-49% relative)\n265\t- k=0.3: 20.6% (-72% relative)\n266\t- Entropy ratio 0.639 (progressive sharpening L0=0.98→L29=0.48, TV=0.50)\n267\t- **Method independence confirmed**: random k=0.95=69.2% ≈ L2norm k=0.95=69.4%; random k=0.5=35.8% ≈ L2norm k=0.5=37.4%. For MLP projectors, pruning method doesn't matter.\n268\t- OFT (same connector, different action head): entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → connector determines attention structure, not action head\n269\t- CogACT (MLP projector, literature): 74.8% → 74.2% under 78% pruning (EfficientVLA)\n270\t\n271\t### Claim 4: Learned Re-Encoding Achieves Near-Lossless Compression Where Deletion Fails (D072+MLP confirmed → upgraded to METHOD per D091)\n272\t**⚠️ Baseline correction (2026-05-22): SmolVLA Object baseline = 59.2% (official HF checkpoint), NOT 44.8% (old reproduced). VTR narrative reframed from \"re-encoding boost\" to \"near-lossless compression recovery\".**\n273\t\n274\tTwo independent re-encoding architectures (~22M params each) validate that **any learned re-encoding** can recover entangled pixel_shuffle tokens from 0% (hard pruning) to near-baseline levels. Cross-attention (60.1±1.3%, 3-seed) and MLP adapter (63.4±2.6%, 3-seed) both achieve this recovery, with p≈0.15 confirming no significant difference between architectures. M=128 passthrough (58.0±3.5%, 3-seed) ≈ baseline 59.2% (-1.2pp), confirming VTR recovers to baseline rather than exceeding it. **M-curve is flat**: M=16 (56.9%) through M=128 (58.0%), all within ±3pp of baseline 59.2% — VTR achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio (0-87.5%) for pixel-shuffle connectors. M=64 achieves best absolute SR at 62.0±2.3% (+2.8pp over baseline) with 50% compression. Cross-suite generalization confirmed: M=32 recovers to 53.2% on Spatial (vs 0.6% pruning cliff-edge) and 56.4% on Goal. M=96 dip statistically confirmed (p=0.034 vs M=64).\n275\t\n276\t**D109 C4-ext on OpenVLA (MLP projector)**: M=128 VTR at 20K steps = **0% SR** (severe overfitting, model outputs identical action every step). This suggests VTR's effectiveness is connector-dependent: pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→~59% ≈ baseline) because re-encoding repairs spatial entanglement, while MLP projector tokens are already individually meaningful and VTR adds unnecessary complexity. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress — if these also fail, VTR is specifically a pixel-shuffle solution, which strengthens the architecture-dependency narrative.\n277\t\n278\t**Evidence** (all confirmed):\n279\t\n280\tCross-attention re-encoding (M sweep, 3-seed where available):\n281\t| M | Compression | SR (3-seed mean±std) | Seeds | Notes |\n282\t|---|------------|-----|-----|-----|\n283\t| 16 | 87.5% | **56.9±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ ZERO loss vs M=128 |\n284\t| 32 | 75% | **60.1±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ |\n285\t| 64 | 50% | **62.0±2.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ best tradeoff |\n286\t| 96 | 25% | 54.5±3.2% | 42/43/44 | ✅ highest variance |\n287\t| 128 | 0% (passthrough) | **58.0±3.5%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ passthrough control |\n288\t\n289\tMLP adapter control (M=32, ~22.14M params, 3-seed):\n290\t| Architecture | Params | M | Mean SR (3-seed) | Std | Individual seeds |\n291\t|---|---|---|-----|-----|-----|\n292\t| Cross-attention (VTC) | 22.2M | 32 | **60.1%** | ±1.3 | 61.6 / 59.2 / 59.6 |\n293\t| **MLP adapter** | **22.14M** | **32** | **63.4%** | **±2.6** | **65.2 / 64.6 / 60.4** |\n294\t\n295\tTwo-sample t-test: t≈1.94, p≈0.15 → **no significant difference** (α=0.05). Both >> 0% (hard pruning) and ≈ 59.2% (baseline). MLP ≥ VTC in all 3 seeds but difference not statistically significant — confirms any re-encoding architecture recovers to near-baseline, not a specific mechanism. (Note: M=32 seed43 corrected from 62.4% to 59.2% per registry verification; 62.4% was M=96 seed43 CI upper bound misattributed.)\n296\t\n297\t### Claim 5: CV Predicts Optimal Pruning Strategy — Scaling Law (D132→D139→D140→D142)\n298\tToken importance CV determines **which pruning method to use**, with the L2norm-vs-random gap scaling monotonically with CV. **Validated at TWO k values (D142):**\n299\t\n300\t**k=0.5 (main table):**\n301\t| Model | CV | Tokens | L2norm k=0.5 | Random k=0.5 | Δ (R-L2) |\n302\t|-------|-----|--------|-------------|-------------|----------|\n303\t| π0.5 | 0.055 | 768 | **33.4%** | **69.4%** | **+36.0pp** |\n304\t| X-VLA | 0.151 | 50 | 43.4%³ | 70.3%⁴ | +26.9pp |\n305\t| OpenVLA | 0.215 | 256 | 39.2% | 37.4%¹⁰ | -1.8pp |\n306\t\n307\t**k=0.7 (second validation, D142):**\n308\t| Model | CV | Tokens | L2norm k=0.7 | Random k=0.7 | Δ (R-L2) |\n309\t|-------|-----|--------|-------------|-------------|----------|\n310\t| π0.5 | 0.055 | 768 | **55.0%** | **77.2%** | **+22.2pp** |\n311\t| X-VLA | 0.151 | 50 | 58.6%⁶ | 65.1%⁷ | +6.5pp |\n312\t| OpenVLA | 0.215 | 256 | 49.8% | 44.4% | -5.4pp |\n313\t⁶ X-VLA L2norm k=0.7 2-seed: 58.2/59.0, mean=58.6%, σ=0.4pp (seed44 pending → tri-seed)\n314\t⁷ X-VLA random k=0.7 2-seed: 65.2/65.0, mean=65.1%, σ=0.1pp (seed44 running)\n315\t\n316\t³ X-VLA L2norm k=0.5 3-seed mean: 42.6/43.4/44.2, mean=43.4%, range 1.6pp\n317\t⁴ X-VLA random k=0.5 3-seed mean: 70.6/71.0/69.2, mean=70.3%, σ=0.9pp\n318\t\n319\t¹⁰ OpenVLA random k=0.5 = 37.4% (seed7). Table 3 previously showed 35.8% (unverified source). seed42 running on westd-38929, will replace when available.\n320\t\n321\t✅ **D139+D142 CONFIRMED**: Scaling law validated at BOTH k=0.5 (-1.8→+26.9→+36.0) and k=0.7 (-5.4→+6.5→+22.2). Same monotonic pattern. Paper: k=0.5 as main table, k=0.7 as confirmatory second row or separate table.\n322\t\n323\t**D140: k=0.3 interaction — method preference REVERSES at extreme compression for π0.5:**\n324\t\n325\t| Model | CV | Tokens | k=0.3 kept | L2norm k=0.3 | Random k=0.3 | Δ (R-L2) |\n326\t|-------|-----|--------|-----------|-------------|-------------|----------|\n327\t| π0.5 | 0.055 | 768 | 230 | **51.0%** | 36.4% | **-14.6pp** |\n328\t| X-VLA | 0.151 | 50 | 15 | 22.2%⁸ | **64.5%⁹** | **+42.3pp** |\n329\t| OpenVLA | 0.215 | 256 | 77 | 25.0% | **21.4%** | **+3.6pp** |\n330\t\n331\t⁸ X-VLA L2norm k=0.3 3-seed: 22.2/21.0/22.8 (from D137), mean=22.0%; seed43 running on cqa1\n332\t⁹ X-VLA random k=0.3 2-seed: 62.8/66.2, mean=64.5%, σ=2.4pp; seed44 running on cqa1\n333\t\n334\tAt k=0.3, π0.5 L2norm wins (+14.6pp) while X-VLA random still wins massively (+42.3pp). OpenVLA L2norm also wins (+3.6pp). The pattern: at k=0.3, both high-CV (OpenVLA) and low-CV-with-large-budget (π0.5, 230 tokens) favor L2norm, while mid-CV-with-small-budget (X-VLA, 15 tokens) strongly favors random. Strategy preference is f(CV, k, absolute_token_budget).\n335\t\n336\t**OpenVLA (CV=0.215) full seed42 Δ(L2-R) pattern**: +1.4pp (k=0.95) → +5.4pp (k=0.7) → pending (k=0.5) → +3.6pp (k=0.3). L2norm consistently better at ALL k values — high CV enables meaningful importance-based selection. Peak advantage at k=0.7, not monotonically increasing with compression.\n337\t\n338\t**D141: π0.5 L2norm complete curve — valley at k=0.5 confirmed (multi-seed)**:\n339\t| k | L2norm SR (s42) | L2norm SR (s43) | Random SR | Δ (R-L2) s42 |\n340\t|---|-----------------|-----------------|-----------|---------------|\n341\t| 0.7 | **55.0%** | **57.8%**¹⁰ | **77.2%** / **73.8%** (mean=75.5%) | +22.2pp (s42) / +19.8pp (mean) |\n342\t| 0.5 | **33.4%** | **33.6%** ✅ | **69.4%** / **68.4%** (mean=68.9%) | +36.0pp (s42) / +35.4pp (mean) |\n343\t| 0.3 | **51.0%** | **55.4%** ✅ | 36.4% | -14.6pp |\n344\t\n345\t¹⁰ Agent audit reported 56.4% for L2norm k=0.7 seed43 vs earlier worker result 57.8%. Needs reconciliation. Pattern unchanged.\n346\t\n347\t**V-shape fully confirmed (2 seeds, both methods)**:\n348\t- **Valley (k=0.5)**: L2norm 33.4/33.6% (std=0.1pp); Random 69.4/68.4% (std=0.7pp) — both methods stable\n349\t- **2-seed means**: L2norm k=0.7=56.4%, k=0.5=33.5%, k=0.3=53.2%; Random k=0.7=75.5%, k=0.5=68.9%\n350\t- **V-depth**: seed42=17.6pp, seed43=21.8pp (seed43 deeper because endpoints higher)\n351\t- **Δ(R-L2) dual-seed means**: k=0.7=+19.8pp, k=0.5=+35.4pp — scaling law holds with multi-seed\n352\t- seed43 consistently +2-4pp above seed42 but identical shape. Valley position/depth is architectural determinism.\n353\t\n354\t**Mechanism confirmed by token position visualization (D141)**:\n355\t- k=0.7: 2 clusters, 97% in largest, **100% spatial coverage** — enough tokens to maintain coverage\n356\t- k=0.5: **1 cluster, 100% in single region, 78% coverage** — worst-case spatial concentration\n357\t- k=0.3: **3 clusters**, 86% in largest, 78% coverage — cluster breaks apart, better diversity\n358\t\n359\tThe non-monotonicity arises because k=0.5 sits at the worst point of the spatial correlation structure: L2norm selects exactly the number of tokens that maximizes spatial clustering. At k=0.7 there are enough tokens for coverage; at k=0.3 the selection threshold crosses a boundary that fragments the cluster. Per-task variance is extreme at k=0.7 (T1=94%, T5=98% vs T7=0%) — L2norm deterministic selection can catastrophically miss specific task-critical spatial regions.\n360\t\n361\t**Paper strategy**: k=0.5 as **main table** (cleanest scaling law, monotonic gap). Full L2norm curve as **figure** showing pathological valley — strong evidence for spatial clustering mechanism. k=0.3 reversal as supplementary. Key message: \"CV predicts method preference at k=0.5; L2norm's spatial clustering creates pathological non-monotonicity unique to low-CV models.\"\n362\t\n363\t**Notable asymmetry**: Random tolerance is similar for low/medium CV at k=0.5 (π0.5=69.4% ≈ X-VLA=70.6%), while L2norm harm increases dramatically (π0.5=33.4% < X-VLA=43.4%). High CV (OpenVLA=35.8% random) is less random-tolerant because tokens have genuine importance differentiation that random discards.\n364\t\n365\t**Evidence** (Reviewer-verified, D132 PASS):\n366\t\n367\tX-VLA vs OpenVLA full comparison:\n368\t\n369\t| k | X-VLA (CV=0.151) | | OpenVLA (CV=0.215) | |\n370\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n371\t| | L2norm | Random | L2norm | Random |\n372\t| 0.95 | — | — | 70.6% | 69.2% (+1.4 L2norm) |\n373\t| 0.9 | 97.6% | 97.8% (≈0) | 70.6% | 64.6% (+6.0 L2norm) |\n374\t| 0.85 | 68.0% | 63.6% (+4.4 L2norm) | — | — |\n375\t| 0.8 | 89.0% | 89.4% (≈0) | — | — |\n376\t| 0.7 | 56.2% | **65.2% (+9pp random)** | 49.8%¹ | 44.4% (+5.4 L2norm¹) |\n377\t| 0.5 | **42.6%** | **70.6% (+28pp random!)** | 39.2% | 35.8% (+3.4 L2norm) |\n378\t| 0.3 | **22.8%** | **62.8% (+40pp random!)** | 25.0% | pending² |\n379\t\n380\t¹ OpenVLA L2norm k=0.7 = seed43 only, random = seed42; cross-seed caveat. seed42 L2norm k=0.7 running on westd-38929.\n381\t² OpenVLA random k=0.3 result file missing, re-running on westd-38929.\n382\t³ D137 multi-seed: X-VLA random k=0.5 seed43=71.0% (seed42=70.6%, Δ=0.4pp). Gap reproducible.\n383\t\n384\t**Per-task X-VLA k=0.5 (Reviewer-verified, 9/10 tasks random > L2norm):**\n385\t\n386\t| Task | Baseline | L2 s42 | L2 s43 | Random s42 | Δ(R-L2) |\n387\t|------|---------|--------|--------|------------|---------|\n388\t| T0 alphabet_soup | 98% | 58% | 56% | **96%** | +38 |\n389\t| T1 cream_cheese | 100% | 2% | 6% | 46% | +44 |\n390\t| T4 ketchup | 100% | 42% | 40% | **100%** | **+58** |\n391\t| T7 milk | 100% | 38% | 38% | 82% | +44 |\n392\t| T9 orange_juice | 100% | 68% | 70% | **100%** | +32 |\n393\t| T6 butter | 100% | 2% | 2% | 2% | 0 (both crash) |\n394\t\n395\tL2norm two seeds highly consistent (s42 vs s43 diff <6pp) → not RNG noise.\n396\tT6: baseline=100% but both methods=2% → highly localized visual cue, k=0.5 always loses it regardless of method.\n397\tT4/T9: Random recovers to baseline → L2norm systematically discards the critical tokens for these tasks.\n398\t\n399\t**Pattern**: Low CV (X-VLA) → importance-based selection degenerates at aggressive k → random better. High CV (OpenVLA) → meaningful importance differentiation → L2 norm better.\n400\t\n401\t**Mechanism hypothesis** (Reviewer: consistent with data, needs direct evidence): X-VLA's linear projection + BART encoder produces tokens with relatively uniform L2 norms (CV=0.151). At aggressive compression (k=0.5 = keeping 25 of 50 tokens), L2 norm selects the \"slightly larger\" tokens which tend to be spatially clustered → loses spatial diversity → catastrophic. Random preserves spatial coverage stochastically → dramatically better.\n402\t\n403\t**⚠️ Visualization needed (Reviewer warning)**: Must produce token position visualization — for same input image, show which tokens L2 norm vs random retains. If L2 norm shows spatial clustering, mechanism is proven. This should be a key figure (§4.6 or Fig 4).\n404\t\n405\t**Implication for practitioners**: CV diagnoses → predicts tolerance → prescribes strategy at aggressive compression. Low CV + aggressive k (≤0.5) → random/position-based. High CV → importance-based at all k. Mild compression (k≥0.8) → method choice doesn't matter regardless of CV.\n406\t\n407\t**Pending**: X-VLA random k=0.7 (crossover), multi-seed k=0.5, token position visualization, OpenVLA L2norm k=0.7 seed42, k_ratio=null fix.\n408\t\n409\t## Story Spine\n410\t\n411\t**Problem**: Vision token efficiency is critical for real-time VLA deployment. Growing literature proposes inference-time token reduction (FastV, VLA-IAP, H2O, ToMe). These methods succeed on some VLAs but their behavior across different architectures is unstudied.\n412\t\n413\t**Gap**: No work has systematically compared token pruning robustness across VLA architectures. The implicit assumption that \"token pruning works or fails uniformly\" is untested. The critical architectural factor determining prunability is unknown.\n414\t\n415\t**Discovery**: We find that VLA token pruning robustness is governed by two interacting axes. **Axis 1 — Token Coupling**: connector architecture determines whether tokens are independent (linear proj, MLP) or entangled (BART encoder, pixel-shuffle), diagnosed by importance CV (0.038→0.314). **Axis 2 — Task Complexity**: multi-step tasks (Goal/Long) amplify pruning damage on entangling connectors — X-VLA drops 27.8pp on Goal vs 1.6pp on Object at k=0.9. Evidence from 5 VLA models × 4 LIBERO suites:\n416\t- **Token-independent** (π0, π0.5 linear; OpenVLA, OFT MLP): graded degradation, CV 0.038–0.219\n417\t- **Token-entangling** (X-VLA BART 12L; SmolVLA pixel-shuffle): task-dependent collapse — tolerate simple tasks, catastrophic on complex tasks. CV 0.151–0.314\n418\tCV predicts both pruning tolerance and optimal strategy (L2norm hurts low-CV models, helps high-CV).\n419\t\n420\t**Solution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework. Step 1: Token importance CV provides zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance (one forward pass). Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) provides universal compression. For pixel-shuffle: recovers from 0% (hard pruning) to ~59% ≈ baseline (59.2%), M-curve flat (D105: M=16 56.9% ≈ M=128 58.0%, near-lossless at any compression ratio). For MLP projector: D109 C4-ext = 0% SR (overfitting at M=128); VTC-only M=32/M=64 in progress.\n421\t\n422\t**Headline result**: \"Across 5 VLA models (450M-7B) × 4 task suites, we find that token pruning robustness is governed by two axes: connector architecture (token-independent vs token-entangling, diagnosed by importance CV) and task complexity. Token-entangling connectors (BART encoder, pixel-shuffle) show dramatically amplified sensitivity under complex tasks — X-VLA drops 27.8pp on Goal vs 1.6pp on Object at the same keep ratio; SmolVLA collapses to 0% at 5% removal regardless of task. CV (0.038→0.314) predicts both pruning tolerance and optimal strategy: importance-based pruning is actively harmful on low-CV architectures (+28-36pp gap favoring random), while it helps on high-CV models (+1-6pp). VTR recovers to ~59% (≈baseline) at any compression ratio (0-87.5%) where hard deletion achieves 0%.\"\n423\t\n424\t## Paper Structure (7-model version)\n425\t\n426\t1. **Introduction**: VLA efficiency motivation → diverse connector architectures → 2-axis framework discovery (D171) → Diagnose-then-Compress framework\n427\t2. **Background**: 5 VLA models, 3 connector families (linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle), 4 LIBERO suites, token flow analysis\n428\t3. **Experimental Setup**: 5 models, LIBERO benchmark (4 suites: Object/Spatial/Goal/Long), pruning protocol, VTR compression, diagnostic metrics\n429\t4. **Main Results**:\n430\t   - §4.1: 2-Axis Framework Overview (Table 1: 5 models × token coupling axis; Table 2: cross-suite interaction — connector × task complexity)\n431\t   - §4.2: Token-Entangling Catastrophic — pixel-shuffle cliff-edge (SmolVLA, all configs 0% regardless of task)\n432\t   - §4.3: Token-Independent Graded — MLP degradation (OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT entropy confirmation)\n433\t   - §4.4: Token-Independent Tolerant — linear projection (π0 + π0.5, controlled comparison with OpenVLA)\n434\t   - §4.5: Task Complexity Amplification — X-VLA cross-suite (Object 97.6% vs Goal 70.2% vs Long ~53% at same k)\n435\t   - §4.6: Pruning Strategy Depends on CV (D132: low-CV random>>L2norm, high-CV L2norm>>random)\n436\t   - §4.7: VTR overcomes cliff-edge (M-curve flat + architecture independence)\n437\t   - (REMOVED — D119: LIBERO-Plus L1 SR=3.3% floor effect, noted in Discussion §6)\n438\t5. **Analysis**:\n439\t   - §5.1: Why pixel_shuffle creates entanglement (spatial folding + controlled comparison)\n440\t   - §5.2: Diagnostic metric — Entropy + CV composite (D104, 4-model validation)\n441\t   - §5.3: Re-encoding mechanism (M=128 passthrough + MLP adapter + M-curve flat D105)\n442\t6. **Discussion**: Design implications, limitations (sim-only, no real robot), future work\n443\t7. **Conclusion**: 5 claims summary\n444\t\n445\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n446\t\n447\t### RC1: Only 2 models → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n448\t**Response**: Now 5 models (SmolVLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, π0, X-VLA) across 3 connector families (pixel-shuffle, 3-layer MLP, linear projection) and 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Each connector class has ≥2 models.\n449\t\n450\t### RC2: Model size confound (450M vs 7B) → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n451\t**Response**: π0 (3.3B, linear) is pruning-immune while OpenVLA (7B, MLP) degrades 61% at k=0.1. Larger model is MORE vulnerable, not less — directly falsifies \"larger models are more robust\" hypothesis. X-VLA (880M, linear) also immune, matching π0 behavior despite 4× smaller. Size is not the explanatory variable; connector type is.\n452\t\n453\t### RC3: Why not test SmolVLA without pixel_shuffle?\n454\t**Response**: SmolVLA's connector is integral (LLM expects 128 tokens, not 1024). Removing it requires retraining from scratch. OpenVLA comparison isolates the connector's role.\n455\t\n456\t### RC4: Smart compression — is re-encoding or compression the mechanism?\n457\t**Response (corrected with baseline=59.2%)**: VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio — the M-curve is flat (M=16: 56.9% → M=128: 58.0%, all within ±3pp of baseline 59.2%). Two lines of evidence: (1) M=128 passthrough (58.0%) ≈ baseline (59.2%) — re-encoding recovers spatial entanglement to baseline level, not above it. (2) Architecture control: MLP adapter (63.4%) ≈ cross-attention (60.1%) with CI overlap — any re-encoding mechanism works. The key contribution is recovery from 0% (hard pruning) to ~59% (baseline), not exceeding baseline. Compression ratio is a free parameter with negligible SR cost.\n458\t\n459\t### RC5: Relationship to VLA-IAP\n460\t**Response**: VLA-IAP's 97.8% on OpenVLA is consistent with our finding: MLP projector preserves token independence. VLA-IAP untested on pixel_shuffle VLAs; our geometric prior experiments (0%) predict it would fail.\n461\t\n462\t### RC6: Is this just \"different models behave differently\"?\n463\t**Response**: We identify the specific mechanism (pixel_shuffle spatial folding) and provide evidence for WHY. Concrete design implications: future VLAs wanting efficiency should avoid pixel_shuffle or include learned re-encoding modules.\n464\t\n465\t### RC7: Only one benchmark (LIBERO-Object) → **ADDRESSING (D115, D119)**\n466\t**Response**: Expanded to ALL 4 LIBERO suites (Object/Spatial/Goal/Long) — 4 genuinely different task distributions (manipulation skills, spatial reasoning, goal-conditioned, long-horizon). Taxonomy consistency validated across suites. LIBERO-Plus robustness benchmark tested (D119) but abandoned: L1 camera perturbation collapses OpenVLA to SR=3.3% (consistent with leaderboard 0.8%), creating floor effect with no room for pruning analysis. This floor effect itself is noted in Discussion as evidence of general VLA brittleness under distribution shift. Sim-only limitation acknowledged.\n467\t\n468\t## All Experimental Evidence (confirmed)\n469\t\n470\t### SmolVLA Cliff-Edge\n471\t- Fine-tuned baseline (Object): 44.8% (224/500) — ⚠️ OLD reproduced checkpoint, superseded by official HF = 59.2%\n472\t- 6 pruning conditions (random/ACIS/ToMe × k=0.5/0.7/0.9): all 0%\n473\t- Geometric prior (Sobel) k=0.5/0.7/0.9: all 0%\n474\t- Attention entropy: 0.952 (flat, TV=0.05)\n475\t- Official checkpoint Object: 59.2% → 0% at k=0.5\n476\t- Official checkpoint Spatial: 43.8% → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%]) at k=0.5 — near-zero, confirms cliff-edge across suites\n477\t- LoRA-FT checkpoint Spatial: 8.0% (per-task: [24,8,4,24,0,2,2,2,14,0]) — LoRA trained on Object only, does not transfer to Spatial. Use official checkpoint for cross-suite SmolVLA analysis.\n478\t\n479\t### OpenVLA Degradation Curve\n480\t- k=1.0: 74.0% (370/500)\n481\t- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n482\t- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n483\t- k=0.7: 49.0% (245/500, -34% relative)\n484\t- k=0.5: 37.4% (187/500, -49% relative)\n485\t- k=0.3: 20.6% (103/500, -72% relative)\n486\t- Entropy: 0.639 (progressive sharpening, TV=0.50)\n487\t\n488\t### Cross-Model Pruning Taxonomy (7 models — D100, D120, D127)\n489\t| Model | Connector | Tokens | k=0.1 norm_L1 | k=0.5 norm_L1 | Class |\n490\t|-------|-----------|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n491\t| π0 (3.3B) | Pure linear proj | 256 | 0.976 (-2.4%) | 0.983 | Immune |\n492\t| π0.5 (4B) | Pure linear proj (×√d scaling) | 768 (3×256) | **98.2%** (491/500) | **L2norm=33.4%, random=69.4%** | **Uniformly Critical (D139)**: L2norm catastrophic (-64.8pp), random tolerant (-28.8pp), gap=+36pp. CV=0.055. |\n493\t| X-VLA (880M) | Linear + BART 12L | 50 | ~1.00 | ~1.00 | Threshold-graded (k=0.7: 56.2%) |\n494\t| OpenVLA (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | 1.608 (+61%) | 1.167 (+17%) | Smooth graded |\n495\t| OFT (7B) | 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP fused) | **512** | N/A | N/A | D136: Blackwell GPU incompatible. CV=0.219≈OpenVLA → graded. Cite official ~97% baseline. |\n496\t| SmolVLA (450M) | Pixel-shuffle | 128 | — | 0% cliff | Catastrophic |\n497\t\n498\tDiagnostic metrics (D104+D106+D120: CV as continuous predictor, 7 models):\n499\t| Model | Connector (effective) | Entropy | CV | Pruning Behavior |\n500\t|-------|----------------------|---------|------|------------------|\n501\t| π0 | Pure linear proj | 0.959 | 0.038 | Immune (offline, k=0.1 improves) |\n502\t| π0.5 | Pure linear proj (×√d) | pending | 0.055 | **Uniformly Critical (D139)**: L2norm=33.4%, random=69.4%, gap=+36pp. Scaling law extreme. |\n503\t| X-VLA | Linear proj + BART enc (12L) | **0.614** | **0.151** | Threshold-graded: robust k≥0.9, cliff k=0.7 (56.2%). D127: random=L2norm at k=0.9 |\n504\t| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.661 | 0.215 | Graded (74→37.4% at k=0.5) |\n505\t| OFT | 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP, **512 tokens**) | 0.667 | 0.219 | D136: Graded expected (CV≈OpenVLA). Blackwell GPU incompatible, no LIBERO SR. |\n506\t| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle (16×) | 0.952 | **0.314** | Catastrophic (0% at k=0.95) |\n507\t\n508\tKey insights (updated with 7-model data):\n509\t1. **CV is a continuous predictor**: 0.038 → 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.219 → 0.314 maps to decreasing pruning tolerance. NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n510\t2. **X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate behavior** — closer to OpenVLA (0.215) than π0 (0.038), matching k=0.7 SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7.\n511\t3. **X-VLA entropy=0.614 ≈ OpenVLA 0.661** — both have BART/MLP non-linear mixing. X-VLA is NOT \"high entropy\" like π0.\n512\t4. **Effective connector complexity matters more than nominal label**: X-VLA is \"linear proj\" but BART encoder introduces 12 transformer layers of mixing. Paper should discuss \"effective connector\" = projection + any intermediate processing.\n513\t5. OFT entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → action head does not affect attention structure\n514\t6. Framing: CV captures \"degree of non-linear mixing in the vision-to-LLM pathway.\" More mixing → higher CV → less tolerant of pruning.\n515\t\n516\t### Smart Compress (Learned Re-encoding)\n517\tCross-attention (VTC) M sweep (3-seed where available):\n518\t- M=16: **56.9% ± 1.3pp** (3-seed: 55.8/58.4/56.5) — 87.5% compression, ZERO loss vs M=128\n519\t- M=32: 60.1±1.3% (3-seed: 61.6/59.2/59.6)\n520\t- M=64: 62.0±2.3% (3-seed: 61.6/60.0/64.4)\n521\t- M=96: 54.5±3.2% (3-seed: 52.6/58.2/52.8) — highest variance\n522\t- M=128: 58.0±3.5pp (3-seed: 59.8/54.0/60.2) — passthrough control\n523\t- **D102 CONFIRMED: M-curve is flat.** M=16 (56.9%) = M=128 (58.0%), difference < 1.1pp. VTC achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio for pixel-shuffle connector. All M values within ±5pp of baseline ~59%.\n524\t\n525\tMLP adapter (M=32, 3-seed):\n526\t- seed42: 65.2% (326/500), seed43: 64.6% (323/500), seed44: 60.4% (302/500)\n527\t- Mean: 63.4% ± 2.6 vs VTC M=32 mean 60.1% ± 1.3\n528\t- t-test p≈0.15, no significant difference — confirms architecture-independence\n529\t\n530\t### D109: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — FAILED\n531\t- C4-ext M=128 at 20K steps: **0% SR** (0/44 episodes before eval termination)\n532\t- Failure mode: model outputs identical action every timestep (severe overfitting)\n533\t- Interpretation: VTR adds unnecessary complexity for MLP projector tokens (already individually meaningful). VTR specifically solves pixel-shuffle entanglement.\n534\t- VTC-only M=32 and M=64 training in progress on westd-41074:2-3\n535\t\n536\t### Cross-Suite VTR Generalization (SmolVLA)\n537\t- M=32 Spatial: 53.2% (vs official Spatial baseline 44.6% per ROADMAP, vs pruning 0.6% — recovery from cliff-edge, +8.6pp over baseline)\n538\t- M=32 Goal: 56.4% (vs official Goal baseline 60.8% per ROADMAP, vs pruning 0% — recovery from cliff-edge, -4.4pp below baseline)\n539\t- ⚠️ Cross-suite baselines need reconciliation: paper_framing previously used 43.8%/63.0%, ROADMAP uses 44.6%/60.8%. Use n=500 official checkpoint data as ground truth.\n540\t- Note: VTR trained on Object suite, evaluated cross-suite. Official baselines from different checkpoint (official vs LoRA-FT); comparisons should emphasize recovery from 0% rather than absolute performance vs uncompressed.\n541\t\n542\t### Pairwise Statistical Tests (Welch's t-test, n=3 per condition)\n543\t- M=32 VTC vs M=32 MLP: p=0.150 (not significant) — confirms architecture-independence\n544\t- M=64 VTC vs M=96 VTC: p=0.034 (significant) — M=96 dip confirmed real\n545\t- M=32 MLP vs M=96 VTC: p=0.022 (significant) — M=96 underperforms\n546\t- M=32/M=64/M=128 VTC cluster: all pairwise p>0.25 — robust across M values\n547\t- Bonferroni note: no pair survives correction at 10 tests; n=3 limits power (~0.2 for medium effects)\n548\t\n549\t### Supplementary\n550\t- Inference latency: 6% speedup at M=32\n551\t- KV-cache: 75% memory reduction at M=32\n552\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66dfde6d-dd0a-44a8-9964-18ea8fcd5ba7","uuid":"94332317-ae61-49e0-b9a1-38a52564a43e","timestamp":"2026-05-25T05:52:50.955Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260525T050917/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — importance_margin_vla_compress\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: **CoRL 2026** (Austin, Nov 9-12; abstract May 26, paper May 29)\n- Timeline: 4 days to abstract, 7 days to paper (as of 2026-05-22)\n\n## Title (working)\n\"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n\n## Core Insight\n\n**⚠️ D171 (2026-05-22): Restructured from 4-class taxonomy to 2-axis framework.** Cross-suite data broke the original per-model classification — X-VLA \"threshold-graded\" on Object becomes catastrophic on Goal (-27.8pp at k=0.9) and Long (-45pp at k=0.95). The same connector produces drastically different pruning outcomes depending on task complexity. Pruning sensitivity is the product of two independent axes:\n\n**Axis 1 — Token Coupling (connector architecture):**\n| Type | Connectors | CV Range | Mechanism |\n|------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n| **Token-independent** | Pure linear (π0, π0.5), MLP (OpenVLA, OFT) | 0.038–0.219 | Tokens retain individual spatial meaning; pruning damage is local |\n| **Token-entangling** | BART post-proc (X-VLA), Pixel-shuffle (SmolVLA) | 0.151–0.314 | Cross-token dependencies; pruning damage cascades |\n\n**Axis 2 — Task Complexity:**\n| Level | Suites | Characteristics |\n|-------|--------|----------------|\n| **Simple** | Object, Spatial | Single-step, pruning impact contained |\n| **Complex** | Goal, Long | Multi-step reasoning, token loss cascades through action sequence |\n\n**Key interaction (D169):** Token-entangling connectors are dramatically more sensitive to task complexity:\n- X-VLA Object k=0.9: 97.6% → X-VLA Goal k=0.9: 70.2% (-27.8pp, same model/method/k, only task differs)\n- X-VLA Long k=0.95: ~53% (-45pp from baseline) — removing 3 of 50 tokens collapses performance\n- SmolVLA: 0% on Object already → floor effect, task complexity cannot worsen\n- Token-independent (π0.5 Goal/Long): data collecting, expected smaller amplification\n\n**CV remains the primary Axis-1 diagnostic** — predicts both pruning tolerance and optimal strategy (Claim 5). Task complexity (Axis 2) explains within-model variance across suites that the old taxonomy could not capture.\n\n_Original per-connector evidence (from Object-suite 4-class taxonomy) retained below; reinterpret through 2-axis lens:_\n- **Linear projection** (π0 3.3B, π0.5 4B): **\"Uniformly Critical\" (D139)**. NOT immune. π0.5 baseline=98.2%, random k=0.5=**69.4%** (-28.8pp), L2norm k=0.5=**33.4%** (-64.8pp). Gap=+36.0pp, random wins 9/10 tasks. Low CV (0.038/0.055) = uniformly important tokens → L2norm's systematic bias selects spatially clustered tokens → catastrophic at k≤0.7. Random preserves spatial coverage → 2× better at k=0.5. **L2norm extended curve:** k=0.1=2.6% (collapse) → k=0.3=51.0% → k=0.5=33.4% (valley) → k=0.7=55.0% → k=0.9=98.2%. V-shape with collapse at extreme compression. CV=0.055 makes this the extreme case of the scaling law. **⚠️ MAJOR FINDING (2026-05-22, fully investigated):** π0.5 random pruning exhibits sharp cliff at k=0.85-0.925 with non-monotonic recovery:\n  - k=0.95: 71.1% FINAL (seed42 500ep; seed43=72.8%) — already 27pp below baseline\n  - k=0.925: **27.6%** FINAL (seed42) — cliff entry point, 43pp drop from k=0.95\n  - k=0.9: 10.8%±1.2pp (dual seed: seed42=12.0%, seed43=9.6%) — **87.4pp gap vs L2norm k=0.9=98.2%**\n  - k=0.85: **5.0%** FINAL (seed42 v2=4.4%) — cliff floor\n  - k=0.7: 75.5% (mean), k=0.5: 68.9%, k=0.3: 36.4% — recovery zone\n  - Cliff profile: 71.1%(k=0.95) → 27.6%(k=0.925) → 10.8%(k=0.9) → 5.0%(k=0.85) — 66pp collapse over 10% keep ratio change\n  **D151 (2026-05-22): Cliff is RANDOM-SPECIFIC.** L2norm maintains 98.0-99.2% plateau across the entire cliff zone:\n  - L2norm k=0.95=98.2%, k=0.925=99.2%, k=0.9=98.2%, k=0.85=98.0% — zero degradation\n  - Random k=0.925: 27.6% vs L2norm=99.2% → **71.6pp gap** (maximum separation)\n  - Random k=0.85: 5.0% vs L2norm=98.0% → **93.0pp gap**\n  - L2norm succeeds because deterministic selection consistently retains the same token subset; random sampling creates variable damage\n  **D152 (2026-05-22): Cliff is TASK-SPECIFIC.** Object tasks collapse catastrophically, Spatial tasks degrade but survive:\n  - Random k=0.9: Object=10.8% vs Spatial=54.6% — Spatial retains 5× more SR\n  - Random k=0.85: Object=5.0% vs Spatial=TBD (collecting)\n  - Within Object suite: all 10 tasks collapse at k=0.9 (2-16%). Within Spatial suite: degradation but not catastrophic.\n  - Mechanism: Object tasks require precise object identity discrimination (visually similar objects); Spatial tasks rely on spatial layout (more distributed visual information). Random token loss destroys fine-grained discriminative features needed for Object before destroying spatial layout features.\n  **Fixed-mask experiment (D149) NEGATES temporal inconsistency hypothesis:** per-episode fixed mask T0=12% = per-call random T0=12%. Temporal mask variation is NOT the cause.\n  **D153: Cross-suite LIBERO-Spatial — weaker non-monotonicity, no catastrophic dip (2026-05-22)**\n  Baseline: 97.2%. Random pruning profile:\n  | k | Object | Spatial | Δ | Pattern |\n  |---|--------|---------|---|---------|\n  | 0.95 | 71.1% | deploying | — | — |\n  | 0.925 | 28.8% (2-seed) | — | — | — |\n  | 0.9 | 10.8% | 54.6% | +43.8pp | Spatial 5× more robust |\n  | 0.85 | 5.0% | **58.4%** | **+53pp** | Maximum divergence |\n  | 0.7 | 75.5% | 74.4% | -1pp | Suite-independent |\n  | 0.5 | 69.4% | 71.6% | +2pp | Suite-independent |\n  | 0.3 | 36.4% | 49.6% | +13pp | Spatial more robust |\n  L2norm Spatial: k=0.9=95.0%, k=0.7=67.0%, k=0.5=55.6%, k=0.3=57.2%. L2norm k=0.95/k=0.85 deploying.\n  **Object has deep V-shape dip**: 5%(k=0.85) → 10.8%(k=0.9) → 75.5%(k=0.7), 70pp recovery from cliff floor. **Spatial has weaker non-monotonicity**: k=0.5(71.6%) > k=0.85(58.4%) > k=0.9(54.6%), but no catastrophic collapse — floor stays above 50% vs Object's 5% floor. The cliff zone gap (Object 5% vs Spatial 58%) reflects concentrated vs distributed critical token patterns.\n  **Mechanism**: Object tasks have **concentrated** critical tokens (object identity discrimination — visually similar objects). Random removal at cliff zone destroys these concentrated patches → catastrophic. Spatial tasks have **distributed** critical information (layout patches spread across image). Random removal damages any random subset but never completely destroys spatial signal → graceful degradation.\n  **Paper value**: Two distinct cliff behavior modes — **concentrated-critical (Object)** vs **distributed-critical (Spatial)** — as a function of task semantics. Pruning sensitivity = f(connector, method, k, task_semantics). Suite-independent at moderate k (0.5-0.7), suite-dependent at cliff zone (0.85-0.95).\n  **Paper value:** strengthens \"uniformly critical\" class — even uniform importance distribution doesn't make pruning safe. Simple deletion fails; learned compression (VTR) needed.\n- **Linear projection + deep post-processing** (X-VLA 880M, linear proj + 12-layer BART encoder): robust k≥0.9 (97.6% SR), **cliff at k=0.7 (56.2% SR, -43pp)**. BART encoder introduces non-linear mixing that creates partial token dependencies. CV=0.151. **D127: random pruning k=0.9=97.8% ≈ L2norm 97.6% — pruning method independence confirmed for low-CV connectors.**\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA 7B, OpenVLA-OFT 7B): graded degradation. k=0.1 normalized loss = 1.608 (+61%). Non-linear mixing creates partial dependencies. OFT entropy (0.667) ≈ Standard (0.661), CV(OFT)=0.219 ≈ CV(OpenVLA)=0.215, confirming connector — not action head — determines attention structure. **D136: OFT LIBERO eval infeasible (Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility, requires A100+torch2.2). OFT included via CV/entropy analysis only; cite official baseline ~97% SR.** π0.5 baseline confirmed 98.2% (D135).\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA 450M): catastrophic cliff-edge. k=0.95 (removing 5%) → 0% SR. Spatial folding creates irreversible entanglement. **D147: Official HF checkpoint (HuggingFaceVLA/smolvla_libero) confirms identical cliff — random k=0.95 = 0%, L2norm k=0.95 = 0%. Cliff is architectural, not training artifact. Resolves W-C2.** **Dual-seed confirmed (2026-05-22):** Baseline 59.4%±0.3pp (seed42=59.2%, seed43=59.6%), random k=0.95: 0.1% mean (0.0%/0.2%), random k=0.5: 0.0%, L2norm k=0.95: 0.2% mean (0.4%/0.0%). All pruning ≤0.2% across both seeds. cqa1 supplementary: L2norm k=0.7=0%, random k=0.9=0%.\n\nKey controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) — same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. k=0.1: π0 improves 2.4% vs OpenVLA degrades 61%. This isolates connector as the causal factor.\n\nLearned re-encoding (VTR) overcomes the cliff-edge: cross-attention 60.1±1.3% and MLP adapter 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (vs 0% hard pruning), with M=128 passthrough (58.0%±3.5, 3-seed) ≈ baseline 59.2% — VTR recovers to baseline rather than exceeding it. SmolVLA M-curve confirmed flat (D105): M=16 (56.9%±1.3) = M=128 (58.0%±3.5), all 5 M-values within ±3pp of baseline 59.2%. VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio (0-87.5%) for pixel-shuffle connectors.\n\n## Paper Identity (Round 5 Upgrade — D171 2-Axis, 2026-05-22)\n**ANALYSIS + METHOD paper.** (D091 → D097 → D171: 5 models × 3 connector families × 4 LIBERO suites)\n\n**Analysis contribution (primary)**: First systematic study revealing that VLA token pruning robustness is determined by the interaction of two axes: (1) connector architecture (token-independent vs token-entangling, diagnosed by importance CV 0.038→0.314) and (2) task complexity (simple vs multi-step). Token-entangling connectors (BART encoder, pixel-shuffle) show dramatically amplified sensitivity under complex tasks — X-VLA drops 27.8pp on Goal vs 1.6pp on Object at the same keep ratio. 5 models × 4 suites × 4 model sizes (450M-7B) eliminate confounds. No competing work does cross-architecture, cross-task VLA token analysis.\n\n**Method contribution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework:\n- Step 1: **Connector Compressibility Diagnostic** (D104: resolved)\n  - **Primary metric: Importance CV** (token importance heterogeneity) — zero-cost, one forward pass\n  - CV forms continuous spectrum predicting pruning tolerance: π0=0.038 < π0.5=0.055 < X-VLA=0.151 < OpenVLA=0.215 < OFT=0.219 < SmolVLA=0.314\n  - ⚠️ D106+: X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate pruning behavior (k=0.7 ≈50% SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7). CV is a valid continuous predictor, NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n  - **Key discovery**: X-VLA \"linear projection\" passes through BART encoder (12 transformer layers) before decoder → introduces non-linear mixing → explains CV=0.151 (much higher than π0=0.038 pure linear)\n  - **Entropy as mechanistic supplement** (CV is primary; entropy is supplementary):\n    - π0: entropy=0.959 (per-layer mean, range 0.931–0.983), CV=0.038 — uniform & independent → most tolerant\n    - **π0.5: entropy=0.666, CV=0.055** — similar entropy to OpenVLA (0.661) but vastly different pruning behavior (CV correctly differentiates)\n    - X-VLA: entropy=0.614, CV=0.151 — selective & BART-mixed → intermediate\n    - OpenVLA: entropy=0.661, CV=0.215 — selective & MLP-mixed → graded\n    - SmolVLA: entropy=0.952, CV=0.314 — near-uniform but spatially entangled → catastrophic\n  - **KEY INSIGHT**: Entropy clusters π0.5/X-VLA/OpenVLA together (0.61-0.67) despite very different pruning behaviors. CV correctly separates them (0.055 vs 0.151 vs 0.215). Entropy fails as diagnostic because it doesn't capture token independence structure — only attention distribution shape.\n  - ✅ Batch 2 complete: continuous CV spectrum confirmed (X-VLA full 8-point curve validates threshold-graded class)\n  - Supplementary: lightweight pruning probe (remove 5%, one forward pass) as practitioner-friendly alternative\n- Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) — lightweight cross-attention module (~22M params) for universal compression\n- For entangled tokens (pixel-shuffle): recovers from 0% (hard pruning) to ~59% ≈ baseline, M-curve flat D105 (near-lossless compression at any ratio 0-87.5%)\n- For independent tokens (MLP projector): **D109 C4-ext confirmed 0% SR** at 20K steps (M=128, severe overfitting — model outputs identical action every step). VTR on MLP projector does NOT improve SR; reframed as \"VTR ceiling depends on connector type\" finding. User directive: performance degradation acceptable if efficiency improves — VTR value is 75% KV-cache reduction + attention speedup. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress to test whether smaller M values fare better.\n\n**Differentiation from concurrent work**: 4 concurrent works (Compressor-VLA, SpecPrune-VLA, LightVLA ICRA'26, See What Matters ICML'26) all propose pruning on MLP-projector VLAs. We (1) explain why pruning fails on pixel-shuffle architectures, (2) identify why pruning succeeds on linear projection (tokens are truly independent), and (3) propose a re-encoding method motivated by the diagnostic analysis.\n\n**Model coverage**: 5 VLA models × 3 connector families × 4 LIBERO suites × 4 model sizes (450M-7B). RC1 (only 2 models), RC2 (size confound), and RC7 (only one suite) fully addressed.\n\n## Core Claims (5 claims, expanded from 4)\n\n### Claim 1: 2-Axis Compressibility Framework (D107 → D171 UPGRADED)\nPruning sensitivity = f(connector_architecture, task_complexity). Two axes interact:\n\n**Axis 1 — Token Coupling (connector determines base sensitivity):**\n- **Token-independent** connectors (pure linear π0/π0.5, MLP OpenVLA/OFT): tokens retain spatial meaning → pruning damage is local, graded degradation\n- **Token-entangling** connectors (BART X-VLA, pixel-shuffle SmolVLA): cross-token dependencies → pruning damage cascades\n\n**Axis 2 — Task Complexity (task amplifies entangling-connector sensitivity):**\n- Simple tasks (Object): even entangling connectors tolerate mild pruning (X-VLA k=0.9=97.6%)\n- Complex tasks (Goal/Long): entangling connectors collapse (X-VLA Goal k=0.9=70.2%, Long k=0.95≈53%)\n- Key: same connector, same k, same method — **only task differs** → 27.8pp drop (Object→Goal)\n\n**CV predicts Axis-1 position**: 0.038 (most independent) → 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.219 → 0.314 (most entangled)\n\n**Evidence**: 5 models, 3 connector families, 4 LIBERO suites, 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Key controlled comparisons:\n1. π0 (256 tokens, linear) k=0.1 = 0.976 vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, MLP) k=0.1 = 1.608 → connector isolates base sensitivity\n2. X-VLA Object k=0.9 = 97.6% vs X-VLA Goal k=0.9 = 70.2% → task complexity isolates amplification\n3. SmolVLA Object = 0% at k=0.95 → extreme entanglement dominates even on simple tasks\n\n🔴 **D108→D127→D130→D132: Pruning method comparison — MAJOR REVERSAL at aggressive compression**\n\nBoth L2 norm and random pruning tested on X-VLA and OpenVLA. **CV predicts not just tolerance but optimal strategy**:\n\n- **OpenVLA (MLP, CV=0.215)**: L2 norm consistently ≥ random at all k values. High CV → meaningful importance differentiation → L2 norm selection effective.\n  - k=0.95: L2norm=69.4% ≈ random=69.2% (+0.2pp)\n  - k=0.7: L2norm=49.8%¹ > random=44.4% (+5.4pp). ¹seed43 only, seed42 running on westd-38929:2\n  - k=0.5: L2norm=39.2% > random=35.8% (+3.4pp)\n  - k=0.3: L2norm=25.0%, random=pending (re-running)\n\n- **X-VLA (BART, CV=0.151)**: 🔴 **REVERSAL** — L2 norm ≈ random at mild compression, but **random MASSIVELY outperforms L2 norm at aggressive compression**:\n  - k=0.9: L2norm=97.6% ≈ random=97.8% (≈0pp)\n  - k=0.85: L2norm=68.0% > random=63.6% (+4.4pp, cliff boundary)\n  - k=0.8: L2norm=89.0% ≈ random=89.4% (≈0pp, non-monotonic recovery)\n  - **k=0.5: L2norm=42.6% << random=70.6% (-28.0pp!)** — CI non-overlapping, statistically significant. Random wins 9/10 tasks; T4 ketchup: L2norm=42% vs random=100% (+58pp). Only T6 butter both crash at 2%.\n  - k=0.7: L2norm=56.2% << random=65.2% (+9pp). Crossover confirmed at k≈0.8.\n  - **k=0.3: L2norm=22.8% << random=62.8% (+40pp!)** — gap scales monotonically with compression.\n  - **D137**: seed43 k=0.5=71.0% confirms seed42=70.6% (Δ=0.4pp). Gap reproducible.\n\n- **SmolVLA**: all methods = 0% at all k values → trivially method independent.\n\n**KEY INSIGHT (D132→D137)**: Importance-based pruning can be **actively harmful** on low-CV architectures under aggressive compression, and the harm SCALES: +9pp@k=0.7, +28pp@k=0.5, +40pp@k=0.3. Mechanism: X-VLA's linear projection + BART encoder produces relatively uniform token norms (CV=0.151). L2 norm selection on a near-uniform distribution degenerates into selecting spatially clustered tokens → loses diversity → catastrophic failure. Random pruning preserves spatial coverage → dramatically better. Multi-seed confirmed.\n\n**This strengthens the paper**: CV serves as a dual predictor — predicts both (1) pruning tolerance ceiling and (2) whether importance-based methods help or hurt. Connector architecture determines both via its effect on token importance distribution.\n\n**Paper narrative upgrade**: From \"connector determines compressibility\" to \"connector determines both compressibility AND optimal compression strategy.\" This is a significantly stronger and more novel contribution.\n\n**Pending data**: X-VLA random k=0.7 (crossover characterization), multi-seed k=0.5 random (robustness). OpenVLA L2norm k_ratio=null provenance issue needs fixing.\n\n### Claim 2: Pixel Shuffle Creates Irreversible Token Entanglement\nSmolVLA's pixel_shuffle connector spatially folds 1024 SigLIP patches into 64 tokens per camera (16x compression). Each resulting token encodes a 32x32 pixel region via channel-to-spatial reorganization. This creates extreme cross-token spatial entanglement: removing any single token eliminates an entire spatial quadrant's information with no redundancy to compensate.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- k=0.95 (remove only 7/128 tokens = 5.5%) = 0% SR — even minimal removal is catastrophic\n- k=0.9 (remove 13/128 tokens) = 0% SR\n- Geometric prior (Sobel edge) k=0.5/0.7/0.9 = all 0%\n- Attention entropy ratio 0.952 (near-uniform, TV=0.05)\n- Official checkpoint Object (59.2% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0%\n- Official checkpoint Spatial (43.8% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%])\n\n### Claim 3a: Linear Projection → Depends on Effective Pipeline (D107: RESOLVED)\nPure linear projection (π0): immune. Linear projection + deep post-processing (X-VLA, BART 12L): \"robust-then-cliff\" — immune at k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation. The BART encoder introduces non-linear cross-token mixing that explains intermediate CV=0.151 and the cliff pattern.\n\n**Evidence** (X-VLA LIBERO SR — Batch 1 + Batch 2 COMPLETE, full 8-point curve):\n- k=1.0: **99.2%** (baseline, 496/500) — per-task: [98, 100, 98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n- k=0.95: **99.0%** (-0.2pp) — per-task: [98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n- k=0.9: **97.6%** (-1.6pp) — per-task: [96, 98, 100, 92, 100, 96, 100, 98, 96, 100]\n- k=0.7: **56.2%** (-43pp, CLIFF — 281/500) — per-task: [94, 2, 100, 80, 28, 92, 12, 66, 0, 88]\n- k=0.5: **42.6%** (-57pp) — Batch 2 confirmed (MSH fix applied)\n- k=0.3: **23.0%** (-77pp) — graded degradation continues below cliff\n- k=0.2: **~4.0%** (-96pp) — near-zero\n- k=0.1: **~0.0%** (-100pp) — complete failure\n✅ Full curve confirms threshold-graded pattern: immune k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%).\n\n**Cliff localization (D114, D117: 3-seed deterministic, L2norm)**:\n- k=0.80: **89.0% ± 0.72pp** (seeds: 88.8/88.4/89.8)\n- k=0.85: **67.9% ± 0.31pp** (seeds: 68.0/67.6/68.2 — T4=26%, T6=0% across ALL 3 seeds)\n- Non-monotonic: k=0.85 < k=0.80 by **21.1pp**. BART encoder creates length-dependent interactions near critical token density. SD < 1pp confirms fully deterministic, not stochastic.\n\n**Random pruning comparison (D127-D130, D132 REVERSAL)**:\n- k=0.9: random=97.8% ≈ L2norm=97.6% → method independent at mild compression\n- k=0.85: random=63.6% vs L2norm=68.0% (+4.4pp for L2norm at cliff boundary). Both crash on same tasks (T1, T4, T6, T8) → cliff is architectural.\n- k=0.8: random=89.4% ≈ L2norm=89.0% → method independent, non-monotonic recovery confirmed in both\n- 🔴 **k=0.5: random=70.6% >> L2norm=42.6% (+28pp REVERSAL, CI non-overlapping)**. Per-task random: [96, 46, 100, 92, 100, 94, 2, 82, 42, 100]. Random wins 9/10 tasks; L2norm actively harmful. T4: random=100% vs L2norm=42% (+58pp).\n- k=0.7: random=65.2% vs L2norm=56.2% (+9pp random). Crossover confirmed at k≈0.8.\n- 🔴 **k=0.3: random=62.8% vs L2norm=22.8% (+40pp!)** — gap SCALES with compression: +9@k=0.7, +28@k=0.5, +40@k=0.3.\n- **D137 multi-seed confirmed**: seed43 k=0.5=71.0% (seed42=70.6%, Δ=0.4pp). Gap is reproducible.\n- **Random non-monotonicity confirmed**: k=0.5 (70.6%) > k=0.7 (65.2%) > k=0.3 (62.8%). seed43 reproduces (71.0%). L2norm monotonically decreasing (42.6% > 22.8%). Random's k=0.5 \"sweet spot\" may reflect optimal diversity-coverage tradeoff: enough tokens removed to break BART clustering, but enough retained for spatial coverage.\n- k=0.85 per-task (random): [100, 10, 100, 94, 24, 92, 0, 94, 22, 100] = 63.6%.\n- **Non-monotonicity confirmed in both methods**: k=0.85 (42 tokens) cliff vs k=0.8 (40 tokens) recovery. 2-token difference, 21-26pp gap.\n- **D132 KEY INSIGHT**: At aggressive compression (k=0.5), L2 norm is catastrophically worse than random for X-VLA. Low CV=0.151 → near-uniform importance → L2 norm degenerates into spatially clustered selection → loses diversity. This is the opposite of OpenVLA (CV=0.215) where L2 norm helps. **CV predicts optimal pruning strategy, not just tolerance.**\n\n**Cross-suite generalization (D117, updated with full results)**:\n- X-VLA Spatial baseline: **91.6%** [88.8%, 93.7%] (500 eps, T5=48% is hardest task)\n- X-VLA Goal baseline: **98.0%** [96.4%, 98.9%] (500 eps, all tasks ≥92%)\n- X-VLA-Libero checkpoint covers all 4 suites without suite-specific fine-tuning.\n\n**⚠️ Cross-suite pruning sensitivity (key finding — potential new contribution)**:\n\nX-VLA pruning curve comparison across suites:\n\n| Suite | k=1.0 | k=0.9 | k=0.85 (L2/Rand) | k=0.8 (L2/Rand) | k=0.7 (L2/Rand) | k=0.5 (L2/Rand) |\n|-------|-------|-------|-----|-------|----------|----------|\n| Object | 99.2% | 97.8% | 68.0/63.6% | 89.0/89.4% | 56.2/65.2% | 42.6/**70.6%** |\n| Spatial | 91.6% | 79.0% | 66.6/67.6% | — | — | 58.8%/**71.4%** |\n| Goal | 98.0% | 70.2% | — | — | — | 61.0%/— |\n\n**Goal suite FINAL results (10/10 tasks, D123: suite-level monotonic confirmed)**:\n- k=0.9: **70.2%** (351/500) — much larger drop than Object (-1.4pp) despite similar baseline\n- k=0.5: **61.0%** (305/500) — suite-level monotonic (k=0.9 > k=0.5), D123 retracted earlier partial-data non-monotonic claim\n\n**Per-task non-monotonic pruning remains valid (selected tasks)**:\n\n| Task | k=1.0 | k=0.9 | k=0.5 | Pattern |\n|------|-------|-------|-------|---------|\n| T0 open drawer | 100% | 100% | 82% | monotonic ↓ |\n| T2 close drawer | 94% | 96% | **100%** | **pruning improves** |\n| T3 open+put (multi-step) | 100% | **6%** | **40%** | catastrophic + non-monotonic (k=0.5 > k=0.9) |\n| T8 | — | — | — | +46pp non-monotonic (k=0.5 > k=0.9) |\n| T9 | 98% | — | ~0% | catastrophic collapse (-98pp) |\n\n- Suite-level: Goal k=0.5=61.0% > Spatial k=0.5=58.8% — Goal slightly more robust, but both moderate degradation\n- Per-task: T3/T8 show non-monotonicity (k=0.5 > k=0.9), T9 catastrophic collapse. These are genuine misalignments between global L2-norm ranking and task-specific token utility.\n- T2 pruning improvement: consistent with π0 finding — simple tasks benefit from token noise removal\n\n**Key cross-suite finding**: Goal k=0.9 drops **27.8pp** (vs Object -1.4pp). Same connector, same pruning method, different task distribution → **task complexity amplifies pruning sensitivity**. Goal tasks involve multi-step reasoning that depends heavily on precise spatial tokens.\n\n**Task-level analysis (Spatial, k=0.5 vs baseline)**:\n- Robust (Δ≤10pp): T0 \"between plate and ramekin\" (-4pp), T4 \"in top drawer\" (-2pp) — global spatial / unambiguous target\n- Moderate (Δ 10-30pp): T2(-10), T3(-24), T6(-22), T8(-18) — mild spatial precision needed\n- Catastrophic (Δ>40pp): T5 \"on ramekin\" (-48pp, 0%), T9 \"on cabinet\" (-58pp), T7 \"on stove\" (-64pp), T1 \"next to ramekin\" (-78pp)\n- **T1 has 100% baseline but 22% at k=0.5** — high baseline ≠ pruning robustness\n\n**Mechanism**: Goal tasks are semantically diverse (different verbs/objects) → language instruction alone disambiguates → vision tokens are redundant for task selection. Spatial tasks are semantically near-identical (all \"pick bowl...\") → disambiguation relies entirely on spatial vision tokens → pruning destroys the only discriminative signal.\n\n**Paper framing upgrade (Reviewer suggestion, agreed)**:\n- From \"connector determines pruning tolerance\" → \"pruning sensitivity = f(connector_type, task_semantics)\"\n- Connector CV predicts degradation *class* (immune/threshold/graded/catastrophic)\n- Task semantic structure determines degradation *severity* within that class\n- When language disambiguates: aggressive pruning is safe (Goal k=0.5 ≈ baseline)\n- When spatial vision disambiguates: even conservative pruning degrades (Spatial k=0.9 -12.6pp)\n- **Potential new contribution**: first task-level pruning sensitivity analysis in VLAs. §4.6 should include per-task heatmap + the language-vs-spatial disambiguation framework.\n\nπ0 evidence:\n- π0 (3.3B, 256 tokens, pure linear proj): k=0.1 normalized_L1 = 0.976 (-2.4% = improvement), k=0.5 = 0.983\n- Attention entropy: π0 suffix-to-vision mean 0.959 (near-uniform across 18 layers, range [0.931, 0.983])\n- Importance CV: π0 = 0.038 (lowest in spectrum)\n\n**Key insight**: \"Linear projection\" is NOT sufficient for immunity. The effective pipeline matters. X-VLA's BART encoder (12 transformer layers after linear proj) introduces partial dependencies → CV=0.151 → cliff at k=0.7. π0's pure linear proj → CV=0.038 → immune even at k=0.1.\n\n### Claim 3b: MLP Projector → Graded Degradation\nMulti-layer MLP connectors create partial token dependencies through non-linear mixing, enabling graceful but real degradation.\n\n**Evidence** (OpenVLA 6-point degradation curve):\n- k=1.0: 74.0% (baseline)\n- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n- k=0.7: 49.0% (-34% relative)\n- k=0.5: 37.4% (-49% relative)\n- k=0.3: 20.6% (-72% relative)\n- Entropy ratio 0.639 (progressive sharpening L0=0.98→L29=0.48, TV=0.50)\n- **Method independence confirmed**: random k=0.95=69.2% ≈ L2norm k=0.95=69.4%; random k=0.5=35.8% ≈ L2norm k=0.5=37.4%. For MLP projectors, pruning method doesn't matter.\n- OFT (same connector, different action head): entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → connector determines attention structure, not action head\n- CogACT (MLP projector, literature): 74.8% → 74.2% under 78% pruning (EfficientVLA)\n\n### Claim 4: Learned Re-Encoding Achieves Near-Lossless Compression Where Deletion Fails (D072+MLP confirmed → upgraded to METHOD per D091)\n**⚠️ Baseline correction (2026-05-22): SmolVLA Object baseline = 59.2% (official HF checkpoint), NOT 44.8% (old reproduced). VTR narrative reframed from \"re-encoding boost\" to \"near-lossless compression recovery\".**\n\nTwo independent re-encoding architectures (~22M params each) validate that **any learned re-encoding** can recover entangled pixel_shuffle tokens from 0% (hard pruning) to near-baseline levels. Cross-attention (60.1±1.3%, 3-seed) and MLP adapter (63.4±2.6%, 3-seed) both achieve this recovery, with p≈0.15 confirming no significant difference between architectures. M=128 passthrough (58.0±3.5%, 3-seed) ≈ baseline 59.2% (-1.2pp), confirming VTR recovers to baseline rather than exceeding it. **M-curve is flat**: M=16 (56.9%) through M=128 (58.0%), all within ±3pp of baseline 59.2% — VTR achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio (0-87.5%) for pixel-shuffle connectors. M=64 achieves best absolute SR at 62.0±2.3% (+2.8pp over baseline) with 50% compression. Cross-suite generalization confirmed: M=32 recovers to 53.2% on Spatial (vs 0.6% pruning cliff-edge) and 56.4% on Goal. M=96 dip statistically confirmed (p=0.034 vs M=64).\n\n**D109 C4-ext on OpenVLA (MLP projector)**: M=128 VTR at 20K steps = **0% SR** (severe overfitting, model outputs identical action every step). This suggests VTR's effectiveness is connector-dependent: pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→~59% ≈ baseline) because re-encoding repairs spatial entanglement, while MLP projector tokens are already individually meaningful and VTR adds unnecessary complexity. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress — if these also fail, VTR is specifically a pixel-shuffle solution, which strengthens the architecture-dependency narrative.\n\n**Evidence** (all confirmed):\n\nCross-attention re-encoding (M sweep, 3-seed where available):\n| M | Compression | SR (3-seed mean±std) | Seeds | Notes |\n|---|------------|-----|-----|-----|\n| 16 | 87.5% | **56.9±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ ZERO loss vs M=128 |\n| 32 | 75% | **60.1±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ |\n| 64 | 50% | **62.0±2.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ best tradeoff |\n| 96 | 25% | 54.5±3.2% | 42/43/44 | ✅ highest variance |\n| 128 | 0% (passthrough) | **58.0±3.5%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ passthrough control |\n\nMLP adapter control (M=32, ~22.14M params, 3-seed):\n| Architecture | Params | M | Mean SR (3-seed) | Std | Individual seeds |\n|---|---|---|-----|-----|-----|\n| Cross-attention (VTC) | 22.2M | 32 | **60.1%** | ±1.3 | 61.6 / 59.2 / 59.6 |\n| **MLP adapter** | **22.14M** | **32** | **63.4%** | **±2.6** | **65.2 / 64.6 / 60.4** |\n\nTwo-sample t-test: t≈1.94, p≈0.15 → **no significant difference** (α=0.05). Both >> 0% (hard pruning) and ≈ 59.2% (baseline). MLP ≥ VTC in all 3 seeds but difference not statistically significant — confirms any re-encoding architecture recovers to near-baseline, not a specific mechanism. (Note: M=32 seed43 corrected from 62.4% to 59.2% per registry verification; 62.4% was M=96 seed43 CI upper bound misattributed.)\n\n### Claim 5: CV Predicts Optimal Pruning Strategy — Scaling Law (D132→D139→D140→D142)\nToken importance CV determines **which pruning method to use**, with the L2norm-vs-random gap scaling monotonically with CV. **Validated at TWO k values (D142):**\n\n**k=0.5 (main table):**\n| Model | CV | Tokens | L2norm k=0.5 | Random k=0.5 | Δ (R-L2) |\n|-------|-----|--------|-------------|-------------|----------|\n| π0.5 | 0.055 | 768 | **33.4%** | **69.4%** | **+36.0pp** |\n| X-VLA | 0.151 | 50 | 43.4%³ | 70.3%⁴ | +26.9pp |\n| OpenVLA | 0.215 | 256 | 39.2% | 37.4%¹⁰ | -1.8pp |\n\n**k=0.7 (second validation, D142):**\n| Model | CV | Tokens | L2norm k=0.7 | Random k=0.7 | Δ (R-L2) |\n|-------|-----|--------|-------------|-------------|----------|\n| π0.5 | 0.055 | 768 | **55.0%** | **77.2%** | **+22.2pp** |\n| X-VLA | 0.151 | 50 | 58.6%⁶ | 65.1%⁷ | +6.5pp |\n| OpenVLA | 0.215 | 256 | 49.8% | 44.4% | -5.4pp |\n⁶ X-VLA L2norm k=0.7 2-seed: 58.2/59.0, mean=58.6%, σ=0.4pp (seed44 pending → tri-seed)\n⁷ X-VLA random k=0.7 2-seed: 65.2/65.0, mean=65.1%, σ=0.1pp (seed44 running)\n\n³ X-VLA L2norm k=0.5 3-seed mean: 42.6/43.4/44.2, mean=43.4%, range 1.6pp\n⁴ X-VLA random k=0.5 3-seed mean: 70.6/71.0/69.2, mean=70.3%, σ=0.9pp\n\n¹⁰ OpenVLA random k=0.5 = 37.4% (seed7). Table 3 previously showed 35.8% (unverified source). seed42 running on westd-38929, will replace when available.\n\n✅ **D139+D142 CONFIRMED**: Scaling law validated at BOTH k=0.5 (-1.8→+26.9→+36.0) and k=0.7 (-5.4→+6.5→+22.2). Same monotonic pattern. Paper: k=0.5 as main table, k=0.7 as confirmatory second row or separate table.\n\n**D140: k=0.3 interaction — method preference REVERSES at extreme compression for π0.5:**\n\n| Model | CV | Tokens | k=0.3 kept | L2norm k=0.3 | Random k=0.3 | Δ (R-L2) |\n|-------|-----|--------|-----------|-------------|-------------|----------|\n| π0.5 | 0.055 | 768 | 230 | **51.0%** | 36.4% | **-14.6pp** |\n| X-VLA | 0.151 | 50 | 15 | 22.2%⁸ | **64.5%⁹** | **+42.3pp** |\n| OpenVLA | 0.215 | 256 | 77 | 25.0% | **21.4%** | **+3.6pp** |\n\n⁸ X-VLA L2norm k=0.3 3-seed: 22.2/21.0/22.8 (from D137), mean=22.0%; seed43 running on cqa1\n⁹ X-VLA random k=0.3 2-seed: 62.8/66.2, mean=64.5%, σ=2.4pp; seed44 running on cqa1\n\nAt k=0.3, π0.5 L2norm wins (+14.6pp) while X-VLA random still wins massively (+42.3pp). OpenVLA L2norm also wins (+3.6pp). The pattern: at k=0.3, both high-CV (OpenVLA) and low-CV-with-large-budget (π0.5, 230 tokens) favor L2norm, while mid-CV-with-small-budget (X-VLA, 15 tokens) strongly favors random. Strategy preference is f(CV, k, absolute_token_budget).\n\n**OpenVLA (CV=0.215) full seed42 Δ(L2-R) pattern**: +1.4pp (k=0.95) → +5.4pp (k=0.7) → pending (k=0.5) → +3.6pp (k=0.3). L2norm consistently better at ALL k values — high CV enables meaningful importance-based selection. Peak advantage at k=0.7, not monotonically increasing with compression.\n\n**D141: π0.5 L2norm complete curve — valley at k=0.5 confirmed (multi-seed)**:\n| k | L2norm SR (s42) | L2norm SR (s43) | Random SR | Δ (R-L2) s42 |\n|---|-----------------|-----------------|-----------|---------------|\n| 0.7 | **55.0%** | **57.8%**¹⁰ | **77.2%** / **73.8%** (mean=75.5%) | +22.2pp (s42) / +19.8pp (mean) |\n| 0.5 | **33.4%** | **33.6%** ✅ | **69.4%** / **68.4%** (mean=68.9%) | +36.0pp (s42) / +35.4pp (mean) |\n| 0.3 | **51.0%** | **55.4%** ✅ | 36.4% | -14.6pp |\n\n¹⁰ Agent audit reported 56.4% for L2norm k=0.7 seed43 vs earlier worker result 57.8%. Needs reconciliation. Pattern unchanged.\n\n**V-shape fully confirmed (2 seeds, both methods)**:\n- **Valley (k=0.5)**: L2norm 33.4/33.6% (std=0.1pp); Random 69.4/68.4% (std=0.7pp) — both methods stable\n- **2-seed means**: L2norm k=0.7=56.4%, k=0.5=33.5%, k=0.3=53.2%; Random k=0.7=75.5%, k=0.5=68.9%\n- **V-depth**: seed42=17.6pp, seed43=21.8pp (seed43 deeper because endpoints higher)\n- **Δ(R-L2) dual-seed means**: k=0.7=+19.8pp, k=0.5=+35.4pp — scaling law holds with multi-seed\n- seed43 consistently +2-4pp above seed42 but identical shape. Valley position/depth is architectural determinism.\n\n**Mechanism confirmed by token position visualization (D141)**:\n- k=0.7: 2 clusters, 97% in largest, **100% spatial coverage** — enough tokens to maintain coverage\n- k=0.5: **1 cluster, 100% in single region, 78% coverage** — worst-case spatial concentration\n- k=0.3: **3 clusters**, 86% in largest, 78% coverage — cluster breaks apart, better diversity\n\nThe non-monotonicity arises because k=0.5 sits at the worst point of the spatial correlation structure: L2norm selects exactly the number of tokens that maximizes spatial clustering. At k=0.7 there are enough tokens for coverage; at k=0.3 the selection threshold crosses a boundary that fragments the cluster. Per-task variance is extreme at k=0.7 (T1=94%, T5=98% vs T7=0%) — L2norm deterministic selection can catastrophically miss specific task-critical spatial regions.\n\n**Paper strategy**: k=0.5 as **main table** (cleanest scaling law, monotonic gap). Full L2norm curve as **figure** showing pathological valley — strong evidence for spatial clustering mechanism. k=0.3 reversal as supplementary. Key message: \"CV predicts method preference at k=0.5; L2norm's spatial clustering creates pathological non-monotonicity unique to low-CV models.\"\n\n**Notable asymmetry**: Random tolerance is similar for low/medium CV at k=0.5 (π0.5=69.4% ≈ X-VLA=70.6%), while L2norm harm increases dramatically (π0.5=33.4% < X-VLA=43.4%). High CV (OpenVLA=35.8% random) is less random-tolerant because tokens have genuine importance differentiation that random discards.\n\n**Evidence** (Reviewer-verified, D132 PASS):\n\nX-VLA vs OpenVLA full comparison:\n\n| k | X-VLA (CV=0.151) | | OpenVLA (CV=0.215) | |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | L2norm | Random | L2norm | Random |\n| 0.95 | — | — | 70.6% | 69.2% (+1.4 L2norm) |\n| 0.9 | 97.6% | 97.8% (≈0) | 70.6% | 64.6% (+6.0 L2norm) |\n| 0.85 | 68.0% | 63.6% (+4.4 L2norm) | — | — |\n| 0.8 | 89.0% | 89.4% (≈0) | — | — |\n| 0.7 | 56.2% | **65.2% (+9pp random)** | 49.8%¹ | 44.4% (+5.4 L2norm¹) |\n| 0.5 | **42.6%** | **70.6% (+28pp random!)** | 39.2% | 35.8% (+3.4 L2norm) |\n| 0.3 | **22.8%** | **62.8% (+40pp random!)** | 25.0% | pending² |\n\n¹ OpenVLA L2norm k=0.7 = seed43 only, random = seed42; cross-seed caveat. seed42 L2norm k=0.7 running on westd-38929.\n² OpenVLA random k=0.3 result file missing, re-running on westd-38929.\n³ D137 multi-seed: X-VLA random k=0.5 seed43=71.0% (seed42=70.6%, Δ=0.4pp). Gap reproducible.\n\n**Per-task X-VLA k=0.5 (Reviewer-verified, 9/10 tasks random > L2norm):**\n\n| Task | Baseline | L2 s42 | L2 s43 | Random s42 | Δ(R-L2) |\n|------|---------|--------|--------|------------|---------|\n| T0 alphabet_soup | 98% | 58% | 56% | **96%** | +38 |\n| T1 cream_cheese | 100% | 2% | 6% | 46% | +44 |\n| T4 ketchup | 100% | 42% | 40% | **100%** | **+58** |\n| T7 milk | 100% | 38% | 38% | 82% | +44 |\n| T9 orange_juice | 100% | 68% | 70% | **100%** | +32 |\n| T6 butter | 100% | 2% | 2% | 2% | 0 (both crash) |\n\nL2norm two seeds highly consistent (s42 vs s43 diff <6pp) → not RNG noise.\nT6: baseline=100% but both methods=2% → highly localized visual cue, k=0.5 always loses it regardless of method.\nT4/T9: Random recovers to baseline → L2norm systematically discards the critical tokens for these tasks.\n\n**Pattern**: Low CV (X-VLA) → importance-based selection degenerates at aggressive k → random better. High CV (OpenVLA) → meaningful importance differentiation → L2 norm better.\n\n**Mechanism hypothesis** (Reviewer: consistent with data, needs direct evidence): X-VLA's linear projection + BART encoder produces tokens with relatively uniform L2 norms (CV=0.151). At aggressive compression (k=0.5 = keeping 25 of 50 tokens), L2 norm selects the \"slightly larger\" tokens which tend to be spatially clustered → loses spatial diversity → catastrophic. Random preserves spatial coverage stochastically → dramatically better.\n\n**⚠️ Visualization needed (Reviewer warning)**: Must produce token position visualization — for same input image, show which tokens L2 norm vs random retains. If L2 norm shows spatial clustering, mechanism is proven. This should be a key figure (§4.6 or Fig 4).\n\n**Implication for practitioners**: CV diagnoses → predicts tolerance → prescribes strategy at aggressive compression. Low CV + aggressive k (≤0.5) → random/position-based. High CV → importance-based at all k. Mild compression (k≥0.8) → method choice doesn't matter regardless of CV.\n\n**Pending**: X-VLA random k=0.7 (crossover), multi-seed k=0.5, token position visualization, OpenVLA L2norm k=0.7 seed42, k_ratio=null fix.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: Vision token efficiency is critical for real-time VLA deployment. Growing literature proposes inference-time token reduction (FastV, VLA-IAP, H2O, ToMe). These methods succeed on some VLAs but their behavior across different architectures is unstudied.\n\n**Gap**: No work has systematically compared token pruning robustness across VLA architectures. The implicit assumption that \"token pruning works or fails uniformly\" is untested. The critical architectural factor determining prunability is unknown.\n\n**Discovery**: We find that VLA token pruning robustness is governed by two interacting axes. **Axis 1 — Token Coupling**: connector architecture determines whether tokens are independent (linear proj, MLP) or entangled (BART encoder, pixel-shuffle), diagnosed by importance CV (0.038→0.314). **Axis 2 — Task Complexity**: multi-step tasks (Goal/Long) amplify pruning damage on entangling connectors — X-VLA drops 27.8pp on Goal vs 1.6pp on Object at k=0.9. Evidence from 5 VLA models × 4 LIBERO suites:\n- **Token-independent** (π0, π0.5 linear; OpenVLA, OFT MLP): graded degradation, CV 0.038–0.219\n- **Token-entangling** (X-VLA BART 12L; SmolVLA pixel-shuffle): task-dependent collapse — tolerate simple tasks, catastrophic on complex tasks. CV 0.151–0.314\nCV predicts both pruning tolerance and optimal strategy (L2norm hurts low-CV models, helps high-CV).\n\n**Solution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework. Step 1: Token importance CV provides zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance (one forward pass). Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) provides universal compression. For pixel-shuffle: recovers from 0% (hard pruning) to ~59% ≈ baseline (59.2%), M-curve flat (D105: M=16 56.9% ≈ M=128 58.0%, near-lossless at any compression ratio). For MLP projector: D109 C4-ext = 0% SR (overfitting at M=128); VTC-only M=32/M=64 in progress.\n\n**Headline result**: \"Across 5 VLA models (450M-7B) × 4 task suites, we find that token pruning robustness is governed by two axes: connector architecture (token-independent vs token-entangling, diagnosed by importance CV) and task complexity. Token-entangling connectors (BART encoder, pixel-shuffle) show dramatically amplified sensitivity under complex tasks — X-VLA drops 27.8pp on Goal vs 1.6pp on Object at the same keep ratio; SmolVLA collapses to 0% at 5% removal regardless of task. CV (0.038→0.314) predicts both pruning tolerance and optimal strategy: importance-based pruning is actively harmful on low-CV architectures (+28-36pp gap favoring random), while it helps on high-CV models (+1-6pp). VTR recovers to ~59% (≈baseline) at any compression ratio (0-87.5%) where hard deletion achieves 0%.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (7-model version)\n\n1. **Introduction**: VLA efficiency motivation → diverse connector architectures → 2-axis framework discovery (D171) → Diagnose-then-Compress framework\n2. **Background**: 5 VLA models, 3 connector families (linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle), 4 LIBERO suites, token flow analysis\n3. **Experimental Setup**: 5 models, LIBERO benchmark (4 suites: Object/Spatial/Goal/Long), pruning protocol, VTR compression, diagnostic metrics\n4. **Main Results**:\n   - §4.1: 2-Axis Framework Overview (Table 1: 5 models × token coupling axis; Table 2: cross-suite interaction — connector × task complexity)\n   - §4.2: Token-Entangling Catastrophic — pixel-shuffle cliff-edge (SmolVLA, all configs 0% regardless of task)\n   - §4.3: Token-Independent Graded — MLP degradation (OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT entropy confirmation)\n   - §4.4: Token-Independent Tolerant — linear projection (π0 + π0.5, controlled comparison with OpenVLA)\n   - §4.5: Task Complexity Amplification — X-VLA cross-suite (Object 97.6% vs Goal 70.2% vs Long ~53% at same k)\n   - §4.6: Pruning Strategy Depends on CV (D132: low-CV random>>L2norm, high-CV L2norm>>random)\n   - §4.7: VTR overcomes cliff-edge (M-curve flat + architecture independence)\n   - (REMOVED — D119: LIBERO-Plus L1 SR=3.3% floor effect, noted in Discussion §6)\n5. **Analysis**:\n   - §5.1: Why pixel_shuffle creates entanglement (spatial folding + controlled comparison)\n   - §5.2: Diagnostic metric — Entropy + CV composite (D104, 4-model validation)\n   - §5.3: Re-encoding mechanism (M=128 passthrough + MLP adapter + M-curve flat D105)\n6. **Discussion**: Design implications, limitations (sim-only, no real robot), future work\n7. **Conclusion**: 5 claims summary\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### RC1: Only 2 models → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n**Response**: Now 5 models (SmolVLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, π0, X-VLA) across 3 connector families (pixel-shuffle, 3-layer MLP, linear projection) and 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Each connector class has ≥2 models.\n\n### RC2: Model size confound (450M vs 7B) → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n**Response**: π0 (3.3B, linear) is pruning-immune while OpenVLA (7B, MLP) degrades 61% at k=0.1. Larger model is MORE vulnerable, not less — directly falsifies \"larger models are more robust\" hypothesis. X-VLA (880M, linear) also immune, matching π0 behavior despite 4× smaller. Size is not the explanatory variable; connector type is.\n\n### RC3: Why not test SmolVLA without pixel_shuffle?\n**Response**: SmolVLA's connector is integral (LLM expects 128 tokens, not 1024). Removing it requires retraining from scratch. OpenVLA comparison isolates the connector's role.\n\n### RC4: Smart compression — is re-encoding or compression the mechanism?\n**Response (corrected with baseline=59.2%)**: VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio — the M-curve is flat (M=16: 56.9% → M=128: 58.0%, all within ±3pp of baseline 59.2%). Two lines of evidence: (1) M=128 passthrough (58.0%) ≈ baseline (59.2%) — re-encoding recovers spatial entanglement to baseline level, not above it. (2) Architecture control: MLP adapter (63.4%) ≈ cross-attention (60.1%) with CI overlap — any re-encoding mechanism works. The key contribution is recovery from 0% (hard pruning) to ~59% (baseline), not exceeding baseline. Compression ratio is a free parameter with negligible SR cost.\n\n### RC5: Relationship to VLA-IAP\n**Response**: VLA-IAP's 97.8% on OpenVLA is consistent with our finding: MLP projector preserves token independence. VLA-IAP untested on pixel_shuffle VLAs; our geometric prior experiments (0%) predict it would fail.\n\n### RC6: Is this just \"different models behave differently\"?\n**Response**: We identify the specific mechanism (pixel_shuffle spatial folding) and provide evidence for WHY. Concrete design implications: future VLAs wanting efficiency should avoid pixel_shuffle or include learned re-encoding modules.\n\n### RC7: Only one benchmark (LIBERO-Object) → **ADDRESSING (D115, D119)**\n**Response**: Expanded to ALL 4 LIBERO suites (Object/Spatial/Goal/Long) — 4 genuinely different task distributions (manipulation skills, spatial reasoning, goal-conditioned, long-horizon). Taxonomy consistency validated across suites. LIBERO-Plus robustness benchmark tested (D119) but abandoned: L1 camera perturbation collapses OpenVLA to SR=3.3% (consistent with leaderboard 0.8%), creating floor effect with no room for pruning analysis. This floor effect itself is noted in Discussion as evidence of general VLA brittleness under distribution shift. Sim-only limitation acknowledged.\n\n## All Experimental Evidence (confirmed)\n\n### SmolVLA Cliff-Edge\n- Fine-tuned baseline (Object): 44.8% (224/500) — ⚠️ OLD reproduced checkpoint, superseded by official HF = 59.2%\n- 6 pruning conditions (random/ACIS/ToMe × k=0.5/0.7/0.9): all 0%\n- Geometric prior (Sobel) k=0.5/0.7/0.9: all 0%\n- Attention entropy: 0.952 (flat, TV=0.05)\n- Official checkpoint Object: 59.2% → 0% at k=0.5\n- Official checkpoint Spatial: 43.8% → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%]) at k=0.5 — near-zero, confirms cliff-edge across suites\n- LoRA-FT checkpoint Spatial: 8.0% (per-task: [24,8,4,24,0,2,2,2,14,0]) — LoRA trained on Object only, does not transfer to Spatial. Use official checkpoint for cross-suite SmolVLA analysis.\n\n### OpenVLA Degradation Curve\n- k=1.0: 74.0% (370/500)\n- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n- k=0.7: 49.0% (245/500, -34% relative)\n- k=0.5: 37.4% (187/500, -49% relative)\n- k=0.3: 20.6% (103/500, -72% relative)\n- Entropy: 0.639 (progressive sharpening, TV=0.50)\n\n### Cross-Model Pruning Taxonomy (7 models — D100, D120, D127)\n| Model | Connector | Tokens | k=0.1 norm_L1 | k=0.5 norm_L1 | Class |\n|-------|-----------|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n| π0 (3.3B) | Pure linear proj | 256 | 0.976 (-2.4%) | 0.983 | Immune |\n| π0.5 (4B) | Pure linear proj (×√d scaling) | 768 (3×256) | **98.2%** (491/500) | **L2norm=33.4%, random=69.4%** | **Uniformly Critical (D139)**: L2norm catastrophic (-64.8pp), random tolerant (-28.8pp), gap=+36pp. CV=0.055. |\n| X-VLA (880M) | Linear + BART 12L | 50 | ~1.00 | ~1.00 | Threshold-graded (k=0.7: 56.2%) |\n| OpenVLA (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | 1.608 (+61%) | 1.167 (+17%) | Smooth graded |\n| OFT (7B) | 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP fused) | **512** | N/A | N/A | D136: Blackwell GPU incompatible. CV=0.219≈OpenVLA → graded. Cite official ~97% baseline. |\n| SmolVLA (450M) | Pixel-shuffle | 128 | — | 0% cliff | Catastrophic |\n\nDiagnostic metrics (D104+D106+D120: CV as continuous predictor, 7 models):\n| Model | Connector (effective) | Entropy | CV | Pruning Behavior |\n|-------|----------------------|---------|------|------------------|\n| π0 | Pure linear proj | 0.959 | 0.038 | Immune (offline, k=0.1 improves) |\n| π0.5 | Pure linear proj (×√d) | pending | 0.055 | **Uniformly Critical (D139)**: L2norm=33.4%, random=69.4%, gap=+36pp. Scaling law extreme. |\n| X-VLA | Linear proj + BART enc (12L) | **0.614** | **0.151** | Threshold-graded: robust k≥0.9, cliff k=0.7 (56.2%). D127: random=L2norm at k=0.9 |\n| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.661 | 0.215 | Graded (74→37.4% at k=0.5) |\n| OFT | 3-layer MLP (DINOv2+SigLIP, **512 tokens**) | 0.667 | 0.219 | D136: Graded expected (CV≈OpenVLA). Blackwell GPU incompatible, no LIBERO SR. |\n| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle (16×) | 0.952 | **0.314** | Catastrophic (0% at k=0.95) |\n\nKey insights (updated with 7-model data):\n1. **CV is a continuous predictor**: 0.038 → 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.219 → 0.314 maps to decreasing pruning tolerance. NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n2. **X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate behavior** — closer to OpenVLA (0.215) than π0 (0.038), matching k=0.7 SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7.\n3. **X-VLA entropy=0.614 ≈ OpenVLA 0.661** — both have BART/MLP non-linear mixing. X-VLA is NOT \"high entropy\" like π0.\n4. **Effective connector complexity matters more than nominal label**: X-VLA is \"linear proj\" but BART encoder introduces 12 transformer layers of mixing. Paper should discuss \"effective connector\" = projection + any intermediate processing.\n5. OFT entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → action head does not affect attention structure\n6. Framing: CV captures \"degree of non-linear mixing in the vision-to-LLM pathway.\" More mixing → higher CV → less tolerant of pruning.\n\n### Smart Compress (Learned Re-encoding)\nCross-attention (VTC) M sweep (3-seed where available):\n- M=16: **56.9% ± 1.3pp** (3-seed: 55.8/58.4/56.5) — 87.5% compression, ZERO loss vs M=128\n- M=32: 60.1±1.3% (3-seed: 61.6/59.2/59.6)\n- M=64: 62.0±2.3% (3-seed: 61.6/60.0/64.4)\n- M=96: 54.5±3.2% (3-seed: 52.6/58.2/52.8) — highest variance\n- M=128: 58.0±3.5pp (3-seed: 59.8/54.0/60.2) — passthrough control\n- **D102 CONFIRMED: M-curve is flat.** M=16 (56.9%) = M=128 (58.0%), difference < 1.1pp. VTC achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio for pixel-shuffle connector. All M values within ±5pp of baseline ~59%.\n\nMLP adapter (M=32, 3-seed):\n- seed42: 65.2% (326/500), seed43: 64.6% (323/500), seed44: 60.4% (302/500)\n- Mean: 63.4% ± 2.6 vs VTC M=32 mean 60.1% ± 1.3\n- t-test p≈0.15, no significant difference — confirms architecture-independence\n\n### D109: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — FAILED\n- C4-ext M=128 at 20K steps: **0% SR** (0/44 episodes before eval termination)\n- Failure mode: model outputs identical action every timestep (severe overfitting)\n- Interpretation: VTR adds unnecessary complexity for MLP projector tokens (already individually meaningful). VTR specifically solves pixel-shuffle entanglement.\n- VTC-only M=32 and M=64 training in progress on westd-41074:2-3\n\n### Cross-Suite VTR Generalization (SmolVLA)\n- M=32 Spatial: 53.2% (vs official Spatial baseline 44.6% per ROADMAP, vs pruning 0.6% — recovery from cliff-edge, +8.6pp over baseline)\n- M=32 Goal: 56.4% (vs official Goal baseline 60.8% per ROADMAP, vs pruning 0% — recovery from cliff-edge, -4.4pp below baseline)\n- ⚠️ Cross-suite baselines need reconciliation: paper_framing previously used 43.8%/63.0%, ROADMAP uses 44.6%/60.8%. Use n=500 official checkpoint data as ground truth.\n- Note: VTR trained on Object suite, evaluated cross-suite. Official baselines from different checkpoint (official vs LoRA-FT); comparisons should emphasize recovery from 0% rather than absolute performance vs uncompressed.\n\n### Pairwise Statistical Tests (Welch's t-test, n=3 per condition)\n- M=32 VTC vs M=32 MLP: p=0.150 (not significant) — confirms architecture-independence\n- M=64 VTC vs M=96 VTC: p=0.034 (significant) — M=96 dip confirmed real\n- M=32 MLP vs M=96 VTC: p=0.022 (significant) — M=96 underperforms\n- M=32/M=64/M=128 VTC cluster: all pairwise p>0.25 — robust across M values\n- Bonferroni note: no pair survives correction at 10 tests; n=3 limits power (~0.2 for medium effects)\n\n### Supplementary\n- Inference latency: 6% speedup at M=32\n- KV-cache: 75% memory reduction at M=32\n","numLines":552,"startLine":1,"totalLines":552}}}
